--| A ratio is zero iff the numerator is zero. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem diveq0d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne B2 cc0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) cc0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 cc0) $;

--| Equality in terms of unit ratio. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem diveq1d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne B2 cc0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) c1) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 B2) $;

--| The quotient of two complex numbers is one iff they are equal. Deduction form of ~ diveq1 . Generalization of ~ diveq1d . (Contributed by David Moews, 28-Feb-2017.)
theorem diveq1ad (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne B2 cc0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) c1) (wceq A2 B2)) $;

--| A fraction of complex numbers is zero iff its numerator is. Deduction form of ~ diveq0 . (Contributed by David Moews, 28-Feb-2017.)
theorem diveq0ad (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne B2 cc0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) cc0) (wceq A2 cc0)) $;

--| If two complex numbers are unequal, their quotient is not one. Contrapositive of ~ diveq1d . (Contributed by David Moews, 28-Feb-2017.)
theorem divne1d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne B2 cc0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne A2 B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne (co A2 B2 cdiv) c1) $;

