theorem funcsetcestrclem3 {x3: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2 C: class) (S U E F: class x3):
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv S cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq F (cmpt x3 C (csn (cop (cfv cnx cbs) (cv x3))))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cwun) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel com U) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv U cestrc) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv E cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf C B2 F) $;

--| Lemma for ~ embedsetcestrc . (Contributed by AV, 31-Mar-2020.)
theorem embedsetcestrclem {x3: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2 C: class) (S U E F: class x3):
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv S cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq F (cmpt x3 C (csn (cop (cfv cnx cbs) (cv x3))))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cwun) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel com U) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv U cestrc) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv E cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf1 C B2 F) $;

--| Lemma 4 for ~ funcsetcestrc . (Contributed by AV, 27-Mar-2020.)
theorem funcsetcestrclem4 {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff y1) (C: class) (S U F G: class x3 y1):
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv S cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq F (cmpt x3 C (csn (cop (cfv cnx cbs) (cv x3))))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cwun) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel com U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq G (cmpo x3 y1 C C (cres cid (co (cv y1) (cv x3) cmap)))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wfn G (cxp C C)) $;

--| Lemma 5 for ~ funcsetcestrc . (Contributed by AV, 27-Mar-2020.)
theorem funcsetcestrclem5 {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (C: class) (S U F G: class x3 y1) (X Y: class):
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv S cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq F (cmpt x3 C (csn (cop (cfv cnx cbs) (cv x3))))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cwun) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel com U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq G (cmpo x3 y1 C C (cres cid (co (cv y1) (cv x3) cmap)))) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wcel X C) (wcel Y C))) (wceq (co X Y G) (cres cid (co Y X cmap))) $;

--| Lemma 6 for ~ funcsetcestrc . (Contributed by AV, 27-Mar-2020.)
theorem funcsetcestrclem6 {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (C: class) (S U F G H: class x3 y1) (X Y: class):
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv S cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq F (cmpt x3 C (csn (cop (cfv cnx cbs) (cv x3))))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cwun) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel com U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq G (cmpo x3 y1 C C (cres cid (co (cv y1) (cv x3) cmap)))) $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph (wa (wcel X C) (wcel Y C)) (wcel H (co Y X cmap))) (wceq (cfv H (co X Y G)) H) $;

--| Lemma 7 for ~ funcsetcestrc . (Contributed by AV, 27-Mar-2020.)
theorem funcsetcestrclem7 {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (C: class) (S U E F G: class x3 y1) (X: class):
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv S cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq F (cmpt x3 C (csn (cop (cfv cnx cbs) (cv x3))))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cwun) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel com U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq G (cmpo x3 y1 C C (cres cid (co (cv y1) (cv x3) cmap)))) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv U cestrc) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel X C)) (wceq (cfv (cfv X (cfv S ccid)) (co X X G)) (cfv (cfv X F) (cfv E ccid))) $;

--| Lemma 8 for ~ funcsetcestrc . (Contributed by AV, 28-Mar-2020.)
theorem funcsetcestrclem8 {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (C: class) (S U E F G: class x3 y1) (X Y: class):
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv S cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq F (cmpt x3 C (csn (cop (cfv cnx cbs) (cv x3))))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cwun) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel com U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq G (cmpo x3 y1 C C (cres cid (co (cv y1) (cv x3) cmap)))) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv U cestrc) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wcel X C) (wcel Y C))) (wf (co X Y (cfv S chom)) (co (cfv X F) (cfv Y F) (cfv E chom)) (co X Y G)) $;

--| Lemma 9 for ~ funcsetcestrc . (Contributed by AV, 28-Mar-2020.)
theorem funcsetcestrclem9 {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (C: class) (S U E F G H K: class x3 y1) (X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv S cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq F (cmpt x3 C (csn (cop (cfv cnx cbs) (cv x3))))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cwun) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel com U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq G (cmpo x3 y1 C C (cres cid (co (cv y1) (cv x3) cmap)))) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv U cestrc) $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph (w3a (wcel X C) (wcel Y C) (wcel Z C)) (wa (wcel H (co X Y (cfv S chom))) (wcel K (co Y Z (cfv S chom))))) (wceq (cfv (co K H (co (cop X Y) Z (cfv S cco))) (co X Z G)) (co (cfv K (co Y Z G)) (cfv H (co X Y G)) (co (cop (cfv X F) (cfv Y F)) (cfv Z F) (cfv E cco)))) $;

--| The "embedding functor" from the category of sets into the category of extensible structures which sends each set to an extensible structure consisting of the base set slot only, preserving the morphisms as mappings between the corresponding base sets. (Contributed by AV, 28-Mar-2020.)
theorem funcsetcestrc {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (C: class) (S U: class x3 y1) (E: class y1) (F G: class x3 y1):
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv S cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq F (cmpt x3 C (csn (cop (cfv cnx cbs) (cv x3))))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cwun) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel com U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq G (cmpo x3 y1 C C (cres cid (co (cv y1) (cv x3) cmap)))) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv U cestrc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F G (co S E cfunc)) $;

--| The "embedding functor" from the category of sets into the category of extensible structures which sends each set to an extensible structure consisting of the base set slot only is faithful. (Contributed by AV, 31-Mar-2020.)
theorem fthsetcestrc {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (C: class) (S U: class x3 y1) (E: class y1) (F G: class x3 y1):
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv S cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq F (cmpt x3 C (csn (cop (cfv cnx cbs) (cv x3))))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cwun) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel com U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq G (cmpo x3 y1 C C (cres cid (co (cv y1) (cv x3) cmap)))) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv U cestrc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F G (co S E cfth)) $;

--| The "embedding functor" from the category of sets into the category of extensible structures which sends each set to an extensible structure consisting of the base set slot only is full. (Contributed by AV, 1-Apr-2020.)
theorem fullsetcestrc {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (C: class) (S U: class x3 y1) (E: class y1) (F G: class x3 y1):
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv S cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq F (cmpt x3 C (csn (cop (cfv cnx cbs) (cv x3))))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cwun) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel com U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq G (cmpo x3 y1 C C (cres cid (co (cv y1) (cv x3) cmap)))) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv U cestrc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F G (co S E cful)) $;

--| The "embedding functor" from the category of sets into the category of extensible structures which sends each set to an extensible structure consisting of the base set slot only is an embedding. According to definition 3.27 (1) of [Adamek] p. 34, a functor "F is called an _embedding_ provided that F is injective on morphisms", or according to remark 3.28 (1) in [Adamek] p. 34, "a functor is an embedding if and only if it is faithful and injective on objects". (Contributed by AV, 31-Mar-2020.)
theorem embedsetcestrc {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2: class y1) (C: class) (S U: class x3 y1) (E: class y1) (F G: class x3 y1):
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv S cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq F (cmpt x3 C (csn (cop (cfv cnx cbs) (cv x3))))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cwun) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel com U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq G (cmpo x3 y1 C C (cres cid (co (cv y1) (cv x3) cmap)))) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv U cestrc) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv E cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wbr F G (co S E cfth)) (wf1 C B2 F)) $;

--| Extend class notation with the product of two categories.
term cxpc: class;

--| Extend class notation with the first projection functor.
term c1stf: class;

--| Extend class notation with the second projection functor.
term c2ndf: class;

--| Extend class notation with the functor pairing operation.
term cprf: class;

--| Define the binary product of categories, which has objects for each pair of objects of the factors, and morphisms for each pair of morphisms of the factors. Composition is componentwise. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 10-Jan-2017.)
axiom df_xpc {x3 y1 v u f2 g2 h s1 r b: setvar}:
  $ wceq cxpc (cmpo r s1 cvv cvv (csb b (cxp (cfv (cv r) cbs) (cfv (cv s1) cbs)) (csb h (cmpo u v (cv b) (cv b) (cxp (co (cfv (cv u) c1st) (cfv (cv v) c1st) (cfv (cv r) chom)) (co (cfv (cv u) c2nd) (cfv (cv v) c2nd) (cfv (cv s1) chom)))) (ctp (cop (cfv cnx cbs) (cv b)) (cop (cfv cnx chom) (cv h)) (cop (cfv cnx cco) (cmpo x3 y1 (cxp (cv b) (cv b)) (cv b) (cmpo g2 f2 (co (cfv (cv x3) c2nd) (cv y1) (cv h)) (cfv (cv x3) (cv h)) (cop (co (cfv (cv g2) c1st) (cfv (cv f2) c1st) (co (cop (cfv (cfv (cv x3) c1st) c1st) (cfv (cfv (cv x3) c2nd) c1st)) (cfv (cv y1) c1st) (cfv (cv r) cco))) (co (cfv (cv g2) c2nd) (cfv (cv f2) c2nd) (co (cop (cfv (cfv (cv x3) c1st) c2nd) (cfv (cfv (cv x3) c2nd) c2nd)) (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) (cfv (cv s1) cco))))))))))) $;

--| Define the first projection functor out of the product of categories. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
axiom df_1stf {x3 y1 s1 r b: setvar}:
  $ wceq c1stf (cmpo r s1 ccat ccat (csb b (cxp (cfv (cv r) cbs) (cfv (cv s1) cbs)) (cop (cres c1st (cv b)) (cmpo x3 y1 (cv b) (cv b) (cres c1st (co (cv x3) (cv y1) (cfv (co (cv r) (cv s1) cxpc) chom))))))) $;

--| Define the second projection functor out of the product of categories. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
axiom df_2ndf {x3 y1 s1 r b: setvar}:
  $ wceq c2ndf (cmpo r s1 ccat ccat (csb b (cxp (cfv (cv r) cbs) (cfv (cv s1) cbs)) (cop (cres c2nd (cv b)) (cmpo x3 y1 (cv b) (cv b) (cres c2nd (co (cv x3) (cv y1) (cfv (co (cv r) (cv s1) cxpc) chom))))))) $;

--| Define the pairing operation for functors (which takes two functors ` F : C --> D ` and ` G : C --> E ` and produces ` ( F pairF G ) : C --> ( D Xc. E ) ` ). (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
axiom df_prf {x3 y1 f2 g2 h b: setvar}:
  $ wceq cprf (cmpo f2 g2 cvv cvv (csb b (cdm (cfv (cv f2) c1st)) (cop (cmpt x3 (cv b) (cop (cfv (cv x3) (cfv (cv f2) c1st)) (cfv (cv x3) (cfv (cv g2) c1st)))) (cmpo x3 y1 (cv b) (cv b) (cmpt h (cdm (co (cv x3) (cv y1) (cfv (cv f2) c2nd))) (cop (cfv (cv h) (co (cv x3) (cv y1) (cfv (cv f2) c2nd))) (cfv (cv h) (co (cv x3) (cv y1) (cfv (cv g2) c2nd))))))))) $;

--| The binary product of categories is a two-argument function. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 10-Jan-2017.)
theorem fnxpc:
  $ wfn cxpc (cxp cvv cvv) $;

--| Value of the binary product of categories. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 10-Jan-2017.)
theorem xpcval {x3 y1 v u f2 g2: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2 C D: class) (c_xb T c_x H J: class x3 y1 v u f2 g2) (K: class v u) (O V W X Y: class x3 y1 v u f2 g2):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq Y (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wceq J (cfv D chom) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv C cco) $ >
  $ wceq c_xb (cfv D cco) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq B2 (cxp X Y)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq K (cmpo u v B2 B2 (cxp (co (cfv (cv u) c1st) (cfv (cv v) c1st) H) (co (cfv (cv u) c2nd) (cfv (cv v) c2nd) J)))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq O (cmpo x3 y1 (cxp B2 B2) B2 (cmpo g2 f2 (co (cfv (cv x3) c2nd) (cv y1) K) (cfv (cv x3) K) (cop (co (cfv (cv g2) c1st) (cfv (cv f2) c1st) (co (cop (cfv (cfv (cv x3) c1st) c1st) (cfv (cfv (cv x3) c2nd) c1st)) (cfv (cv y1) c1st) c_x)) (co (cfv (cv g2) c2nd) (cfv (cv f2) c2nd) (co (cop (cfv (cfv (cv x3) c1st) c2nd) (cfv (cfv (cv x3) c2nd) c2nd)) (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) c_xb)))))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq T (ctp (cop (cfv cnx cbs) B2) (cop (cfv cnx chom) K) (cop (cfv cnx cco) O))) $;

--| Set of objects of the binary product of categories. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 10-Jan-2017.)
theorem xpcbas (C D T X Y: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq Y (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wceq (cxp X Y) (cfv T cbs) $;

--| Set of morphisms of the binary product of categories. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.) (Proof shortened by AV, 1-Mar-2024.)
theorem xpchomfval {v u: setvar} (B2 C D: class) (T: class v u) (H J: class) (K: class v u):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv T cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wceq J (cfv D chom) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv T chom) $ >
  $ wceq K (cmpo u v B2 B2 (cxp (co (cfv (cv u) c1st) (cfv (cv v) c1st) H) (co (cfv (cv u) c2nd) (cfv (cv v) c2nd) J))) $;

--| Set of morphisms of the binary product of categories. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem xpchom (ph: wff) (B2 C D T H J K X Y: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv T cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wceq J (cfv D chom) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv T chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co X Y K) (cxp (co (cfv X c1st) (cfv Y c1st) H) (co (cfv X c2nd) (cfv Y c2nd) J))) $;

--| A hom-set in the binary product of categories is a relation. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem relxpchom (C D T K X Y: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv T chom) $ >
  $ wrel (co X Y K) $;

--| Value of composition in the binary product of categories. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.) (Proof shortened by AV, 2-Mar-2024.)
theorem xpccofval {x3 y1 f2 g2: setvar} (B2 C D c_xb: class) (T: class x3 y1 f2 g2) (c_x K: class) (O: class f2 g2):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv T cbs) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv T chom) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv C cco) $ >
  $ wceq c_xb (cfv D cco) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv T cco) $ >
  $ wceq O (cmpo x3 y1 (cxp B2 B2) B2 (cmpo g2 f2 (co (cfv (cv x3) c2nd) (cv y1) K) (cfv (cv x3) K) (cop (co (cfv (cv g2) c1st) (cfv (cv f2) c1st) (co (cop (cfv (cfv (cv x3) c1st) c1st) (cfv (cfv (cv x3) c2nd) c1st)) (cfv (cv y1) c1st) c_x)) (co (cfv (cv g2) c2nd) (cfv (cv f2) c2nd) (co (cop (cfv (cfv (cv x3) c1st) c2nd) (cfv (cfv (cv x3) c2nd) c2nd)) (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) c_xb))))) $;

--| Value of composition in the binary product of categories. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem xpcco (ph: wff) (B2 C D c_xb T c_x F G K O X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv T cbs) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv T chom) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv C cco) $ >
  $ wceq c_xb (cfv D cco) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv T cco) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co X Y K)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co Y Z K)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G F (co (cop X Y) Z O)) (cop (co (cfv G c1st) (cfv F c1st) (co (cop (cfv X c1st) (cfv Y c1st)) (cfv Z c1st) c_x)) (co (cfv G c2nd) (cfv F c2nd) (co (cop (cfv X c2nd) (cfv Y c2nd)) (cfv Z c2nd) c_xb)))) $;

--| Value of composition in the binary product of categories. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem xpcco1st (ph: wff) (B2 C D T c_x F G K O X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv T cbs) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv T chom) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv T cco) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co X Y K)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co Y Z K)) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv C cco) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv (co G F (co (cop X Y) Z O)) c1st) (co (cfv G c1st) (cfv F c1st) (co (cop (cfv X c1st) (cfv Y c1st)) (cfv Z c1st) c_x))) $;

--| Value of composition in the binary product of categories. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem xpcco2nd (ph: wff) (B2 C D T c_x F G K O X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv T cbs) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv T chom) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv T cco) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co X Y K)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co Y Z K)) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv D cco) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv (co G F (co (cop X Y) Z O)) c2nd) (co (cfv G c2nd) (cfv F c2nd) (co (cop (cfv X c2nd) (cfv Y c2nd)) (cfv Z c2nd) c_x))) $;

--| Value of the set of morphisms in the binary product of categories. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem xpchom2 (ph: wff) (C D P Q T H J K M N X Y: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq Y (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wceq J (cfv D chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M X) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N Y) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel P X) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Q Y) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv T chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (cop M N) (cop P Q) K) (cxp (co M P H) (co N Q J))) $;

--| Value of composition in the binary product of categories. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem xpcco2 (ph: wff) (C D P Q R S c_xb T c_x F G H J K L M N O X Y: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq Y (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wceq J (cfv D chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M X) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N Y) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel P X) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Q Y) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv C cco) $ >
  $ wceq c_xb (cfv D cco) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv T cco) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel R X) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S Y) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co M P H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co N Q J)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K (co P R H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel L (co Q S J)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (cop K L) (cop F G) (co (cop (cop M N) (cop P Q)) (cop R S) O)) (cop (co K F (co (cop M P) R c_x)) (co L G (co (cop N Q) S c_xb)))) $;

--| The product of two categories is a category. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem xpccatid {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (C D: class) (T: class x3 y1) (I J X Y: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq Y (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wceq I (cfv C ccid) $ >
  $ wceq J (cfv D ccid) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel T ccat) (wceq (cfv T ccid) (cmpo x3 y1 X Y (cop (cfv (cv x3) I) (cfv (cv y1) J))))) $;

--| The identity morphism in the product of categories. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem xpcid (ph: wff) (C D R S T c_1 I J X Y: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq Y (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wceq I (cfv C ccid) $ >
  $ wceq J (cfv D ccid) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv T ccid) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel R X) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S Y) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv (cop R S) c_1) (cop (cfv R I) (cfv S J))) $;

--| The product of two categories is a category. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem xpccat (ph: wff) (C D T: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel T ccat) $;

--| Value of the first projection functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem _1stfval {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2 C D: class) (P T: class x3 y1) (H: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv T cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv T chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq P (co C D c1stf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq P (cop (cres c1st B2) (cmpo x3 y1 B2 B2 (cres c1st (co (cv x3) (cv y1) H))))) $;

--| Value of the first projection on an object. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem _1stf1 (ph: wff) (B2 C D P R T H: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv T cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv T chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq P (co C D c1stf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel R B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv R (cfv P c1st)) (cfv R c1st)) $;

--| Value of the first projection on a morphism. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem _1stf2 (ph: wff) (B2 C D P R S T H: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv T cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv T chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq P (co C D c1stf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel R B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co R S (cfv P c2nd)) (cres c1st (co R S H))) $;

--| Value of the first projection functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem _2ndfval {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2 C D: class) (Q T: class x3 y1) (H: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv T cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv T chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq Q (co C D c2ndf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq Q (cop (cres c2nd B2) (cmpo x3 y1 B2 B2 (cres c2nd (co (cv x3) (cv y1) H))))) $;

--| Value of the first projection on an object. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem _2ndf1 (ph: wff) (B2 C D Q R T H: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv T cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv T chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq Q (co C D c2ndf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel R B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv R (cfv Q c1st)) (cfv R c2nd)) $;

--| Value of the first projection on a morphism. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem _2ndf2 (ph: wff) (B2 C D Q R S T H: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv T cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv T chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq Q (co C D c2ndf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel R B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co R S (cfv Q c2nd)) (cres c2nd (co R S H))) $;

--| The first projection functor is a functor onto the left argument. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem _1stfcl (ph: wff) (C D P T: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq P (co C D c1stf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel P (co T C cfunc)) $;

--| The second projection functor is a functor onto the right argument. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
theorem _2ndfcl (ph: wff) (C D Q T: class):
  $ wceq T (co C D cxpc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq Q (co C D c2ndf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Q (co T D cfunc)) $;

--| Value of the pairing functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem prfval {x3 y1 h: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2: class) (C D: class h) (P E: class x3 y1 h) (F G H: class):
  $ wceq P (co F G cprf) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co C D cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co C E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq P (cop (cmpt x3 B2 (cop (cfv (cv x3) (cfv F c1st)) (cfv (cv x3) (cfv G c1st)))) (cmpo x3 y1 B2 B2 (cmpt h (co (cv x3) (cv y1) H) (cop (cfv (cv h) (co (cv x3) (cv y1) (cfv F c2nd))) (cfv (cv h) (co (cv x3) (cv y1) (cfv G c2nd)))))))) $;

--| Value of the pairing functor on objects. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem prf1 (ph: wff) (B2 C D P E F G H X: class):
  $ wceq P (co F G cprf) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co C D cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co C E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv X (cfv P c1st)) (cop (cfv X (cfv F c1st)) (cfv X (cfv G c1st)))) $;

--| Value of the pairing functor on morphisms. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem prf2fval {h: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2: class) (C D P E: class h) (F G H X Y: class):
  $ wceq P (co F G cprf) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co C D cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co C E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co X Y (cfv P c2nd)) (cmpt h (co X Y H) (cop (cfv (cv h) (co X Y (cfv F c2nd))) (cfv (cv h) (co X Y (cfv G c2nd)))))) $;

--| Value of the pairing functor on morphisms. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem prf2 (ph: wff) (B2 C D P E F G H K X Y: class):
  $ wceq P (co F G cprf) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co C D cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co C E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K (co X Y H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv K (co X Y (cfv P c2nd))) (cop (cfv K (co X Y (cfv F c2nd))) (cfv K (co X Y (cfv G c2nd))))) $;

--| The pairing of functors ` F : C --> D ` and ` G : C --> D ` is a functor ` <. F , G >. : C --> ( D X. E ) ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem prfcl (ph: wff) (C D P T E F G: class):
  $ wceq P (co F G cprf) $ >
  $ wceq T (co D E cxpc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co C D cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co C E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel P (co C T cfunc)) $;

--| Cancellation of pairing with first projection. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem prf1st (ph: wff) (C D P E F G: class):
  $ wceq P (co F G cprf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co C D cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co C E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co D E c1stf) P ccofu) F) $;

--| Cancellation of pairing with second projection. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem prf2nd (ph: wff) (C D P E F G: class):
  $ wceq P (co F G cprf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co C D cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co C E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co D E c2ndf) P ccofu) G) $;

--| Break a functor into a product category into first and second projections. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem _1st2ndprf (ph: wff) (C D T E F: class):
  $ wceq T (co D E cxpc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co C T cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq F (co (co (co D E c1stf) F ccofu) (co (co D E c2ndf) F ccofu) cprf)) $;

--| The category of categories for a weak universe is closed under the product category operation. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.) (Proof shortened by AV, 14-Oct-2024.)
theorem catcxpccl (ph: wff) (B2 C T U X Y: class):
  $ wceq C (cfv U ccatc) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq T (co X Y cxpc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cwun) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel com U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel T B2) $;

--| If two categories have the same set of objects, morphisms, and compositions, then they have the same product category. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 17-Jan-2017.)
theorem xpcpropd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D V: class):
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv A2 chomf) (cfv B2 chomf)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv A2 ccomf) (cfv B2 ccomf)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv C chomf) (cfv D chomf)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv C ccomf) (cfv D ccomf)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 C cxpc) (co B2 D cxpc)) $;

--| Extend class notation with the evaluation functor.
term cevlf: class;

--| Extend class notation with the currying of a functor.
term ccurf: class;

--| Extend class notation with the uncurrying of a functor.
term cuncf: class;

--| Extend class notation to include the diagonal functor.
term cdiag: class;

--| Define the evaluation functor, which is the extension of the evaluation map ` f , x |-> ( f `` x ) ` of functors, to a functor ` ( C --> D ) X. C --> D ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
axiom df_evlf {x3 y1 f2 g2 m n a c d: setvar}:
  $ wceq cevlf (cmpo c d ccat ccat (cop (cmpo f2 x3 (co (cv c) (cv d) cfunc) (cfv (cv c) cbs) (cfv (cv x3) (cfv (cv f2) c1st))) (cmpo x3 y1 (cxp (co (cv c) (cv d) cfunc) (cfv (cv c) cbs)) (cxp (co (cv c) (cv d) cfunc) (cfv (cv c) cbs)) (csb m (cfv (cv x3) c1st) (csb n (cfv (cv y1) c1st) (cmpo a g2 (co (cv m) (cv n) (co (cv c) (cv d) cnat)) (co (cfv (cv x3) c2nd) (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) (cfv (cv c) chom)) (co (cfv (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) (cv a)) (cfv (cv g2) (co (cfv (cv x3) c2nd) (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) (cfv (cv m) c2nd))) (co (cop (cfv (cfv (cv x3) c2nd) (cfv (cv m) c1st)) (cfv (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) (cfv (cv m) c1st))) (cfv (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) (cfv (cv n) c1st)) (cfv (cv d) cco))))))))) $;

--| Define the curry functor, which maps a functor ` F : C X. D --> E ` to ` curryF ( F ) : C --> ( D --> E ) ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
axiom df_curf {x3 y1 z e f2 g2 c d: setvar}:
  $ wceq ccurf (cmpo e f2 cvv cvv (csb c (cfv (cv e) c1st) (csb d (cfv (cv e) c2nd) (cop (cmpt x3 (cfv (cv c) cbs) (cop (cmpt y1 (cfv (cv d) cbs) (co (cv x3) (cv y1) (cfv (cv f2) c1st))) (cmpo y1 z (cfv (cv d) cbs) (cfv (cv d) cbs) (cmpt g2 (co (cv y1) (cv z) (cfv (cv d) chom)) (co (cfv (cv x3) (cfv (cv c) ccid)) (cv g2) (co (cop (cv x3) (cv y1)) (cop (cv x3) (cv z)) (cfv (cv f2) c2nd))))))) (cmpo x3 y1 (cfv (cv c) cbs) (cfv (cv c) cbs) (cmpt g2 (co (cv x3) (cv y1) (cfv (cv c) chom)) (cmpt z (cfv (cv d) cbs) (co (cv g2) (cfv (cv z) (cfv (cv d) ccid)) (co (cop (cv x3) (cv z)) (cop (cv y1) (cv z)) (cfv (cv f2) c2nd)))))))))) $;

--| Define the uncurry functor, which can be defined equationally using ` evalF ` . Strictly speaking, the third category argument is not needed, since the resulting functor is extensionally equal regardless, but it is used in the equational definition and is too much work to remove. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Jan-2017.)
axiom df_uncf {f2 c: setvar}:
  $ wceq cuncf (cmpo c f2 cvv cvv (co (co (cfv c1 (cv c)) (cfv c2 (cv c)) cevlf) (co (co (cv f2) (co (cfv cc0 (cv c)) (cfv c1 (cv c)) c1stf) ccofu) (co (cfv cc0 (cv c)) (cfv c1 (cv c)) c2ndf) cprf) ccofu)) $;

--| Define the diagonal functor, which is the functor ` C --> ( D Func C ) ` whose object part is ` x e. C |-> ( y e. D |-> x ) ` . The value of the functor at an object ` x ` is the constant functor which maps all objects in ` D ` to ` x ` and all morphisms to ` 1 ( x ) ` . The morphism part is a natural transformation between these functors, which takes ` f : x --> y ` to the natural transformation with every component equal to ` f ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Jan-2017.)
axiom df_diag {c d: setvar}:
  $ wceq cdiag (cmpo c d ccat ccat (co (cop (cv c) (cv d)) (co (cv c) (cv d) c1stf) ccurf)) $;

--| Value of the evaluation functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem evlfval {x3 y1 f2 g2 m n a: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2: class f2 g2 m n a) (C D: class) (c_x: class f2) (E: class x3 y1 f2 g2 m n a) (H: class f2 a) (N: class f2):
  $ wceq E (co C D cevlf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv D cco) $ >
  $ wceq N (co C D cnat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq E (cop (cmpo f2 x3 (co C D cfunc) B2 (cfv (cv x3) (cfv (cv f2) c1st))) (cmpo x3 y1 (cxp (co C D cfunc) B2) (cxp (co C D cfunc) B2) (csb m (cfv (cv x3) c1st) (csb n (cfv (cv y1) c1st) (cmpo a g2 (co (cv m) (cv n) N) (co (cfv (cv x3) c2nd) (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) H) (co (cfv (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) (cv a)) (cfv (cv g2) (co (cfv (cv x3) c2nd) (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) (cfv (cv m) c2nd))) (co (cop (cfv (cfv (cv x3) c2nd) (cfv (cv m) c1st)) (cfv (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) (cfv (cv m) c1st))) (cfv (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) (cfv (cv n) c1st)) c_x)))))))) $;

--| Value of the evaluation functor at a morphism. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem evlf2 {g2 a: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2: class g2 a) (C D c_x: class) (E: class g2 a) (F G: class) (H: class a) (L: class g2 a) (N X Y: class):
  $ wceq E (co C D cevlf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv D cco) $ >
  $ wceq N (co C D cnat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co C D cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co C D cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wceq L (co (cop F X) (cop G Y) (cfv E c2nd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq L (cmpo a g2 (co F G N) (co X Y H) (co (cfv Y (cv a)) (cfv (cv g2) (co X Y (cfv F c2nd))) (co (cop (cfv X (cfv F c1st)) (cfv Y (cfv F c1st))) (cfv Y (cfv G c1st)) c_x)))) $;

--| Value of the evaluation natural transformation at an object. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem evlf2val (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D c_x E F G H K L N X Y: class):
  $ wceq E (co C D cevlf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv D cco) $ >
  $ wceq N (co C D cnat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co C D cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co C D cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wceq L (co (cop F X) (cop G Y) (cfv E c2nd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 (co F G N)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K (co X Y H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 K L) (co (cfv Y A2) (cfv K (co X Y (cfv F c2nd))) (co (cop (cfv X (cfv F c1st)) (cfv Y (cfv F c1st))) (cfv Y (cfv G c1st)) c_x))) $;

--| Value of the evaluation functor at an object. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem evlf1 (ph: wff) (B2 C D E F X: class):
  $ wceq E (co C D cevlf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co C D cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co F X (cfv E c1st)) (cfv X (cfv F c1st))) $;

--| Lemma for ~ evlfcl . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem evlfcllem (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D Q E F G H K L N X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq E (co C D cevlf) $ >
  $ wceq Q (co C D cfuc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq N (co C D cnat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel F (co C D cfunc)) (wcel X (cfv C cbs))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel G (co C D cfunc)) (wcel Y (cfv C cbs))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel H (co C D cfunc)) (wcel Z (cfv C cbs))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel A2 (co F G N)) (wcel K (co X Y (cfv C chom)))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel B2 (co G H N)) (wcel L (co Y Z (cfv C chom)))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv (co (cop B2 L) (cop A2 K) (co (cop (cop F X) (cop G Y)) (cop H Z) (cfv (co Q C cxpc) cco))) (co (cop F X) (cop H Z) (cfv E c2nd))) (co (cfv (cop B2 L) (co (cop G Y) (cop H Z) (cfv E c2nd))) (cfv (cop A2 K) (co (cop F X) (cop G Y) (cfv E c2nd))) (co (cop (cfv (cop F X) (cfv E c1st)) (cfv (cop G Y) (cfv E c1st))) (cfv (cop H Z) (cfv E c1st)) (cfv D cco)))) $;

--| The evaluation functor is a bifunctor (a two-argument functor) with the first parameter taking values in the set of functors ` C --> D ` , and the second parameter in ` D ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem evlfcl (ph: wff) (C D Q E: class):
  $ wceq E (co C D cevlf) $ >
  $ wceq Q (co C D cfuc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E (co (co Q C cxpc) D cfunc)) $;

--| Value of the curry functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem curfval {x3 y1 z g2: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class z g2) (B2 C D c_1: class) (E: class x3) (F: class) (G: class x3 y1 z g2) (H: class x3) (I: class x3 y1 z g2) (J: class y1 z):
  $ wceq G (co (cop C D) F ccurf) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co (co C D cxpc) E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wceq J (cfv D chom) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv C ccid) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wceq I (cfv D ccid) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq G (cop (cmpt x3 A2 (cop (cmpt y1 B2 (co (cv x3) (cv y1) (cfv F c1st))) (cmpo y1 z B2 B2 (cmpt g2 (co (cv y1) (cv z) J) (co (cfv (cv x3) c_1) (cv g2) (co (cop (cv x3) (cv y1)) (cop (cv x3) (cv z)) (cfv F c2nd))))))) (cmpo x3 y1 A2 A2 (cmpt g2 (co (cv x3) (cv y1) H) (cmpt z B2 (co (cv g2) (cfv (cv z) I) (co (cop (cv x3) (cv z)) (cop (cv y1) (cv z)) (cfv F c2nd)))))))) $;

--| Value of the object part of the curry functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem curf1fval {x3 y1 z g2: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class z g2) (B2 C D c_1: class) (E: class x3) (F: class) (G: class x3 y1 z g2) (J: class y1 z):
  $ wceq G (co (cop C D) F ccurf) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co (co C D cxpc) E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wceq J (cfv D chom) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv C ccid) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv G c1st) (cmpt x3 A2 (cop (cmpt y1 B2 (co (cv x3) (cv y1) (cfv F c1st))) (cmpo y1 z B2 B2 (cmpt g2 (co (cv y1) (cv z) J) (co (cfv (cv x3) c_1) (cv g2) (co (cop (cv x3) (cv y1)) (cop (cv x3) (cv z)) (cfv F c2nd)))))))) $;

--| Value of the object part of the curry functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem curf1 {y1 z g2: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class z g2) (B2 C D c_1 E F: class) (G: class y1 z g2) (J: class y1 z) (K X: class):
  $ wceq G (co (cop C D) F ccurf) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co (co C D cxpc) E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X A2) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv X (cfv G c1st)) $ >
  $ wceq J (cfv D chom) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv C ccid) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq K (cop (cmpt y1 B2 (co X (cv y1) (cfv F c1st))) (cmpo y1 z B2 B2 (cmpt g2 (co (cv y1) (cv z) J) (co (cfv X c_1) (cv g2) (co (cop X (cv y1)) (cop X (cv z)) (cfv F c2nd))))))) $;

--| Value of the double evaluated curry functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem curf11 (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D E F G K X Y: class):
  $ wceq G (co (cop C D) F ccurf) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co (co C D cxpc) E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X A2) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv X (cfv G c1st)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv Y (cfv K c1st)) (co X Y (cfv F c1st))) $;

--| The partially evaluated curry functor at a morphism. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-Jan-2017.)
theorem curf12 (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D c_1 E F G H J K X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq G (co (cop C D) F ccurf) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co (co C D cxpc) E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X A2) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv X (cfv G c1st)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wceq J (cfv D chom) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv C ccid) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H (co Y Z J)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv H (co Y Z (cfv K c2nd))) (co (cfv X c_1) H (co (cop X Y) (cop X Z) (cfv F c2nd)))) $;

--| The partially evaluated curry functor is a functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Jan-2017.)
theorem curf1cl (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D E F G K X: class):
  $ wceq G (co (cop C D) F ccurf) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co (co C D cxpc) E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X A2) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv X (cfv G c1st)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K (co D E cfunc)) $;

--| Value of the curry functor at a morphism. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Jan-2017.)
theorem curf2 {z: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class z) (B2 C D E F G H I K L X Y: class):
  $ wceq G (co (cop C D) F ccurf) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co (co C D cxpc) E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wceq I (cfv D ccid) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K (co X Y H)) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv K (co X Y (cfv G c2nd))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq L (cmpt z B2 (co K (cfv (cv z) I) (co (cop X (cv z)) (cop Y (cv z)) (cfv F c2nd))))) $;

--| Value of a component of the curry functor natural transformation. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Jan-2017.)
theorem curf2val (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D E F G H I K L X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq G (co (cop C D) F ccurf) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co (co C D cxpc) E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wceq I (cfv D ccid) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K (co X Y H)) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv K (co X Y (cfv G c2nd))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv Z L) (co K (cfv Z I) (co (cop X Z) (cop Y Z) (cfv F c2nd)))) $;

--| The curry functor at a morphism is a natural transformation. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Jan-2017.)
theorem curf2cl (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D E F G H I K L N X Y: class):
  $ wceq G (co (cop C D) F ccurf) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co (co C D cxpc) E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wceq I (cfv D ccid) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K (co X Y H)) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv K (co X Y (cfv G c2nd))) $ >
  $ wceq N (co D E cnat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel L (co (cfv X (cfv G c1st)) (cfv Y (cfv G c1st)) N)) $;

--| The curry functor of a functor ` F : C X. D --> E ` is a functor ` curryF ( F ) : C --> ( D --> E ) ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Jan-2017.)
theorem curfcl (ph: wff) (C D Q E F G: class):
  $ wceq G (co (cop C D) F ccurf) $ >
  $ wceq Q (co D E cfuc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co (co C D cxpc) E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co C Q cfunc)) $;

--| If two categories have the same set of objects, morphisms, and compositions, then they curry the same functor to the same result. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Jan-2017.)
theorem curfpropd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D E F: class):
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv A2 chomf) (cfv B2 chomf)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv A2 ccomf) (cfv B2 ccomf)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv C chomf) (cfv D chomf)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv C ccomf) (cfv D ccomf)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co (co A2 C cxpc) E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (cop A2 C) F ccurf) (co (cop B2 D) F ccurf)) $;

--| Value of the uncurry functor, which is the reverse of the curry functor, taking ` G : C --> ( D --> E ) ` to ` uncurryF ( G ) : C X. D --> E ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Jan-2017.)
theorem uncfval (ph: wff) (C D E F G: class):
  $ wceq F (co (cs3 C D E) G cuncf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co C (co D E cfuc) cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq F (co (co D E cevlf) (co (co G (co C D c1stf) ccofu) (co C D c2ndf) cprf) ccofu)) $;

--| The uncurry operation takes a functor ` F : C --> ( D --> E ) ` to a functor ` uncurryF ( F ) : C X. D --> E ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Jan-2017.)
theorem uncfcl (ph: wff) (C D E F G: class):
  $ wceq F (co (cs3 C D E) G cuncf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co C (co D E cfuc) cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co (co C D cxpc) E cfunc)) $;

--| Value of the uncurry functor on an object. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Jan-2017.)
theorem uncf1 (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D E F G X Y: class):
  $ wceq F (co (cs3 C D E) G cuncf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co C (co D E cfuc) cfunc)) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co X Y (cfv F c1st)) (cfv Y (cfv (cfv X (cfv G c1st)) c1st))) $;

--| Value of the uncurry functor on a morphism. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Jan-2017.)
theorem uncf2 (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D R S E F G H J W X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq F (co (cs3 C D E) G cuncf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co C (co D E cfuc) cfunc)) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wceq J (cfv D chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel W B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel R (co X Z H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S (co Y W J)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co R S (co (cop X Y) (cop Z W) (cfv F c2nd))) (co (cfv W (cfv R (co X Z (cfv G c2nd)))) (cfv S (co Y W (cfv (cfv X (cfv G c1st)) c2nd))) (co (cop (cfv Y (cfv (cfv X (cfv G c1st)) c1st)) (cfv W (cfv (cfv X (cfv G c1st)) c1st))) (cfv W (cfv (cfv Z (cfv G c1st)) c1st)) (cfv E cco)))) $;

--| Cancellation of curry with uncurry. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Jan-2017.)
theorem curfuncf (ph: wff) (C D E F G: class):
  $ wceq F (co (cs3 C D E) G cuncf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co C (co D E cfuc) cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (cop C D) F ccurf) G) $;

--| Cancellation of uncurry with curry. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Jan-2017.)
theorem uncfcurf (ph: wff) (C D E F G: class):
  $ wceq G (co (cop C D) F ccurf) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co (co C D cxpc) E cfunc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (cs3 C D E) G cuncf) F) $;

--| Define the diagonal functor, which is the functor ` C --> ( D Func C ) ` whose object part is ` x e. C |-> ( y e. D |-> x ) ` . We can define this equationally as the currying of the first projection functor, and by expressing it this way we get a quick proof of functoriality. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Jan-2017.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 15-Jan-2017.)
theorem diagval (ph: wff) (C D L: class):
  $ wceq L (co C D cdiag) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq L (co (cop C D) (co C D c1stf) ccurf)) $;

--| The diagonal functor is a functor from the base category to the functor category. Another way of saying this is that the constant functor ` ( y e. D |-> X ) ` is a construction that is natural in ` X ` (and covariant). (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 7-Jan-2017.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 15-Jan-2017.)
theorem diagcl (ph: wff) (C D Q L: class):
  $ wceq L (co C D cdiag) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq Q (co D C cfuc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel L (co C Q cfunc)) $;

--| The constant functor of ` X ` is a functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Jan-2017.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 15-Jan-2017.)
theorem diag1cl (ph: wff) (A2 C D K L X: class):
  $ wceq L (co C D cdiag) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X A2) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv X (cfv L c1st)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K (co D C cfunc)) $;

--| Value of the constant functor at an object. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 7-Jan-2017.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 15-Jan-2017.)
theorem diag11 (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D K L X Y: class):
  $ wceq L (co C D cdiag) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X A2) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv X (cfv L c1st)) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv Y (cfv K c1st)) X) $;

--| Value of the constant functor at a morphism. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Jan-2017.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 15-Jan-2017.)
theorem diag12 (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D c_1 F J K L X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq L (co C D cdiag) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X A2) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv X (cfv L c1st)) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wceq J (cfv D chom) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv C ccid) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co Y Z J)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv F (co Y Z (cfv K c2nd))) (cfv X c_1)) $;

--| Value of the diagonal functor at a morphism. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 7-Jan-2017.)
theorem diag2 (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D F H L X Y: class):
  $ wceq L (co C D cdiag) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co X Y H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv F (co X Y (cfv L c2nd))) (cxp B2 (csn F))) $;

--| The diagonal functor at a morphism is a natural transformation between constant functors. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 7-Jan-2017.)
theorem diag2cl (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D F H L N X Y: class):
  $ wceq L (co C D cdiag) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv D cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co X Y H)) $ >
  $ wceq N (co D C cnat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cxp B2 (csn F)) (co (cfv X (cfv L c1st)) (cfv Y (cfv L c1st)) N)) $;

--| As shown in ~ diagval , the currying of the first projection is the diagonal functor. On the other hand, the currying of the second projection is ` x e. C |-> ( y e. D |-> y ) ` , which is a constant functor of the identity functor at ` D ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Jan-2017.)
theorem curf2ndf (ph: wff) (C D Q: class):
  $ wceq Q (co D D cfuc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (cop C D) (co C D c2ndf) ccurf) (cfv (cfv D cidfu) (cfv (co Q C cdiag) c1st))) $;

--| Extend class notation with the Hom functor.
term chof: class;

--| Extend class notation with the Yoneda embedding.
term cyon: class;

--| Define the Hom functor, which is a bifunctor (a functor of two arguments), contravariant in the first argument and covariant in the second, from ` ( oppCat `` C ) X. C ` to ` SetCat ` , whose object part is the hom-function ` Hom ` , and with morphism part given by pre- and post-composition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
axiom df_hof {x3 y1 f2 g2 h b c: setvar}:
  $ wceq chof (cmpt c ccat (cop (cfv (cv c) chomf) (csb b (cfv (cv c) cbs) (cmpo x3 y1 (cxp (cv b) (cv b)) (cxp (cv b) (cv b)) (cmpo f2 g2 (co (cfv (cv y1) c1st) (cfv (cv x3) c1st) (cfv (cv c) chom)) (co (cfv (cv x3) c2nd) (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) (cfv (cv c) chom)) (cmpt h (cfv (cv x3) (cfv (cv c) chom)) (co (co (cv g2) (cv h) (co (cv x3) (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) (cfv (cv c) cco))) (cv f2) (co (cop (cfv (cv y1) c1st) (cfv (cv x3) c1st)) (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) (cfv (cv c) cco))))))))) $;

--| Define the Yoneda embedding, which is the currying of the (opposite) Hom functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2017.)
axiom df_yon {c: setvar}:
  $ wceq cyon (cmpt c ccat (co (cop (cv c) (cfv (cv c) coppc)) (cfv (cfv (cv c) coppc) chof) ccurf)) $;

--| Value of the Hom functor, which is a bifunctor (a functor of two arguments), contravariant in the first argument and covariant in the second, from ` ( oppCat `` C ) X. C ` to ` SetCat ` , whose object part is the hom-function ` Hom ` , and with morphism part given by pre- and post-composition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Jan-2017.)
theorem hofval {x3 y1 f2 g2 h: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2 C c_x H: class) (M: class x3 y1 f2 g2 h):
  $ wceq M (cfv C chof) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv C cco) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq M (cop (cfv C chomf) (cmpo x3 y1 (cxp B2 B2) (cxp B2 B2) (cmpo f2 g2 (co (cfv (cv y1) c1st) (cfv (cv x3) c1st) H) (co (cfv (cv x3) c2nd) (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) H) (cmpt h (cfv (cv x3) H) (co (co (cv g2) (cv h) (co (cv x3) (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) c_x)) (cv f2) (co (cop (cfv (cv y1) c1st) (cfv (cv x3) c1st)) (cfv (cv y1) c2nd) c_x))))))) $;

--| The object part of the Hom functor is the ` Homf ` operation, which is just a functionalized version of ` Hom ` . That is, it is a two argument function, which maps ` X , Y ` to the set of morphisms from ` X ` to ` Y ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Jan-2017.)
theorem hof1fval (ph: wff) (C M: class):
  $ wceq M (cfv C chof) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv M c1st) (cfv C chomf)) $;

--| The object part of the Hom functor maps ` X , Y ` to the set of morphisms from ` X ` to ` Y ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Jan-2017.)
theorem hof1 (ph: wff) (B2 C H M X Y: class):
  $ wceq M (cfv C chof) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co X Y (cfv M c1st)) (co X Y H)) $;

--| The morphism part of the Hom functor, for morphisms ` <. f , g >. : <. X , Y >. --> <. Z , W >. ` (which since the first argument is contravariant means morphisms ` f : Z --> X ` and ` g : Y --> W ` ), yields a function (a morphism of ` SetCat ` ) mapping ` h : X --> Y ` to ` g o. h o. f : Z --> W ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Jan-2017.)
theorem hof2fval {f2 g2 h: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2 C c_x H: class) (M: class f2 g2 h) (W X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq M (cfv C chof) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel W B2) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv C cco) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (cop X Y) (cop Z W) (cfv M c2nd)) (cmpo f2 g2 (co Z X H) (co Y W H) (cmpt h (co X Y H) (co (co (cv g2) (cv h) (co (cop X Y) W c_x)) (cv f2) (co (cop Z X) W c_x))))) $;

--| The morphism part of the Hom functor, for morphisms ` <. f , g >. : <. X , Y >. --> <. Z , W >. ` (which since the first argument is contravariant means morphisms ` f : Z --> X ` and ` g : Y --> W ` ), yields a function (a morphism of ` SetCat ` ) mapping ` h : X --> Y ` to ` g o. h o. f : Z --> W ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Jan-2017.)
theorem hof2val {h: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2 C c_x F G H: class) (M: class h) (W X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq M (cfv C chof) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel W B2) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv C cco) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co Z X H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co Y W H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co F G (co (cop X Y) (cop Z W) (cfv M c2nd))) (cmpt h (co X Y H) (co (co G (cv h) (co (cop X Y) W c_x)) F (co (cop Z X) W c_x)))) $;

--| The morphism part of the Hom functor, for morphisms ` <. f , g >. : <. X , Y >. --> <. Z , W >. ` (which since the first argument is contravariant means morphisms ` f : Z --> X ` and ` g : Y --> W ` ), yields a function (a morphism of ` SetCat ` ) mapping ` h : X --> Y ` to ` g o. h o. f : Z --> W ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Jan-2017.)
theorem hof2 (ph: wff) (B2 C c_x F G H K M W X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq M (cfv C chof) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel W B2) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv C cco) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co Z X H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co Y W H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K (co X Y H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv K (co F G (co (cop X Y) (cop Z W) (cfv M c2nd)))) (co (co G K (co (cop X Y) W c_x)) F (co (cop Z X) W c_x))) $;

--| Lemma for ~ hofcl . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Jan-2017.)
theorem hofcllem (ph: wff) (B2 C D P Q S T U H K L M O V W X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq M (cfv C chof) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv C coppc) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn (cfv C chomf)) U) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel W B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel T B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K (co Z X H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel L (co Y W H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel P (co S Z H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Q (co W T H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co K P (co (cop S Z) X (cfv C cco))) (co Q L (co (cop Y W) T (cfv C cco))) (co (cop X Y) (cop S T) (cfv M c2nd))) (co (co P Q (co (cop Z W) (cop S T) (cfv M c2nd))) (co K L (co (cop X Y) (cop Z W) (cfv M c2nd))) (co (cop (co X Y H) (co Z W H)) (co S T H) (cfv D cco)))) $;

--| Closure of the Hom functor. Note that the codomain is the category ` SetCat `` U ` for any universe ` U ` which contains each Hom-set. This corresponds to the assertion that ` C ` be locally small (with respect to ` U ` ). (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Jan-2017.)
theorem hofcl (ph: wff) (C D U M O V: class):
  $ wceq M (cfv C chof) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv C coppc) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn (cfv C chomf)) U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M (co (co O C cxpc) D cfunc)) $;

--| Closure of the opposite Hom functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 17-Jan-2017.)
theorem oppchofcl (ph: wff) (C D U M O V: class):
  $ wceq O (cfv C coppc) $ >
  $ wceq M (cfv O chof) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn (cfv C chomf)) U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M (co (co C O cxpc) D cfunc)) $;

--| Value of the Yoneda embedding. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 17-Jan-2017.)
theorem yonval (ph: wff) (C M O Y: class):
  $ wceq Y (cfv C cyon) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv C coppc) $ >
  $ wceq M (cfv O chof) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq Y (co (cop C O) M ccurf)) $;

--| The Yoneda embedding is a functor from the category to the category ` Q ` of presheaves on ` C ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 17-Jan-2017.)
theorem yoncl (ph: wff) (C Q S U O V Y: class):
  $ wceq Y (cfv C cyon) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv C coppc) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wceq Q (co O S cfuc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn (cfv C chomf)) U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y (co C Q cfunc)) $;

--| The Yoneda embedding at an object of ` C ` is a presheaf on ` C ` , also known as the contravariant Hom functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 17-Jan-2017.)
theorem yon1cl (ph: wff) (B2 C S U O V X Y: class):
  $ wceq Y (cfv C cyon) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv C coppc) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn (cfv C chomf)) U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cfv X (cfv Y c1st)) (co O S cfunc)) $;

--| Value of the Yoneda embedding at an object. The partially evaluated Yoneda embedding is also the contravariant Hom functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 17-Jan-2017.)
theorem yon11 (ph: wff) (B2 C H X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq Y (cfv C cyon) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv Z (cfv (cfv X (cfv Y c1st)) c1st)) (co Z X H)) $;

--| Value of the Yoneda embedding at a morphism. The partially evaluated Yoneda embedding is also the contravariant Hom functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 17-Jan-2017.)
theorem yon12 (ph: wff) (B2 C c_x F G H W X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq Y (cfv C cyon) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv C cco) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel W B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co W Z H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co Z X H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv G (cfv F (co Z W (cfv (cfv X (cfv Y c1st)) c2nd)))) (co G F (co (cop W Z) X c_x))) $;

--| Value of the Yoneda embedding at a morphism. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 17-Jan-2017.)
theorem yon2 (ph: wff) (B2 C c_x F G H W X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq Y (cfv C cyon) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv C chom) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv C cco) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel W B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co X Z H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G (co W X H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv G (cfv W (cfv F (co X Z (cfv Y c2nd))))) (co F G (co (cop W X) Z c_x))) $;

--| If two categories have the same set of objects, morphisms, and compositions, then they have the same Hom functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Jan-2017.)
theorem hofpropd (ph: wff) (C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv C chomf) (cfv D chomf)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv C ccomf) (cfv D ccomf)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv C chof) (cfv D chof)) $;

--| If two categories have the same set of objects, morphisms, and compositions, then they have the same Yoneda functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Jan-2017.)
theorem yonpropd (ph: wff) (C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv C chomf) (cfv D chomf)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv C ccomf) (cfv D ccomf)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv C cyon) (cfv D cyon)) $;

--| Value of the opposite Yoneda embedding. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Jan-2017.)
theorem oppcyon (ph: wff) (C M O Y: class):
  $ wceq O (cfv C coppc) $ >
  $ wceq Y (cfv O cyon) $ >
  $ wceq M (cfv C chof) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq Y (co (cop O C) M ccurf)) $;

--| The opposite Yoneda embedding is a functor from ` oppCat `` C ` to the functor category ` C -> SetCat ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Jan-2017.)
theorem oyoncl (ph: wff) (C Q S U O V Y: class):
  $ wceq O (cfv C coppc) $ >
  $ wceq Y (cfv O cyon) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn (cfv C chomf)) U) $ >
  $ wceq Q (co C S cfuc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y (co O Q cfunc)) $;

--| The opposite Yoneda embedding at an object of ` C ` is a functor from ` C ` to Set, also known as the covariant Hom functor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 17-Jan-2017.)
theorem oyon1cl (ph: wff) (B2 C S U O V X Y: class):
  $ wceq O (cfv C coppc) $ >
  $ wceq Y (cfv O cyon) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn (cfv C chomf)) U) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cfv X (cfv Y c1st)) (co C S cfunc)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ yoneda . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-Jan-2017.)
theorem yonedalem1 (ph: wff) (B2 C Q R S T U c_1 E H O V W Y Z: class):
  $ wceq Y (cfv C cyon) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv C ccid) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv C coppc) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wceq T (cfv V csetc) $ >
  $ wceq Q (co O S cfuc) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv Q chof) $ >
  $ wceq R (co (co Q O cxpc) T cfuc) $ >
  $ wceq E (co O S cevlf) $ >
  $ wceq Z (co H (co (co (cop (cfv Y c1st) (ctpos (cfv Y c2nd))) (co Q O c2ndf) ccofu) (co Q O c1stf) cprf) ccofu) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel V W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn (cfv C chomf)) U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (cun (crn (cfv Q chomf)) U) V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel Z (co (co Q O cxpc) T cfunc)) (wcel E (co (co Q O cxpc) T cfunc))) $;

--| Lemma for ~ yoneda . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-Jan-2017.)
theorem yonedalem21 (ph: wff) (B2 C Q R S T U c_1 E F H O V W X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq Y (cfv C cyon) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv C ccid) $ >
