--| The Yoneda Lemma with explicit inverse. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 29-Jan-2017.)
theorem yonedainv {x3 y1 u f2 g2 a: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2 C: class) (Q: class y1) (R: class x3 y1 f2 g2 a) (S: class) (T: class x3 a) (U: class x3 y1 u f2 g2 a) (c_1: class u) (E: class x3) (H I: class x3 y1 u f2 g2 a) (M: class x3 f2 a) (N: class x3 y1 u f2 g2) (O: class) (V W: class x3 y1 u f2 g2 a) (Y Z: class):
  $ wceq Y (cfv C cyon) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv C ccid) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv C coppc) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv U csetc) $ >
  $ wceq T (cfv V csetc) $ >
  $ wceq Q (co O S cfuc) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv Q chof) $ >
  $ wceq R (co (co Q O cxpc) T cfuc) $ >
  $ wceq E (co O S cevlf) $ >
  $ wceq Z (co H (co (co (cop (cfv Y c1st) (ctpos (cfv Y c2nd))) (co Q O c2ndf) ccofu) (co Q O c1stf) cprf) ccofu) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C ccat) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel V W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn (cfv C chomf)) U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (cun (crn (cfv Q chomf)) U) V) $ >
