--| The reduced word that forms the base of the sequence in ~ efgsval is uniquely determined, given the ending representation. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-Sep-2015.) (Proof shortened by AV, 3-Nov-2022.)
theorem efgredlem {x3 y1 z w v t k m n a b: setvar} (ph: wff x3 y1 z w v t k m n a b) (A2 B2: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (D: class x3 y1 z w v k n) (c_sm: class w v k n) (S: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (T: class y1 z w v n) (I: class k) (M: class y1 z k) (W: class):
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq M (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cop (cv y1) (cdif c1o (cv z)))) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpt v W (cmpo n w (co cc0 (cfv (cv v) chash) cfz) (cxp I c2o) (co (cv v) (cotp (cv n) (cv n) (cs2 (cv w) (cfv (cv w) M))) csplice))) $ >
  $ wceq D (cdif W (ciun x3 W (crn (cfv (cv x3) T)))) $ >
  $ wceq S (cmpt m (crab t (wa (wcel (cfv cc0 (cv t)) D) (wral k (wcel (cfv (cv k) (cv t)) (crn (cfv (cfv (co (cv k) c1 cmin) (cv t)) T))) (co c1 (cfv (cv t) chash) cfzo))) (cdif (cword W) (csn c0))) (cfv (co (cfv (cv m) chash) c1 cmin) (cv m))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral a (wral b (wi (wbr (cfv (cfv (cv a) S) chash) (cfv (cfv A2 S) chash) clt) (wi (wceq (cfv (cv a) S) (cfv (cv b) S)) (wceq (cfv cc0 (cv a)) (cfv cc0 (cv b))))) (cdm S)) (cdm S)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 (cdm S)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 (cdm S)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv A2 S) (cfv B2 S)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn (wceq (cfv cc0 A2) (cfv cc0 B2))) $ >
  $ wn ph $;

--| The reduced word that forms the base of the sequence in ~ efgsval is uniquely determined, given the terminal point. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-Sep-2015.)
theorem efgred {x3 y1 z w v t k m n: setvar} (A2 B2: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (D: class x3 y1 z w v k n) (c_sm: class w v k n) (S: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (T: class y1 z w v n) (I: class k) (M: class y1 z k) (W: class):
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq M (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cop (cv y1) (cdif c1o (cv z)))) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpt v W (cmpo n w (co cc0 (cfv (cv v) chash) cfz) (cxp I c2o) (co (cv v) (cotp (cv n) (cv n) (cs2 (cv w) (cfv (cv w) M))) csplice))) $ >
  $ wceq D (cdif W (ciun x3 W (crn (cfv (cv x3) T)))) $ >
  $ wceq S (cmpt m (crab t (wa (wcel (cfv cc0 (cv t)) D) (wral k (wcel (cfv (cv k) (cv t)) (crn (cfv (cfv (co (cv k) c1 cmin) (cv t)) T))) (co c1 (cfv (cv t) chash) cfzo))) (cdif (cword W) (csn c0))) (cfv (co (cfv (cv m) chash) c1 cmin) (cv m))) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 (cdm S)) (wcel B2 (cdm S)) (wceq (cfv A2 S) (cfv B2 S))) (wceq (cfv cc0 A2) (cfv cc0 B2)) $;

--| If two words ` A , B ` are related under the free group equivalence, then there exist two extension sequences ` a , b ` such that ` a ` ends at ` A ` , ` b ` ends at ` B ` , and ` a ` and ` B ` have the same starting point. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 1-Oct-2015.)
theorem efgrelexlema {x3 y1 z w v t i j k m n a b c d: setvar} (A2 B2: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (D: class x3 y1 z w v k n) (c_sm: class w v k n) (S: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (T: class y1 z w v n d) (I: class k d) (L: class x3 y1 z w v t i j k m n c d) (M: class y1 z k d) (W: class):
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq M (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cop (cv y1) (cdif c1o (cv z)))) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpt v W (cmpo n w (co cc0 (cfv (cv v) chash) cfz) (cxp I c2o) (co (cv v) (cotp (cv n) (cv n) (cs2 (cv w) (cfv (cv w) M))) csplice))) $ >
  $ wceq D (cdif W (ciun x3 W (crn (cfv (cv x3) T)))) $ >
  $ wceq S (cmpt m (crab t (wa (wcel (cfv cc0 (cv t)) D) (wral k (wcel (cfv (cv k) (cv t)) (crn (cfv (cfv (co (cv k) c1 cmin) (cv t)) T))) (co c1 (cfv (cv t) chash) cfzo))) (cdif (cword W) (csn c0))) (cfv (co (cfv (cv m) chash) c1 cmin) (cv m))) $ >
  $ wceq L (copab i j (wrex c (wrex d (wceq (cfv cc0 (cv c)) (cfv cc0 (cv d))) (cima (ccnv S) (csn (cv j)))) (cima (ccnv S) (csn (cv i))))) $ >
  $ wb (wbr A2 B2 L) (wrex a (wrex b (wceq (cfv cc0 (cv a)) (cfv cc0 (cv b))) (cima (ccnv S) (csn B2))) (cima (ccnv S) (csn A2))) $;

--| If two words ` A , B ` are related under the free group equivalence, then there exist two extension sequences ` a , b ` such that ` a ` ends at ` A ` , ` b ` ends at ` B ` , and ` a ` and ` B ` have the same starting point. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 1-Oct-2015.)
theorem efgrelexlemb {x3 y1 z w v t i j k m n c d: setvar} (D: class x3 y1 z w v k n) (c_sm: class w v k n) (S: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (T: class y1 z w v n d) (I: class k d) (L: class x3 y1 z w v t i j k m n c d) (M: class y1 z k d) (W: class):
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq M (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cop (cv y1) (cdif c1o (cv z)))) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpt v W (cmpo n w (co cc0 (cfv (cv v) chash) cfz) (cxp I c2o) (co (cv v) (cotp (cv n) (cv n) (cs2 (cv w) (cfv (cv w) M))) csplice))) $ >
  $ wceq D (cdif W (ciun x3 W (crn (cfv (cv x3) T)))) $ >
  $ wceq S (cmpt m (crab t (wa (wcel (cfv cc0 (cv t)) D) (wral k (wcel (cfv (cv k) (cv t)) (crn (cfv (cfv (co (cv k) c1 cmin) (cv t)) T))) (co c1 (cfv (cv t) chash) cfzo))) (cdif (cword W) (csn c0))) (cfv (co (cfv (cv m) chash) c1 cmin) (cv m))) $ >
  $ wceq L (copab i j (wrex c (wrex d (wceq (cfv cc0 (cv c)) (cfv cc0 (cv d))) (cima (ccnv S) (csn (cv j)))) (cima (ccnv S) (csn (cv i))))) $ >
  $ wss c_sm L $;

--| If two words ` A , B ` are related under the free group equivalence, then there exist two extension sequences ` a , b ` such that ` a ` ends at ` A ` , ` b ` ends at ` B ` , and ` a ` and ` B ` have the same starting point. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 1-Oct-2015.)
theorem efgrelex {x3 y1 z w v t k m n a b: setvar} (A2 B2: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (D: class x3 y1 z w v k n) (c_sm: class w v k n) (S: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (T: class y1 z w v n) (I: class k) (M: class y1 z k) (W: class):
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq M (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cop (cv y1) (cdif c1o (cv z)))) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpt v W (cmpo n w (co cc0 (cfv (cv v) chash) cfz) (cxp I c2o) (co (cv v) (cotp (cv n) (cv n) (cs2 (cv w) (cfv (cv w) M))) csplice))) $ >
  $ wceq D (cdif W (ciun x3 W (crn (cfv (cv x3) T)))) $ >
  $ wceq S (cmpt m (crab t (wa (wcel (cfv cc0 (cv t)) D) (wral k (wcel (cfv (cv k) (cv t)) (crn (cfv (cfv (co (cv k) c1 cmin) (cv t)) T))) (co c1 (cfv (cv t) chash) cfzo))) (cdif (cword W) (csn c0))) (cfv (co (cfv (cv m) chash) c1 cmin) (cv m))) $ >
  $ wi (wbr A2 B2 c_sm) (wrex a (wrex b (wceq (cfv cc0 (cv a)) (cfv cc0 (cv b))) (cima (ccnv S) (csn B2))) (cima (ccnv S) (csn A2))) $;

--| There is a unique reduced word equivalent to a given word. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 1-Oct-2015.)
theorem efgredeu {x3 y1 z w v t k m n d: setvar} (A2: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (D: class x3 y1 z w v k n) (c_sm: class w v k n) (S: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (T: class y1 z w v n d) (I: class k d) (M: class y1 z k d) (W: class):
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq M (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cop (cv y1) (cdif c1o (cv z)))) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpt v W (cmpo n w (co cc0 (cfv (cv v) chash) cfz) (cxp I c2o) (co (cv v) (cotp (cv n) (cv n) (cs2 (cv w) (cfv (cv w) M))) csplice))) $ >
  $ wceq D (cdif W (ciun x3 W (crn (cfv (cv x3) T)))) $ >
  $ wceq S (cmpt m (crab t (wa (wcel (cfv cc0 (cv t)) D) (wral k (wcel (cfv (cv k) (cv t)) (crn (cfv (cfv (co (cv k) c1 cmin) (cv t)) T))) (co c1 (cfv (cv t) chash) cfzo))) (cdif (cword W) (csn c0))) (cfv (co (cfv (cv m) chash) c1 cmin) (cv m))) $ >
  $ wi (wcel A2 W) (wreu d (wbr (cv d) A2 c_sm) D) $;

--| Two extension sequences have related endpoints iff they have the same base. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 1-Oct-2015.)
theorem efgred2 {x3 y1 z w v t k m n: setvar} (A2 B2: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (D: class x3 y1 z w v k n) (c_sm: class w v k n) (S: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (T: class y1 z w v n) (I: class k) (M: class y1 z k) (W: class):
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq M (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cop (cv y1) (cdif c1o (cv z)))) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpt v W (cmpo n w (co cc0 (cfv (cv v) chash) cfz) (cxp I c2o) (co (cv v) (cotp (cv n) (cv n) (cs2 (cv w) (cfv (cv w) M))) csplice))) $ >
  $ wceq D (cdif W (ciun x3 W (crn (cfv (cv x3) T)))) $ >
  $ wceq S (cmpt m (crab t (wa (wcel (cfv cc0 (cv t)) D) (wral k (wcel (cfv (cv k) (cv t)) (crn (cfv (cfv (co (cv k) c1 cmin) (cv t)) T))) (co c1 (cfv (cv t) chash) cfzo))) (cdif (cword W) (csn c0))) (cfv (co (cfv (cv m) chash) c1 cmin) (cv m))) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 (cdm S)) (wcel B2 (cdm S))) (wb (wbr (cfv A2 S) (cfv B2 S) c_sm) (wceq (cfv cc0 A2) (cfv cc0 B2))) $;

--| Lemma for ~ efgrelex . Define an auxiliary equivalence relation ` L ` such that ` A L B ` if there are sequences from ` A ` to ` B ` passing through the same reduced word. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 1-Oct-2015.)
theorem efgcpbllema {x3 y1 z w v t i j k m n: setvar} (A2 B2: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (D: class x3 y1 z w v k n) (c_sm: class w v k n) (S: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (T: class y1 z w v n) (I: class k) (L: class x3 y1 z w v t i j k m n) (M: class y1 z k) (W: class) (X Y: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n):
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq M (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cop (cv y1) (cdif c1o (cv z)))) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpt v W (cmpo n w (co cc0 (cfv (cv v) chash) cfz) (cxp I c2o) (co (cv v) (cotp (cv n) (cv n) (cs2 (cv w) (cfv (cv w) M))) csplice))) $ >
  $ wceq D (cdif W (ciun x3 W (crn (cfv (cv x3) T)))) $ >
  $ wceq S (cmpt m (crab t (wa (wcel (cfv cc0 (cv t)) D) (wral k (wcel (cfv (cv k) (cv t)) (crn (cfv (cfv (co (cv k) c1 cmin) (cv t)) T))) (co c1 (cfv (cv t) chash) cfzo))) (cdif (cword W) (csn c0))) (cfv (co (cfv (cv m) chash) c1 cmin) (cv m))) $ >
  $ wceq L (copab i j (wa (wss (cpr (cv i) (cv j)) W) (wbr (co (co A2 (cv i) cconcat) B2 cconcat) (co (co A2 (cv j) cconcat) B2 cconcat) c_sm))) $ >
  $ wb (wbr X Y L) (w3a (wcel X W) (wcel Y W) (wbr (co (co A2 X cconcat) B2 cconcat) (co (co A2 Y cconcat) B2 cconcat) c_sm)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ efgrelex . Show that ` L ` is an equivalence relation containing all direct extensions of a word, so is closed under ` .~ ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 1-Oct-2015.)
theorem efgcpbllemb {x3 y1 z w v t i j k m n: setvar} (A2 B2: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (D: class x3 y1 z w v k n) (c_sm: class w v k n) (S: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (T: class y1 z w v n) (I: class k) (L: class x3 y1 z w v t i j k m n) (M: class y1 z k) (W: class):
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq M (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cop (cv y1) (cdif c1o (cv z)))) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpt v W (cmpo n w (co cc0 (cfv (cv v) chash) cfz) (cxp I c2o) (co (cv v) (cotp (cv n) (cv n) (cs2 (cv w) (cfv (cv w) M))) csplice))) $ >
  $ wceq D (cdif W (ciun x3 W (crn (cfv (cv x3) T)))) $ >
  $ wceq S (cmpt m (crab t (wa (wcel (cfv cc0 (cv t)) D) (wral k (wcel (cfv (cv k) (cv t)) (crn (cfv (cfv (co (cv k) c1 cmin) (cv t)) T))) (co c1 (cfv (cv t) chash) cfzo))) (cdif (cword W) (csn c0))) (cfv (co (cfv (cv m) chash) c1 cmin) (cv m))) $ >
  $ wceq L (copab i j (wa (wss (cpr (cv i) (cv j)) W) (wbr (co (co A2 (cv i) cconcat) B2 cconcat) (co (co A2 (cv j) cconcat) B2 cconcat) c_sm))) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 W) (wcel B2 W)) (wss c_sm L) $;

--| Two extension sequences have related endpoints iff they have the same base. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 1-Oct-2015.)
theorem efgcpbl {x3 y1 z w v t k m n: setvar} (A2 B2: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (D: class x3 y1 z w v k n) (c_sm: class w v k n) (S: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (T: class y1 z w v n) (I: class k) (M: class y1 z k) (W: class) (X Y: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n):
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq M (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cop (cv y1) (cdif c1o (cv z)))) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpt v W (cmpo n w (co cc0 (cfv (cv v) chash) cfz) (cxp I c2o) (co (cv v) (cotp (cv n) (cv n) (cs2 (cv w) (cfv (cv w) M))) csplice))) $ >
  $ wceq D (cdif W (ciun x3 W (crn (cfv (cv x3) T)))) $ >
  $ wceq S (cmpt m (crab t (wa (wcel (cfv cc0 (cv t)) D) (wral k (wcel (cfv (cv k) (cv t)) (crn (cfv (cfv (co (cv k) c1 cmin) (cv t)) T))) (co c1 (cfv (cv t) chash) cfzo))) (cdif (cword W) (csn c0))) (cfv (co (cfv (cv m) chash) c1 cmin) (cv m))) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 W) (wcel B2 W) (wbr X Y c_sm)) (wbr (co (co A2 X cconcat) B2 cconcat) (co (co A2 Y cconcat) B2 cconcat) c_sm) $;

--| Two extension sequences have related endpoints iff they have the same base. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 1-Oct-2015.)
theorem efgcpbl2 {x3 y1 z w v t k m n: setvar} (A2 B2: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (D: class x3 y1 z w v k n) (c_sm: class w v k n) (S: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n) (T: class y1 z w v n) (I: class k) (M: class y1 z k) (W: class) (X Y: class x3 y1 z w v t k m n):
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq M (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cop (cv y1) (cdif c1o (cv z)))) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpt v W (cmpo n w (co cc0 (cfv (cv v) chash) cfz) (cxp I c2o) (co (cv v) (cotp (cv n) (cv n) (cs2 (cv w) (cfv (cv w) M))) csplice))) $ >
  $ wceq D (cdif W (ciun x3 W (crn (cfv (cv x3) T)))) $ >
  $ wceq S (cmpt m (crab t (wa (wcel (cfv cc0 (cv t)) D) (wral k (wcel (cfv (cv k) (cv t)) (crn (cfv (cfv (co (cv k) c1 cmin) (cv t)) T))) (co c1 (cfv (cv t) chash) cfzo))) (cdif (cword W) (csn c0))) (cfv (co (cfv (cv m) chash) c1 cmin) (cv m))) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr A2 X c_sm) (wbr B2 Y c_sm)) (wbr (co A2 B2 cconcat) (co X Y cconcat) c_sm) $;

--| Value of the free group construction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 1-Oct-2015.)
theorem frgpval (c_sm G I M V: class):
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq M (cfv (cxp I c2o) cfrmd) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wi (wcel I V) (wceq G (co M c_sm cqus)) $;

--| Compatibility of the group operation with the free group equivalence relation. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 1-Oct-2015.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-Feb-2016.)
theorem frgpcpbl (A2 B2 C D c_pl c_sm G I M: class):
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq M (cfv (cxp I c2o) cfrmd) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv M cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr A2 C c_sm) (wbr B2 D c_sm)) (wbr (co A2 B2 c_pl) (co C D c_pl) c_sm) $;

--| The free group is a group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 1-Oct-2015.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-Feb-2016.)
theorem frgp0 (c_sm G I V: class):
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wi (wcel I V) (wa (wcel G cgrp) (wceq (cec c0 c_sm) (cfv G c0g))) $;

--| Closure of the quotient map in a free group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 1-Oct-2015.)
theorem frgpeccl (B2 c_sm G I W X: class):
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi (wcel X W) (wcel (cec X c_sm) B2) $;

--| The free group is a group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 1-Oct-2015.)
theorem frgpgrp (G I V: class):
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wi (wcel I V) (wcel G cgrp) $;

--| Addition in the free group is given by concatenation. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 1-Oct-2015.)
theorem frgpadd (A2 B2 c_pl c_sm G I W: class):
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 W) (wcel B2 W)) (wceq (co (cec A2 c_sm) (cec B2 c_sm) c_pl) (cec (co A2 B2 cconcat) c_sm)) $;

--| The inverse of an element of the free group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 2-Oct-2015.)
theorem frgpinv {y1 z: setvar} (A2: class y1 z) (c_sm: class) (G: class y1 z) (I: class) (M N: class y1 z) (W: class):
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv G cminusg) $ >
  $ wceq M (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cop (cv y1) (cdif c1o (cv z)))) $ >
  $ wi (wcel A2 W) (wceq (cfv (cec A2 c_sm) N) (cec (ccom M (cfv A2 creverse)) c_sm)) $;

--| The "natural map" from words of the free monoid to their cosets in the free group is a surjective monoid homomorphism. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 2-Oct-2015.)
theorem frgpmhm {x3: setvar} (c_sm: class) (F: class x3) (G I: class) (M: class x3) (V W: class):
  $ wceq M (cfv (cxp I c2o) cfrmd) $ >
  $ wceq W (cfv M cbs) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt x3 W (cec (cv x3) c_sm)) $ >
  $ wi (wcel I V) (wcel F (co M G cmhm)) $;

--| The canonical injection from the generating set ` I ` to the base set of the free group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 2-Oct-2015.)
theorem vrgpfval {j: setvar} (c_sm: class) (U: class j) (I V: class):
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv I cvrgp) $ >
  $ wi (wcel I V) (wceq U (cmpt j I (cec (cs1 (cop (cv j) c0)) c_sm))) $;

--| The value of the generating elements of a free group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 2-Oct-2015.)
theorem vrgpval (A2 c_sm U I V: class):
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv I cvrgp) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel I V) (wcel A2 I)) (wceq (cfv A2 U) (cec (cs1 (cop A2 c0)) c_sm)) $;

--| The mapping from the index set to the generators is a function into the free group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 2-Oct-2015.)
theorem vrgpf (c_sm U G I V X: class):
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv I cvrgp) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi (wcel I V) (wf I X U) $;

--| The inverse of a generating element is represented by ` <. A , 1 >. ` instead of ` <. A , 0 >. ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 2-Oct-2015.)
theorem vrgpinv (A2 c_sm U G I N V: class):
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv I cvrgp) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv G cminusg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel I V) (wcel A2 I)) (wceq (cfv (cfv A2 U) N) (cec (cs1 (cop A2 c1o)) c_sm)) $;

--| Any assignment of the generators to target elements can be extended (uniquely) to a homomorphism from a free monoid to an arbitrary other monoid. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 2-Oct-2015.)
theorem frgpuptf {y1 z: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2: class) (T: class y1 z) (F: class) (H: class y1 z) (I N: class) (V: class y1 z):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv H cbs) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv H cminusg) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cif (wceq (cv z) c0) (cfv (cv y1) F) (cfv (cfv (cv y1) F) N))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H cgrp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf I B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf (cxp I c2o) B2 T) $;

--| Any assignment of the generators to target elements can be extended (uniquely) to a homomorphism from a free monoid to an arbitrary other monoid. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 2-Oct-2015.)
theorem frgpuptinv {y1 z: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (T: class y1 z) (F: class) (H: class y1 z) (I: class) (M: class y1 z) (N: class) (V: class y1 z):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv H cbs) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv H cminusg) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cif (wceq (cv z) c0) (cfv (cv y1) F) (cfv (cfv (cv y1) F) N))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H cgrp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf I B2 F) $ >
  $ wceq M (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cop (cv y1) (cdif c1o (cv z)))) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel A2 (cxp I c2o))) (wceq (cfv (cfv A2 M) T) (cfv (cfv A2 T) N)) $;

--| Any assignment of the generators to target elements can be extended (uniquely) to a homomorphism from a free monoid to an arbitrary other monoid. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 2-Oct-2015.)
theorem frgpuplem {y1 z: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (C c_sm T: class y1 z) (F: class) (H: class y1 z) (I N: class) (V W: class y1 z):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv H cbs) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv H cminusg) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cif (wceq (cv z) c0) (cfv (cv y1) F) (cfv (cfv (cv y1) F) N))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H cgrp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf I B2 F) $ >
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wbr A2 C c_sm)) (wceq (co H (ccom T A2) cgsu) (co H (ccom T C) cgsu)) $;

--| Any assignment of the generators to target elements can be extended (uniquely) to a homomorphism from a free monoid to an arbitrary other monoid. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 2-Oct-2015.)
theorem frgpupf {y1 z g2: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2: class) (c_sm T: class y1 z) (E: class y1 z g2) (F: class g2) (G: class y1 z g2) (H: class y1 z) (I N: class g2) (V: class y1 z g2) (W: class y1 z) (X: class y1 z g2):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv H cbs) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv H cminusg) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cif (wceq (cv z) c0) (cfv (cv y1) F) (cfv (cfv (cv y1) F) N))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H cgrp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf I B2 F) $ >
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq E (crn (cmpt g2 W (cop (cec (cv g2) c_sm) (co H (ccom T (cv g2)) cgsu)))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf X B2 E) $;

--| Any assignment of the generators to target elements can be extended (uniquely) to a homomorphism from a free monoid to an arbitrary other monoid. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 2-Oct-2015.)
theorem frgpupval {y1 z g2: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (c_sm T: class y1 z) (E: class y1 z g2) (F: class g2) (G: class y1 z g2) (H: class y1 z) (I N: class g2) (V: class y1 z g2) (W: class y1 z) (X: class y1 z g2):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv H cbs) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv H cminusg) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cif (wceq (cv z) c0) (cfv (cv y1) F) (cfv (cfv (cv y1) F) N))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H cgrp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf I B2 F) $ >
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq E (crn (cmpt g2 W (cop (cec (cv g2) c_sm) (co H (ccom T (cv g2)) cgsu)))) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel A2 W)) (wceq (cfv (cec A2 c_sm) E) (co H (ccom T A2) cgsu)) $;

--| Any assignment of the generators to target elements can be extended (uniquely) to a homomorphism from a free monoid to an arbitrary other monoid. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 2-Oct-2015.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 28-Feb-2016.)
theorem frgpup1 {y1 z g2: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2: class) (c_sm T: class y1 z) (E: class y1 z g2) (F: class g2) (G: class y1 z g2) (H: class y1 z) (I N: class g2) (V: class y1 z g2) (W: class y1 z) (X: class y1 z g2):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv H cbs) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv H cminusg) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cif (wceq (cv z) c0) (cfv (cv y1) F) (cfv (cfv (cv y1) F) N))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H cgrp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf I B2 F) $ >
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq E (crn (cmpt g2 W (cop (cec (cv g2) c_sm) (co H (ccom T (cv g2)) cgsu)))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E (co G H cghm)) $;

--| The evaluation map has the intended behavior on the generators. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 2-Oct-2015.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 28-Feb-2016.)
theorem frgpup2 {y1 z g2: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (c_sm T: class y1 z) (U E: class y1 z g2) (F: class g2) (G: class y1 z g2) (H: class y1 z) (I N: class g2) (V: class y1 z g2) (W: class y1 z) (X: class y1 z g2):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv H cbs) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv H cminusg) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cif (wceq (cv z) c0) (cfv (cv y1) F) (cfv (cfv (cv y1) F) N))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H cgrp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf I B2 F) $ >
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq E (crn (cmpt g2 W (cop (cec (cv g2) c_sm) (co H (ccom T (cv g2)) cgsu)))) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv I cvrgp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv (cfv A2 U) E) (cfv A2 F)) $;

--| The evaluation map has the intended behavior on the generators. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 2-Oct-2015.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 28-Feb-2016.)
theorem frgpup3lem {y1 z g2: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2: class) (c_sm T: class y1 z) (U E: class y1 z g2) (F: class g2) (G: class y1 z g2) (H: class y1 z) (I: class g2) (K: class y1 z g2) (N: class g2) (V: class y1 z g2) (W: class y1 z) (X: class y1 z g2):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv H cbs) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv H cminusg) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cif (wceq (cv z) c0) (cfv (cv y1) F) (cfv (cfv (cv y1) F) N))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H cgrp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf I B2 F) $ >
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq E (crn (cmpt g2 W (cop (cec (cv g2) c_sm) (co H (ccom T (cv g2)) cgsu)))) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv I cvrgp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K (co G H cghm)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (ccom K U) F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq K E) $;

--| Universal property of the free monoid by existential uniqueness. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 2-Oct-2015.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 28-Feb-2016.)
theorem frgpup3 {m: setvar} (B2 U F G H I V: class):
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv H cbs) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv I cvrgp) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel H cgrp) (wcel I V) (wf I B2 F)) (wreu m (wceq (ccom (cv m) U) F) (co G H cghm)) $;

--| The free group on zero generators is trivial. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem _0frgp (B2 G: class):
  $ wceq G (cfv c0 cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wbr B2 c1o cen $;

--| Extend class notation with class of all commutative monoids.
term ccmn: class;

--| Extend class notation with class of all Abelian groups.
term cabl: class;

--| Define class of all commutative monoids. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Jan-2015.)
axiom df_cmn {g2 a b: setvar}:
  $ wceq ccmn (crab g2 (wral a (wral b (wceq (co (cv a) (cv b) (cfv (cv g2) cplusg)) (co (cv b) (cv a) (cfv (cv g2) cplusg))) (cfv (cv g2) cbs)) (cfv (cv g2) cbs)) cmnd) $;

--| Define class of all Abelian groups. (Contributed by NM, 17-Oct-2011.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 6-Jan-2015.)
axiom df_abl:
  $ wceq cabl (cin cgrp ccmn) $;

--| The predicate "is an Abelian (commutative) group". (Contributed by NM, 17-Oct-2011.)
theorem isabl (G: class):
  $ wb (wcel G cabl) (wa (wcel G cgrp) (wcel G ccmn)) $;

--| An Abelian group is a group. (Contributed by NM, 26-Aug-2011.)
theorem ablgrp (G: class):
  $ wi (wcel G cabl) (wcel G cgrp) $;

--| An Abelian group is a group, deduction form of ~ ablgrp . (Contributed by Rohan Ridenour, 3-Aug-2023.)
theorem ablgrpd (ph: wff) (G: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cgrp) $;

--| An Abelian group is a commutative monoid. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Jan-2015.)
theorem ablcmn (G: class):
  $ wi (wcel G cabl) (wcel G ccmn) $;

--| An Abelian group is a commutative monoid. (Contributed by SN, 1-Jun-2024.)
theorem ablcmnd (ph: wff) (G: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $;

--| The predicate "is a commutative monoid". (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Jan-2015.)
theorem iscmn {x3 y1: setvar} (B2: class) (c_pl: class x3 y1) (G: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wb (wcel G ccmn) (wa (wcel G cmnd) (wral x3 (wral y1 (wceq (co (cv x3) (cv y1) c_pl) (co (cv y1) (cv x3) c_pl)) B2) B2)) $;

--| The predicate "is an Abelian (commutative) group". (Contributed by NM, 17-Oct-2011.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 6-Jan-2015.)
theorem isabl2 {x3 y1: setvar} (B2: class) (c_pl: class x3 y1) (G: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wb (wcel G cabl) (wa (wcel G cgrp) (wral x3 (wral y1 (wceq (co (cv x3) (cv y1) c_pl) (co (cv y1) (cv x3) c_pl)) B2) B2)) $;

--| If two structures have the same group components (properties), one is a commutative monoid iff the other one is. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Jan-2015.)
theorem cmnpropd {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2 K L: class):
  $ wi ph (wceq B2 (cfv K cbs)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq B2 (cfv L cbs)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wcel (cv x3) B2) (wcel (cv y1) B2))) (wceq (co (cv x3) (cv y1) (cfv K cplusg)) (co (cv x3) (cv y1) (cfv L cplusg))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wcel K ccmn) (wcel L ccmn)) $;

--| If two structures have the same group components (properties), one is an Abelian group iff the other one is. (Contributed by NM, 6-Dec-2014.)
theorem ablpropd {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2 K L: class):
  $ wi ph (wceq B2 (cfv K cbs)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq B2 (cfv L cbs)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wcel (cv x3) B2) (wcel (cv y1) B2))) (wceq (co (cv x3) (cv y1) (cfv K cplusg)) (co (cv x3) (cv y1) (cfv L cplusg))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wcel K cabl) (wcel L cabl)) $;

--| If two structures have the same group components (properties), one is an Abelian group iff the other one is. (Contributed by NM, 11-Oct-2013.)
theorem ablprop (K L: class):
  $ wceq (cfv K cbs) (cfv L cbs) $ >
  $ wceq (cfv K cplusg) (cfv L cplusg) $ >
  $ wb (wcel K cabl) (wcel L cabl) $;

--| Properties that determine a commutative monoid. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 7-Jan-2015.)
theorem iscmnd {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2: class) (c_pl: class x3 y1) (G: class):
  $ wi ph (wceq B2 (cfv G cbs)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph (wcel (cv x3) B2) (wcel (cv y1) B2)) (wceq (co (cv x3) (cv y1) c_pl) (co (cv y1) (cv x3) c_pl)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $;

--| Properties that determine an Abelian group. (Contributed by NM, 6-Aug-2013.)
theorem isabld {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2: class) (c_pl: class x3 y1) (G: class):
  $ wi ph (wceq B2 (cfv G cbs)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cgrp) $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph (wcel (cv x3) B2) (wcel (cv y1) B2)) (wceq (co (cv x3) (cv y1) c_pl) (co (cv y1) (cv x3) c_pl)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $;

--| Properties that determine an Abelian group. (Contributed by NM, 4-Sep-2011.)
theorem isabli {x3 y1: setvar} (B2: class) (c_pl: class x3 y1) (G: class):
  $ wcel G cgrp $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel (cv x3) B2) (wcel (cv y1) B2)) (wceq (co (cv x3) (cv y1) c_pl) (co (cv y1) (cv x3) c_pl)) $ >
  $ wcel G cabl $;

--| A commutative monoid is a monoid. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Jan-2015.)
theorem cmnmnd (G: class):
  $ wi (wcel G ccmn) (wcel G cmnd) $;

--| A commutative monoid is commutative. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Jan-2015.)
theorem cmncom (B2 c_pl G X Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G ccmn) (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2)) (wceq (co X Y c_pl) (co Y X c_pl)) $;

--| An Abelian group operation is commutative. (Contributed by NM, 26-Aug-2011.)
theorem ablcom (B2 c_pl G X Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G cabl) (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2)) (wceq (co X Y c_pl) (co Y X c_pl)) $;

--| Commutative/associative law for commutative monoids. (Contributed by NM, 4-Feb-2014.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem cmn32 (B2 c_pl G X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G ccmn) (w3a (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2) (wcel Z B2))) (wceq (co (co X Y c_pl) Z c_pl) (co (co X Z c_pl) Y c_pl)) $;

--| Commutative/associative law for commutative monoids. (Contributed by NM, 4-Feb-2014.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem cmn4 (B2 c_pl G W X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G ccmn) (wa (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2)) (wa (wcel Z B2) (wcel W B2))) (wceq (co (co X Y c_pl) (co Z W c_pl) c_pl) (co (co X Z c_pl) (co Y W c_pl) c_pl)) $;

--| Commutative/associative law for commutative monoids. (Contributed by Stefan O'Rear, 5-Sep-2015.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem cmn12 (B2 c_pl G X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G ccmn) (w3a (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2) (wcel Z B2))) (wceq (co X (co Y Z c_pl) c_pl) (co Y (co X Z c_pl) c_pl)) $;

--| Commutative/associative law for Abelian groups. (Contributed by Stefan O'Rear, 10-Apr-2015.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem abl32 (ph: wff) (B2 c_pl G X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co X Y c_pl) Z c_pl) (co (co X Z c_pl) Y c_pl)) $;

--| A commutative monoid is a monoid. (Contributed by SN, 1-Jun-2024.)
theorem cmnmndd (ph: wff) (G: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $;

--| The base set of a commutative monoid is its center. (Contributed by SN, 21-Mar-2025.)
theorem cmnbascntr (B2 G Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntr) $ >
  $ wi (wcel G ccmn) (wceq B2 Z) $;

--| Uniqueness of a right inverse element in a commutative monoid, if it exists. Corresponds to ~ caovmo . (Contributed by AV, 31-Dec-2023.)
theorem rinvmod {w: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 c_pl: class) (G: class w) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wrmo w (wceq (co A2 (cv w) c_pl) c_0) B2) $;

--| The inverse of an Abelian group operation. (Contributed by NM, 31-Mar-2014.)
theorem ablinvadd (B2 c_pl G N X Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv G cminusg) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G cabl) (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2)) (wceq (cfv (co X Y c_pl) N) (co (cfv X N) (cfv Y N) c_pl)) $;

--| Abelian group subtraction of two inverses. (Contributed by Stefan O'Rear, 24-May-2015.)
theorem ablsub2inv (ph: wff) (B2 G c_mi N X Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv G cminusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (cfv X N) (cfv Y N) c_mi) (co Y X c_mi)) $;

--| Relationship between Abelian group subtraction and addition. (Contributed by NM, 31-Mar-2014.)
theorem ablsubadd (B2 c_pl G c_mi X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cabl) (w3a (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2) (wcel Z B2))) (wb (wceq (co X Y c_mi) Z) (wceq (co Y Z c_pl) X)) $;

--| Commutative/associative subtraction law for Abelian groups. (Contributed by Jeff Madsen, 11-Jun-2010.) (Revised by NM, 31-Mar-2014.)
theorem ablsub4 (B2 c_pl G c_mi W X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G cabl) (wa (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2)) (wa (wcel Z B2) (wcel W B2))) (wceq (co (co X Y c_pl) (co Z W c_pl) c_mi) (co (co X Z c_mi) (co Y W c_mi) c_pl)) $;

--| Abelian group addition/subtraction law. (Contributed by NM, 31-Mar-2014.)
theorem abladdsub4 (B2 c_pl G c_mi W X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G cabl) (wa (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2)) (wa (wcel Z B2) (wcel W B2))) (wb (wceq (co X Y c_pl) (co Z W c_pl)) (wceq (co X Z c_mi) (co W Y c_mi))) $;

--| Associative-type law for group subtraction and addition. (Contributed by NM, 19-Apr-2014.)
theorem abladdsub (B2 c_pl G c_mi X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cabl) (w3a (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2) (wcel Z B2))) (wceq (co (co X Y c_pl) Z c_mi) (co (co X Z c_mi) Y c_pl)) $;

--| Commutative/associative law for addition and subtraction in abelian groups. ( ~ subadd23d analog.) (Contributed by AV, 2-Mar-2025.)
theorem ablsubadd23 (B2 c_pl G c_mi X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cabl) (w3a (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2) (wcel Z B2))) (wceq (co (co X Y c_mi) Z c_pl) (co X (co Z Y c_mi) c_pl)) $;

--| Double subtraction and addition in abelian groups. ( ~ cnambpcma analog.) (Contributed by AV, 3-Mar-2025.)
theorem ablsubaddsub (B2 c_pl G c_mi X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cabl) (w3a (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2) (wcel Z B2))) (wceq (co (co (co X Y c_mi) Z c_pl) X c_mi) (co Z Y c_mi)) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction in an Abelian group. (Contributed by NM, 2-Oct-2014.)
theorem ablpncan2 (B2 c_pl G c_mi X Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G cabl) (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2)) (wceq (co (co X Y c_pl) X c_mi) Y) $;

--| A cancellation law for Abelian groups. (Contributed by NM, 23-Mar-2015.)
theorem ablpncan3 (B2 c_pl G c_mi X Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cabl) (wa (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2))) (wceq (co X (co Y X c_mi) c_pl) Y) $;

--| Law for double subtraction. (Contributed by NM, 7-Apr-2015.)
theorem ablsubsub (ph: wff) (B2 c_pl G c_mi X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co X (co Y Z c_mi) c_mi) (co (co X Y c_mi) Z c_pl)) $;

--| Law for double subtraction. (Contributed by NM, 7-Apr-2015.)
theorem ablsubsub4 (ph: wff) (B2 c_pl G c_mi X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co X Y c_mi) Z c_mi) (co X (co Y Z c_pl) c_mi)) $;

--| Cancellation law for mixed addition and subtraction. ( ~ pnpcan analog.) (Contributed by NM, 29-May-2015.)
theorem ablpnpcan (ph: wff) (B2 c_pl G c_mi X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co X Y c_pl) (co X Z c_pl) c_mi) (co Y Z c_mi)) $;

--| Cancellation law for group subtraction. ( ~ nncan analog.) (Contributed by NM, 7-Apr-2015.)
theorem ablnncan (ph: wff) (B2 G c_mi X Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co X (co X Y c_mi) c_mi) Y) $;

--| Swap the second and third terms in a double group subtraction. (Contributed by NM, 7-Apr-2015.)
theorem ablsub32 (ph: wff) (B2 G c_mi X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co X Y c_mi) Z c_mi) (co (co X Z c_mi) Y c_mi)) $;

--| Cancellation law for group subtraction. ( ~ nnncan analog.) (Contributed by NM, 29-Feb-2008.) (Revised by AV, 27-Aug-2021.)
theorem ablnnncan (ph: wff) (B2 G c_mi X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co X (co Y Z c_mi) c_mi) Z c_mi) (co X Y c_mi)) $;

--| Cancellation law for group subtraction. ( ~ nnncan1 analog.) (Contributed by NM, 7-Apr-2015.)
theorem ablnnncan1 (ph: wff) (B2 G c_mi X Y Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co X Y c_mi) (co X Z c_mi) c_mi) (co Z Y c_mi)) $;

--| Swap subtrahend and result of group subtraction. (Contributed by NM, 14-Dec-2007.) (Revised by AV, 7-Oct-2021.)
theorem ablsubsub23 (A2 B2 C G c_mi V: class):
  $ wceq V (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cabl) (w3a (wcel A2 V) (wcel B2 V) (wcel C V))) (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 c_mi) C) (wceq (co A2 C c_mi) B2)) $;

--| Group multiple of a sum, for nonnegative multiples. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Dec-2014.)
theorem mulgnn0di (B2 c_pl c_x G M X Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G ccmn) (w3a (wcel M cn0) (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2))) (wceq (co M (co X Y c_pl) c_x) (co (co M X c_x) (co M Y c_x) c_pl)) $;

--| Group multiple of a sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Dec-2014.)
theorem mulgdi (B2 c_pl c_x G M X Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cabl) (w3a (wcel M cz) (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2))) (wceq (co M (co X Y c_pl) c_x) (co (co M X c_x) (co M Y c_x) c_pl)) $;

--| The map from ` x ` to ` n x ` for a fixed positive integer ` n ` is a monoid homomorphism if the monoid is commutative. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 4-May-2015.)
theorem mulgmhm {x3: setvar} (B2 c_x G M: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G ccmn) (wcel M cn0)) (wcel (cmpt x3 B2 (co M (cv x3) c_x)) (co G G cmhm)) $;

--| The map from ` x ` to ` n x ` for a fixed integer ` n ` is a group homomorphism if the group is commutative. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 4-May-2015.)
theorem mulgghm {x3: setvar} (B2 c_x G M: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cabl) (wcel M cz)) (wcel (cmpt x3 B2 (co M (cv x3) c_x)) (co G G cghm)) $;

--| Group multiple of a difference. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Dec-2014.)
theorem mulgsubdi (B2 c_x G M c_mi X Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cabl) (w3a (wcel M cz) (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2))) (wceq (co M (co X Y c_mi) c_x) (co (co M X c_x) (co M Y c_x) c_mi)) $;

--| The function fulfilling the conditions of ~ ghmgrp is a group homomorphism. (Contributed by Thierry Arnoux, 26-Jan-2020.)
theorem ghmfghm {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (c_pl c_pd F G H X Y: class):
  $ wceq X (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq Y (cfv H cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq c_pd (cfv H cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph (wcel (cv x3) X) (wcel (cv y1) X)) (wceq (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv y1) c_pl) F) (co (cfv (cv x3) F) (cfv (cv y1) F) c_pd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wfo X Y F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cgrp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co G H cghm)) $;

--| The image of a commutative monoid ` G ` under a group homomorphism ` F ` is a commutative monoid. (Contributed by Thierry Arnoux, 26-Jan-2020.)
theorem ghmcmn {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (c_pl c_pd F G H X Y: class):
  $ wceq X (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq Y (cfv H cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq c_pd (cfv H cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph (wcel (cv x3) X) (wcel (cv y1) X)) (wceq (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv y1) c_pl) F) (co (cfv (cv x3) F) (cfv (cv y1) F) c_pd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wfo X Y F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H ccmn) $;

--| The image of an abelian group ` G ` under a group homomorphism ` F ` is an abelian group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-May-2014.) (Revised by Thierry Arnoux, 26-Jan-2020.)
theorem ghmabl {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (c_pl c_pd F G H X Y: class):
  $ wceq X (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq Y (cfv H cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq c_pd (cfv H cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph (wcel (cv x3) X) (wcel (cv y1) X)) (wceq (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv y1) c_pl) F) (co (cfv (cv x3) F) (cfv (cv y1) F) c_pd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wfo X Y F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H cabl) $;

--| The inversion map is a group automorphism if and only if the group is abelian. (In general it is only a group homomorphism into the opposite group, but in an abelian group the opposite group coincides with the group itself.) (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 4-May-2015.)
theorem invghm (B2 G I: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq I (cfv G cminusg) $ >
  $ wb (wcel G cabl) (wcel I (co G G cghm)) $;

--| Value of the subgroup coset equivalence relation on an abelian group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 14-Jun-2015.)
theorem eqgabl (A2 B2 c_sm S G c_mi X: class):
  $ wceq X (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (co G S cqg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cabl) (wss S X)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 c_sm) (w3a (wcel A2 X) (wcel B2 X) (wcel (co B2 A2 c_mi) S))) $;

--| Two subgroup cosets are equal if and only if the difference of their representatives is a member of the subgroup. (Contributed by AV, 7-Mar-2025.)
theorem qusecsub (B2 c_sm S G c_mi X Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (co G S cqg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel G cabl) (wcel S (cfv G csubg))) (wa (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2))) (wb (wceq (cec X c_sm) (cec Y c_sm)) (wcel (co Y X c_mi) S)) $;

--| A subgroup of an abelian group is also abelian. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 3-Dec-2014.)
theorem subgabl (S G H: class):
  $ wceq H (co G S cress) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cabl) (wcel S (cfv G csubg))) (wcel H cabl) $;

--| A submonoid of a commutative monoid is also commutative. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 10-Jan-2015.)
theorem subcmn (S G H: class):
  $ wceq H (co G S cress) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G ccmn) (wcel H cmnd)) (wcel H ccmn) $;

--| A submonoid of a commutative monoid is also commutative. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.)
theorem submcmn (S G H: class):
  $ wceq H (co G S cress) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G ccmn) (wcel S (cfv G csubmnd))) (wcel H ccmn) $;

--| A submonoid is commutative iff it is a subset of its own centralizer. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.)
theorem submcmn2 (S G H Z: class):
  $ wceq H (co G S cress) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi (wcel S (cfv G csubmnd)) (wb (wcel H ccmn) (wss S (cfv S Z))) $;

--| The centralizer of any subset in a commutative monoid is the whole monoid. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 3-Oct-2015.)
theorem cntzcmn (B2 S G Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G ccmn) (wss S B2)) (wceq (cfv S Z) B2) $;

--| Any subset in a commutative monoid is a subset of its centralizer. (Contributed by AV, 12-Jan-2019.)
theorem cntzcmnss (B2 S G Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G ccmn) (wss S B2)) (wss S (cfv S Z)) $;

--| The center of a monoid is a commutative submonoid. (Contributed by Thierry Arnoux, 21-Aug-2023.)
theorem cntrcmnd (M Z: class):
  $ wceq Z (co M (cfv M ccntr) cress) $ >
  $ wi (wcel M cmnd) (wcel Z ccmn) $;

--| The center of a group is an abelian group. (Contributed by Thierry Arnoux, 21-Aug-2023.)
theorem cntrabl (M Z: class):
  $ wceq Z (co M (cfv M ccntr) cress) $ >
  $ wi (wcel M cgrp) (wcel Z cabl) $;

--| If the generators commute, the generated monoid is commutative. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem cntzspan (S G H K Z: class):
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv (cfv G csubmnd) cmrc) $ >
  $ wceq H (co G (cfv S K) cress) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cmnd) (wss S (cfv S Z))) (wcel H ccmn) $;

--| Discharge the centralizer assumption in a commutative monoid. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.)
theorem cntzcmnf (ph: wff) (A2 B2 F G Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $;

--| The pointwise sum of two linear functions is linear. (Contributed by Stefan O'Rear, 5-Sep-2015.)
theorem ghmplusg (c_pl F G M N: class):
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv N cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel N cabl) (wcel F (co M N cghm)) (wcel G (co M N cghm))) (wcel (co F G (cof c_pl)) (co M N cghm)) $;

--| Every subgroup of an abelian group is normal. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 14-Jun-2015.)
theorem ablnsg (G: class):
  $ wi (wcel G cabl) (wceq (cfv G cnsg) (cfv G csubg)) $;

--| The order of a product in an abelian group divides the LCM of the orders of the factors. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 20-Oct-2015.)
theorem odadd1 (A2 B2 c_pl G O X: class):
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G cabl) (wcel A2 X) (wcel B2 X)) (wbr (co (cfv (co A2 B2 c_pl) O) (co (cfv A2 O) (cfv B2 O) cgcd) cmul) (co (cfv A2 O) (cfv B2 O) cmul) cdvds) $;

--| The order of a product in an abelian group is divisible by the LCM of the orders of the factors divided by the GCD. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 20-Oct-2015.)
theorem odadd2 (A2 B2 c_pl G O X: class):
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G cabl) (wcel A2 X) (wcel B2 X)) (wbr (co (cfv A2 O) (cfv B2 O) cmul) (co (cfv (co A2 B2 c_pl) O) (co (co (cfv A2 O) (cfv B2 O) cgcd) c2 cexp) cmul) cdvds) $;

--| The order of a product is the product of the orders, if the factors have coprime order. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 20-Oct-2015.)
theorem odadd (A2 B2 c_pl G O X: class):
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel G cabl) (wcel A2 X) (wcel B2 X)) (wceq (co (cfv A2 O) (cfv B2 O) cgcd) c1)) (wceq (cfv (co A2 B2 c_pl) O) (co (cfv A2 O) (cfv B2 O) cmul)) $;

--| A group with exponent 2 (or 1) is abelian. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.)
theorem gex2abl (E G X: class):
  $ wceq X (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv G cgex) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cgrp) (wbr E c2 cdvds)) (wcel G cabl) $;

--| Lemma for ~ gexex . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.)
theorem gexexlem {y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 E G O X: class):
  $ wceq X (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv G cgex) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 X) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv y1) X)) (wbr (cfv (cv y1) O) (cfv A2 O) cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv A2 O) E) $;

--| In an abelian group with finite exponent, there is an element in the group with order equal to the exponent. In other words, all orders of elements divide the largest order of an element of the group. This fails if ` E = 0 ` , for example in an infinite p-group, where there are elements of arbitrarily large orders (so ` E ` is zero) but no elements of infinite order. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.)
theorem gexex {x3: setvar} (E G O X: class):
  $ wceq X (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv G cgex) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cabl) (wcel E cn)) (wrex x3 (wceq (cfv (cv x3) O) E) X) $;

--| The set of all elements of finite order forms a subgroup of any abelian group, called the torsion subgroup. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 20-Oct-2015.)
theorem torsubg (G O: class):
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wi (wcel G cabl) (wcel (cima (ccnv O) cn) (cfv G csubg)) $;

--| The set of all elements whose order divides a fixed integer is a subgroup of any abelian group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 19-Apr-2016.)
theorem oddvdssubg {x3: setvar} (B2 G N O: class):
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cabl) (wcel N cz)) (wcel (crab x3 (wbr (cfv (cv x3) O) N cdvds) B2) (cfv G csubg)) $;

--| Subgroup sum commutes (extended domain version). (Contributed by NM, 25-Feb-2014.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 19-Apr-2016.)
theorem lsmcomx (B2 c_po T U G: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_po (cfv G clsm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G cabl) (wss T B2) (wss U B2)) (wceq (co T U c_po) (co U T c_po)) $;

--| All subgroups in an abelian group commute. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 19-Apr-2016.)
theorem ablcntzd (ph: wff) (T U G Z: class):
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel T (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss T (cfv U Z)) $;

--| Subgroup sum commutes. (Contributed by NM, 6-Feb-2014.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 21-Jun-2014.)
theorem lsmcom (c_po T U G: class):
  $ wceq c_po (cfv G clsm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G cabl) (wcel T (cfv G csubg)) (wcel U (cfv G csubg))) (wceq (co T U c_po) (co U T c_po)) $;

--| The sum of two subgroups is a subgroup. (Contributed by NM, 4-Feb-2014.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 19-Apr-2016.)
theorem lsmsubg2 (c_po T U G: class):
  $ wceq c_po (cfv G clsm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G cabl) (wcel T (cfv G csubg)) (wcel U (cfv G csubg))) (wcel (co T U c_po) (cfv G csubg)) $;

--| Commutative/associative law for subgroup sum. (Contributed by NM, 26-Sep-2014.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 19-Apr-2016.)
theorem lsm4 (c_po Q R T U G: class):
  $ wceq c_po (cfv G clsm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G cabl) (wa (wcel Q (cfv G csubg)) (wcel R (cfv G csubg))) (wa (wcel T (cfv G csubg)) (wcel U (cfv G csubg)))) (wceq (co (co Q R c_po) (co T U c_po) c_po) (co (co Q T c_po) (co R U c_po) c_po)) $;

--| The product of a family of commutative monoids is commutative. (Contributed by Stefan O'Rear, 10-Jan-2015.)
theorem prdscmnd (ph: wff) (R S I V W Y: class):
  $ wceq Y (co S R cprds) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf I ccmn R) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y ccmn) $;

--| The product of a family of Abelian groups is an Abelian group. (Contributed by Stefan O'Rear, 10-Jan-2015.)
theorem prdsabld (ph: wff) (R S I V W Y: class):
  $ wceq Y (co S R cprds) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf I cabl R) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y cabl) $;

--| The structure power on a commutative monoid is commutative. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Jan-2015.)
theorem pwscmn (R I V Y: class):
  $ wceq Y (co R I cpws) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel R ccmn) (wcel I V)) (wcel Y ccmn) $;

--| The structure power on an Abelian group is Abelian. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Jan-2015.)
theorem pwsabl (R I V Y: class):
  $ wceq Y (co R I cpws) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel R cabl) (wcel I V)) (wcel Y cabl) $;

--| If ` Y ` is a subgroup of the abelian group ` G ` , then ` H = G / Y ` is an abelian group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem qusabl (S G H: class):
  $ wceq H (co G (co G S cqg) cqus) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cabl) (wcel S (cfv G csubg))) (wcel H cabl) $;

--| The (smallest) structure representing a _trivial abelian group_. (Contributed by AV, 28-Apr-2019.)
theorem abl1 (I M V: class):
  $ wceq M (cpr (cop (cfv cnx cbs) (csn I)) (cop (cfv cnx cplusg) (csn (cop (cop I I) I)))) $ >
  $ wi (wcel I V) (wcel M cabl) $;

--| Abelian groups (and therefore also groups and monoids) exist. (Contributed by AV, 29-Apr-2019.)
theorem abln0:
  $ wne cabl c0 $;

--| The complex numbers are an Abelian group under addition. This version of ~ cnaddabl shows the explicit structure "scaffold" we chose for the definition for Abelian groups. Note: This theorem has hard-coded structure indices for demonstration purposes. It is not intended for general use; use ~ cnaddabl instead. (New usage is discouraged.) (Contributed by NM, 18-Oct-2012.)
theorem cnaddablx (G: class):
  $ wceq G (cpr (cop c1 cc) (cop c2 caddc)) $ >
  $ wcel G cabl $;

--| The complex numbers are an Abelian group under addition. This version of ~ cnaddablx hides the explicit structure indices i.e. is "scaffold-independent". Note that the proof also does not reference explicit structure indices. The actual structure is dependent on how ` Base ` and ` +g ` is defined. This theorem should not be referenced in any proof. For the group/ring properties of the complex numbers, see ~ cnring . (Contributed by NM, 20-Oct-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem cnaddabl (G: class):
  $ wceq G (cpr (cop (cfv cnx cbs) cc) (cop (cfv cnx cplusg) caddc)) $ >
  $ wcel G cabl $;

--| The group identity element of complex number addition is zero. See also ~ cnfld0 . (Contributed by Steve Rodriguez, 3-Dec-2006.) (Revised by AV, 26-Aug-2021.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem cnaddid (G: class):
  $ wceq G (cpr (cop (cfv cnx cbs) cc) (cop (cfv cnx cplusg) caddc)) $ >
  $ wceq (cfv G c0g) cc0 $;

--| Value of the group inverse of complex number addition. See also ~ cnfldneg . (Contributed by Steve Rodriguez, 3-Dec-2006.) (Revised by AV, 26-Aug-2021.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem cnaddinv (A2 G: class):
  $ wceq G (cpr (cop (cfv cnx cbs) cc) (cop (cfv cnx cplusg) caddc)) $ >
  $ wi (wcel A2 cc) (wceq (cfv A2 (cfv G cminusg)) (cneg A2)) $;

--| The integers are an Abelian group under addition. Note: This theorem has hard-coded structure indices for demonstration purposes. It is not intended for general use. Use ~ zsubrg instead. (New usage is discouraged.) (Contributed by NM, 4-Sep-2011.)
theorem zaddablx (G: class):
  $ wceq G (cpr (cop c1 cz) (cop c2 caddc)) $ >
  $ wcel G cabl $;

--| Lemma for ~ frgpnabl . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 25-Apr-2024.)
theorem frgpnabllem1 {x3 y1 z w v n: setvar} (ph: wff y1 z w v n) (A2 B2: class y1 z w v n) (D c_pl: class x3 y1 z w v n) (c_sm: class w v n) (T: class y1 z w v n) (U: class x3 y1 z w v n) (G: class y1 z w v n) (I: class) (M: class y1 z) (V: class x3 y1 z w v n) (W: class):
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq M (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cop (cv y1) (cdif c1o (cv z)))) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpt v W (cmpo n w (co cc0 (cfv (cv v) chash) cfz) (cxp I c2o) (co (cv v) (cotp (cv n) (cv n) (cs2 (cv w) (cfv (cv w) M))) csplice))) $ >
  $ wceq D (cdif W (ciun x3 W (crn (cfv (cv x3) T)))) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv I cvrgp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cs2 (cop A2 c0) (cop B2 c0)) (cin D (co (cfv A2 U) (cfv B2 U) c_pl))) $;

--| Lemma for ~ frgpnabl . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 25-Apr-2024.)
theorem frgpnabllem2 {x3 y1 z w v n: setvar} (ph: wff y1 z w v n) (A2 B2: class y1 z w v n) (D c_pl: class x3 y1 z w v n) (c_sm: class w v n) (T: class y1 z w v n) (U: class x3 y1 z w v n) (G: class y1 z w v n) (I: class) (M: class y1 z) (V: class x3 y1 z w v n) (W: class):
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wceq W (cfv (cword (cxp I c2o)) cid) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv I cefg) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq M (cmpo y1 z I c2o (cop (cv y1) (cdif c1o (cv z)))) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpt v W (cmpo n w (co cc0 (cfv (cv v) chash) cfz) (cxp I c2o) (co (cv v) (cotp (cv n) (cv n) (cs2 (cv w) (cfv (cv w) M))) csplice))) $ >
  $ wceq D (cdif W (ciun x3 W (crn (cfv (cv x3) T)))) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv I cvrgp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (cfv A2 U) (cfv B2 U) c_pl) (co (cfv B2 U) (cfv A2 U) c_pl)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 B2) $;

--| The free group on two or more generators is not abelian. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem frgpnabl (G I: class):
  $ wceq G (cfv I cfrgp) $ >
  $ wi (wbr c1o I csdm) (wn (wcel G cabl)) $;

--| The image structure of an abelian group is an abelian group ( ~ imasgrp analog). (Contributed by AV, 22-Feb-2025.)
theorem imasabl {q p a b: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2: class) (c_pl R: class a b) (U F V c_0: class):
  $ wi ph (wceq U (co F R cimas)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq V (cfv R cbs)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq c_pl (cfv R cplusg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wfo V B2 F) $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph (wa (wcel (cv a) V) (wcel (cv b) V)) (wa (wcel (cv p) V) (wcel (cv q) V))) (wi (wa (wceq (cfv (cv a) F) (cfv (cv p) F)) (wceq (cfv (cv b) F) (cfv (cv q) F))) (wceq (cfv (co (cv a) (cv b) c_pl) F) (cfv (co (cv p) (cv q) c_pl) F))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel R cabl) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv R c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel U cabl) (wceq (cfv c_0 F) (cfv U c0g))) $;

--| Cyclic group.
term ccyg: class;

--| Define a cyclic group, which is a group with an element ` x ` , called the generator of the group, such that all elements in the group are multiples of ` x ` . A generator is usually not unique. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
axiom df_cyg {x3 g2 n: setvar}:
  $ wceq ccyg (crab g2 (wrex x3 (wceq (crn (cmpt n cz (co (cv n) (cv x3) (cfv (cv g2) cmg)))) (cfv (cv g2) cbs)) (cfv (cv g2) cbs)) cgrp) $;

--| Definition of a cyclic group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem iscyg {x3 n: setvar} (B2 c_x G: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wb (wcel G ccyg) (wa (wcel G cgrp) (wrex x3 (wceq (crn (cmpt n cz (co (cv n) (cv x3) c_x))) B2) B2)) $;

--| The property of being a cyclic generator for a group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem iscyggen {x3 n: setvar} (B2 c_x: class) (E: class x3 n) (G X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wceq E (crab x3 (wceq (crn (cmpt n cz (co (cv n) (cv x3) c_x))) B2) B2) $ >
  $ wb (wcel X E) (wa (wcel X B2) (wceq (crn (cmpt n cz (co (cv n) X c_x))) B2)) $;

--| The property of being a cyclic generator for a group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem iscyggen2 {x3 y1 n: setvar} (B2 c_x: class) (E: class x3 n) (G X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wceq E (crab x3 (wceq (crn (cmpt n cz (co (cv n) (cv x3) c_x))) B2) B2) $ >
  $ wi (wcel G cgrp) (wb (wcel X E) (wa (wcel X B2) (wral y1 (wrex n (wceq (cv y1) (co (cv n) X c_x)) cz) B2))) $;

--| A cyclic group is a group which contains a generator. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem iscyg2 {x3 n: setvar} (B2 c_x: class) (E: class x3 n) (G: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wceq E (crab x3 (wceq (crn (cmpt n cz (co (cv n) (cv x3) c_x))) B2) B2) $ >
  $ wb (wcel G ccyg) (wa (wcel G cgrp) (wne E c0)) $;

--| The inverse of a cyclic generator is a generator. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem cyggeninv {x3 n: setvar} (B2 c_x: class) (E: class x3 n) (G N X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wceq E (crab x3 (wceq (crn (cmpt n cz (co (cv n) (cv x3) c_x))) B2) B2) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv G cminusg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cgrp) (wcel X E)) (wcel (cfv X N) E) $;

--| An element is the generator of a finite group iff the order of the generator equals the order of the group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem cyggenod {x3 n: setvar} (B2 c_x: class) (E: class x3 n) (G: class) (O: class x3) (X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wceq E (crab x3 (wceq (crn (cmpt n cz (co (cv n) (cv x3) c_x))) B2) B2) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cgrp) (wcel B2 cfn)) (wb (wcel X E) (wa (wcel X B2) (wceq (cfv X O) (cfv B2 chash)))) $;

--| In an infinite cyclic group, the generator must have infinite order, but this property no longer characterizes the generators. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem cyggenod2 {x3 n: setvar} (B2 c_x: class) (E: class x3 n) (G: class) (O: class x3) (X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wceq E (crab x3 (wceq (crn (cmpt n cz (co (cv n) (cv x3) c_x))) B2) B2) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cgrp) (wcel X E)) (wceq (cfv X O) (cif (wcel B2 cfn) (cfv B2 chash) cc0)) $;

--| Definition of a cyclic group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem iscyg3 {x3 y1 n: setvar} (B2 c_x G: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wb (wcel G ccyg) (wa (wcel G cgrp) (wrex x3 (wral y1 (wrex n (wceq (cv y1) (co (cv n) (cv x3) c_x)) cz) B2) B2)) $;

--| Definition of a cyclic group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem iscygd {y1 n: setvar} (ph: wff n) (B2 c_x G X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cgrp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv y1) B2)) (wrex n (wceq (cv y1) (co (cv n) X c_x)) cz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccyg) $;

--| Show that a group with an element the same order as the group is cyclic. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-Apr-2016.)
theorem iscygodd (ph: wff) (B2 G O X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cgrp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv X O) (cfv B2 chash)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccyg) $;

--| The set of nonnegative integer powers of an element ` A ` of a monoid forms a commutative monoid. (Contributed by AV, 20-Jan-2024.)
theorem cycsubmcmn {x3: setvar} (A2 B2 C c_x: class) (F: class x3) (G: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt x3 cn0 (co (cv x3) A2 c_x)) $ >
  $ wceq C (crn F) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cmnd) (wcel A2 B2)) (wcel (co G C cress) ccmn) $;

--| A cyclic group is a group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem cyggrp (G: class):
  $ wi (wcel G ccyg) (wcel G cgrp) $;

--| A cyclic group is abelian. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.) (Proof shortened by AV, 20-Jan-2024.)
theorem cygabl (G: class):
  $ wi (wcel G ccyg) (wcel G cabl) $;

--| A cyclic group is countable. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem cygctb (B2 G: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi (wcel G ccyg) (wbr B2 com cdom) $;

--| The trivial group is cyclic. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem _0cyg (B2 G: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cgrp) (wbr B2 c1o cen)) (wcel G ccyg) $;

--| A group with prime order is cyclic. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-Apr-2016.)
theorem prmcyg (B2 G: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cgrp) (wcel (cfv B2 chash) cprime)) (wcel G ccyg) $;

--| A group with fewer than ` 6 ` elements is abelian. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-Apr-2016.)
theorem lt6abl (B2 G: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cgrp) (wbr (cfv B2 chash) c6 clt)) (wcel G cabl) $;

--| The image of a cyclic group under a surjective group homomorphism is cyclic. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem ghmcyg (B2 C F G H: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv H cbs) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel F (co G H cghm)) (wfo B2 C F)) (wi (wcel G ccyg) (wcel H ccyg)) $;

--| The exponent of a cyclic group is ` 0 ` if the group is infinite, otherwise it equals the order of the group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.)
theorem cyggex2 (B2 E G: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv G cgex) $ >
  $ wi (wcel G ccyg) (wceq E (cif (wcel B2 cfn) (cfv B2 chash) cc0)) $;

--| The exponent of a finite cyclic group is the order of the group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.)
theorem cyggex (B2 E G: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv G cgex) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G ccyg) (wcel B2 cfn)) (wceq E (cfv B2 chash)) $;

--| A finite abelian group is cyclic iff the exponent equals the order of the group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem cyggexb (B2 E G: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv G cgex) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cabl) (wcel B2 cfn)) (wb (wcel G ccyg) (wceq E (cfv B2 chash))) $;

--| Cyclicity is a group property, i.e. it is preserved under isomorphism. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem giccyg (G H: class):
  $ wi (wbr G H cgic) (wi (wcel G ccyg) (wcel H ccyg)) $;

--| The cyclic subgroup generated by ` A ` is a cyclic group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.)
theorem cycsubgcyg {x3: setvar} (A2: class) (S: class x3) (c_x G X: class):
  $ wceq X (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wceq S (crn (cmpt x3 cz (co (cv x3) A2 c_x))) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cgrp) (wcel A2 X)) (wcel (co G S cress) ccyg) $;

--| The cyclic subgroup generated by ` A ` is a cyclic group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-Apr-2016.)
theorem cycsubgcyg2 (A2 B2 G K: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv (cfv G csubg) cmrc) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cgrp) (wcel A2 B2)) (wcel (co G (cfv (csn A2) K) cress) ccyg) $;

--| Value of the group sum operation over an index set with finite support. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 7-Dec-2014.) (Revised by AV, 29-May-2019.)
theorem gsumval3a {x3 f2: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 c_pl F G: class) (V: class f2) (W: class) (c_0: class f2) (Z: class x3 f2):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel W cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne W c0) $ >
  $ wceq W (co F c_0 csupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn (wcel A2 (crn cfz))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G F cgsu) (cio x3 (wex f2 (wa (wf1o (co c1 (cfv W chash) cfz) W (cv f2)) (wceq (cv x3) (cfv (cfv W chash) (cseq c_pl (ccom F (cv f2)) c1))))))) $;

--| The group sum as defined in ~ gsumval3a is uniquely defined. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 8-Dec-2014.)
theorem gsumval3eu {x3 f2: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 c_pl F G: class) (V: class f2) (W: class) (c_0: class f2) (Z: class x3 f2):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel W cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne W c0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss W A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (weu x3 (wex f2 (wa (wf1o (co c1 (cfv W chash) cfz) W (cv f2)) (wceq (cv x3) (cfv (cfv W chash) (cseq c_pl (ccom F (cv f2)) c1)))))) $;

--| Lemma 1 for ~ gsumval3 . (Contributed by AV, 31-May-2019.)
theorem gsumval3lem1 (ph: wff) (A2 B2 c_pl: class) (f2: setvar) (F G H M V W c_0 Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf1 (co c1 M cfz) A2 H) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (co F c_0 csupp) (crn H)) $ >
  $ wceq W (co (ccom F H) c_0 csupp) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph (wne W c0)) (wa (wn (wcel A2 (crn cfz))) (wiso (co c1 (cfv W chash) cfz) W clt clt (cv f2)))) (wf1o (co c1 (cfv (co F c_0 csupp) chash) cfz) (co F c_0 csupp) (ccom H (cv f2))) $;

--| Lemma 2 for ~ gsumval3 . (Contributed by AV, 31-May-2019.)
theorem gsumval3lem2 {f2: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 c_pl F G H M: class) (V: class f2) (W: class) (c_0 Z: class f2):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf1 (co c1 M cfz) A2 H) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (co F c_0 csupp) (crn H)) $ >
  $ wceq W (co (ccom F H) c_0 csupp) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph (wne W c0)) (wa (wn (wcel A2 (crn cfz))) (wiso (co c1 (cfv W chash) cfz) W clt clt (cv f2)))) (wceq (co G F cgsu) (cfv (cfv W chash) (cseq c_pl (ccom F (ccom H (cv f2))) c1))) $;

--| Value of the group sum operation over an arbitrary finite set. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Dec-2014.) (Revised by AV, 31-May-2019.)
theorem gsumval3 (ph: wff) (A2 B2 c_pl F G H M V W c_0 Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf1 (co c1 M cfz) A2 H) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (co F c_0 csupp) (crn H)) $ >
  $ wceq W (co (ccom F H) c_0 csupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G F cgsu) (cfv M (cseq c_pl (ccom F H) c1))) $;

--| Lemma for ~ gsumcl and related theorems. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Dec-2014.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 31-May-2019.)
theorem gsumcllem {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class) (B2 U: class k) (F: class) (V: class k) (W: class) (Z: class k):
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (co F Z csupp) W) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wceq W c0)) (wceq F (cmpt k A2 Z)) $;

--| Extend a finite group sum by padding outside with zeroes. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 31-May-2019.)
theorem gsumzres (ph: wff) (A2 B2 F G V W c_0 Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (co F c_0 csupp) W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cres F W) cgsu) (co G F cgsu)) $;

--| Closure of a finite group sum. This theorem has a weaker hypothesis than ~ gsumzcl , because it is not required that ` F ` is a function (actually, the hypothesis always holds for any proper class ` F ` ). (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 1-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumzcl2 (ph: wff) (A2 B2 F G V c_0 Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co F c_0 csupp) cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co G F cgsu) B2) $;

--| Closure of a finite group sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 1-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumzcl (ph: wff) (A2 B2 F G V c_0 Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co G F cgsu) B2) $;

--| Re-index a finite group sum using a bijection. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 2-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumzf1o (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C F G H V c_0 Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf1o C A2 H) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G F cgsu) (co G (ccom F H) cgsu)) $;

--| Extend a finite group sum by padding outside with zeroes. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Dec-2014.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 3-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumres (ph: wff) (A2 B2 F G V W c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (co F c_0 csupp) W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cres F W) cgsu) (co G F cgsu)) $;

--| Closure of a finite group sum. This theorem has a weaker hypothesis than ~ gsumcl , because it is not required that ` F ` is a function (actually, the hypothesis always holds for any proper class ` F ` ). (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Dec-2014.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 3-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumcl2 (ph: wff) (A2 B2 F G V c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co F c_0 csupp) cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co G F cgsu) B2) $;

--| Closure of a finite group sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Dec-2014.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 3-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumcl (ph: wff) (A2 B2 F G V c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co G F cgsu) B2) $;

--| Re-index a finite group sum using a bijection. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Dec-2014.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 3-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumf1o (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C F G H V c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf1o C A2 H) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G F cgsu) (co G (ccom F H) cgsu)) $;

--| Re-index a finite group sum using a bijection. Corresponds to the first equation in [Lang] p. 5 with ` M = 1 ` . (Contributed by AV, 26-Dec-2023.)
theorem gsumreidx (ph: wff) (B2 F G H M N c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf (co M N cfz) B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf1o (co M N cfz) (co M N cfz) H) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G F cgsu) (co G (ccom F H) cgsu)) $;

--| Closure of a group sum in a submonoid. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 3-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumzsubmcl (ph: wff) (A2 S F G V c_0 Z: class):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S (cfv G csubmnd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 S F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co G F cgsu) S) $;

--| Closure of a group sum in a submonoid. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 10-Jan-2015.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 3-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumsubmcl (ph: wff) (A2 S F G V c_0: class):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S (cfv G csubmnd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 S F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co G F cgsu) S) $;

--| Closure of a group sum in a subgroup. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Dec-2014.) (Revised by AV, 3-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumsubgcl (ph: wff) (A2 S F G V c_0: class):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 S F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co G F cgsu) S) $;

--| The sum of two group sums. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 5-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumzaddlem {x3 k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 c_pl F G H: class) (V: class k) (W c_0 Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr H c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wceq W (co (cun F H) c_0 csupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 H) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn H) (cfv (crn H) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn (co F H (cof c_pl))) (cfv (crn (co F H (cof c_pl))) Z)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wss (cv x3) A2) (wcel (cv k) (cdif A2 (cv x3))))) (wcel (cfv (cv k) F) (cfv (csn (co G (cres H (cv x3)) cgsu)) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (co F H (cof c_pl)) cgsu) (co (co G F cgsu) (co G H cgsu) c_pl)) $;

--| The sum of two group sums. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 5-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumzadd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 c_pl S F G H V c_0 Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr H c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S (cfv G csubmnd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss S (cfv S Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 S F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 S H) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (co F H (cof c_pl)) cgsu) (co (co G F cgsu) (co G H cgsu) c_pl)) $;

--| The sum of two group sums. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 19-Dec-2014.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 5-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumadd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 c_pl F G H V c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 H) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr H c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (co F H (cof c_pl)) cgsu) (co (co G F cgsu) (co G H cgsu) c_pl)) $;

--| The sum of two group sums expressed as mappings. (Contributed by AV, 4-Apr-2019.) (Revised by AV, 9-Jul-2019.)
theorem gsummptfsadd {x3: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (C D: class x3) (c_pl: class) (F G H V c_0: class x3):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) A2)) (wcel C B2) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) A2)) (wcel D B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq F (cmpt x3 A2 C)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq H (cmpt x3 A2 D)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr H c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt x3 A2 (co C D c_pl)) cgsu) (co (co G F cgsu) (co G H cgsu) c_pl)) $;

--| The sum of two group sums expressed as mappings with finite domain. (Contributed by AV, 23-Jul-2019.)
theorem gsummptfidmadd {x3: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (C D: class x3) (c_pl: class) (F G H: class x3):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) A2)) (wcel C B2) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) A2)) (wcel D B2) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt x3 A2 C) $ >
  $ wceq H (cmpt x3 A2 D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt x3 A2 (co C D c_pl)) cgsu) (co (co G F cgsu) (co G H cgsu) c_pl)) $;

--| The sum of two group sums expressed as mappings with finite domain, using a function operation. (Contributed by AV, 23-Jul-2019.)
theorem gsummptfidmadd2 {x3: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (C D: class x3) (c_pl: class) (F G H: class x3):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) A2)) (wcel C B2) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) A2)) (wcel D B2) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt x3 A2 C) $ >
  $ wceq H (cmpt x3 A2 D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (co F H (cof c_pl)) cgsu) (co (co G F cgsu) (co G H cgsu) c_pl)) $;

--| Split a group sum into two parts. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 5-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumzsplit (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D c_pl F G V c_0 Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin C D) c0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 (cun C D)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G F cgsu) (co (co G (cres F C) cgsu) (co G (cres F D) cgsu) c_pl)) $;

--| Split a group sum into two parts. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 19-Dec-2014.) (Revised by AV, 5-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumsplit (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D c_pl F G V c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin C D) c0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 (cun C D)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G F cgsu) (co (co G (cres F C) cgsu) (co G (cres F D) cgsu) c_pl)) $;

--| Split a group sum into two parts. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 19-Dec-2014.) (Revised by AV, 5-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumsplit2 {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class) (c_pl G V X c_0: class k):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv k) A2)) (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cmpt k A2 X) c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin C D) c0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 (cun C D)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt k A2 X) cgsu) (co (co G (cmpt k C X) cgsu) (co G (cmpt k D X) cgsu) c_pl)) $;

--| Split a group sum expressed as mapping with a finite domain into two parts. (Contributed by AV, 23-Jul-2019.)
theorem gsummptfidmsplit {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class) (c_pl G Y: class k):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv k) A2)) (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin C D) c0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 (cun C D)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt k A2 Y) cgsu) (co (co G (cmpt k C Y) cgsu) (co G (cmpt k D Y) cgsu) c_pl)) $;

--| Split a group sum expressed as mapping with a finite domain into two parts using restrictions. (Contributed by AV, 23-Jul-2019.)
theorem gsummptfidmsplitres {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class) (c_pl F G Y: class k):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv k) A2)) (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin C D) c0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 (cun C D)) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt k A2 Y) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G F cgsu) (co (co G (cres F C) cgsu) (co G (cres F D) cgsu) c_pl)) $;

--| Split a group sum expressed as mapping with a finite set of sequential integers as domain into two parts, extracting a singleton from the right. (Contributed by AV, 25-Oct-2019.)
theorem gsummptfzsplit {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2: class) (c_pl G: class k) (N: class) (Y: class k):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn0) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv k) (co cc0 (co N c1 caddc) cfz))) (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt k (co cc0 (co N c1 caddc) cfz) Y) cgsu) (co (co G (cmpt k (co cc0 N cfz) Y) cgsu) (co G (cmpt k (csn (co N c1 caddc)) Y) cgsu) c_pl)) $;

--| Split a group sum expressed as mapping with a finite set of sequential integers as domain into two parts, , extracting a singleton from the left. (Contributed by AV, 7-Nov-2019.)
theorem gsummptfzsplitl {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2: class) (c_pl G: class k) (N: class) (Y: class k):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn0) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv k) (co cc0 N cfz))) (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt k (co cc0 N cfz) Y) cgsu) (co (co G (cmpt k (co c1 N cfz) Y) cgsu) (co G (cmpt k (csn cc0) Y) cgsu) c_pl)) $;

--| Sum of a constant series. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 19-Dec-2014.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.)
theorem gsumconst {k: setvar} (A2 B2: class) (c_x: class k) (G X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G cmnd) (wcel A2 cfn) (wcel X B2)) (wceq (co G (cmpt k A2 X) cgsu) (co (cfv A2 chash) X c_x)) $;

--| Sum of a constant series. (Contributed by Thierry Arnoux, 5-Jul-2017.)
theorem gsumconstf {k: setvar} (A2: class) (B2 c_x G X: class k):
  $ wnfc k X $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G cmnd) (wcel A2 cfn) (wcel X B2)) (wceq (co G (cmpt k A2 X) cgsu) (co (cfv A2 chash) X c_x)) $;

--| Index shift of a finite group sum over a finite set of sequential integers. (Contributed by AV, 24-Aug-2019.)
theorem gsummptshft {j k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class j) (B2 C: class k) (G: class j k) (K M N: class) (c_0: class j k):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K cz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M cz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cz) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv j) (co M N cfz))) (wcel A2 B2) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv j) (co (cv k) K cmin)) (wceq A2 C) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt j (co M N cfz) A2) cgsu) (co G (cmpt k (co (co M K caddc) (co N K caddc) cfz) C) cgsu)) $;

--| Apply a group homomorphism to a group sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 6-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumzmhm (ph: wff) (A2 B2 F G H K V c_0 Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K (co G H cmhm)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co H (ccom K F) cgsu) (cfv (co G F cgsu) K)) $;

--| Apply a group homomorphism to a group sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Dec-2014.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 6-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsummhm (ph: wff) (A2 B2 F G H K V c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K (co G H cmhm)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co H (ccom K F) cgsu) (cfv (co G F cgsu) K)) $;

--| Apply a group homomorphism to a group sum, mapping version with implicit substitution. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 5-May-2015.) (Revised by AV, 6-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsummhm2 {x3 k: setvar} (ph: wff x3) (A2 B2: class) (C: class x3) (D E G H: class k) (V: class x3 k) (X: class k) (c_0: class x3 k):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 B2 C) (co G H cmhm)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv k) A2)) (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cmpt k A2 X) c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv x3) X) (wceq C D) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv x3) (co G (cmpt k A2 X) cgsu)) (wceq C E) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co H (cmpt k A2 D) cgsu) E) $;

--| Apply a group homomorphism to a group sum expressed with a mapping. (Contributed by Thierry Arnoux, 7-Sep-2018.) (Revised by AV, 8-Sep-2019.)
theorem gsummptmhm {x3: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (C G H: class x3) (K: class) (V c_0: class x3):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K (co G H cmhm)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) A2)) (wcel C B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cmpt x3 A2 C) c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co H (cmpt x3 A2 (cfv C K)) cgsu) (cfv (co G (cmpt x3 A2 C) cgsu) K)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ gsummulg and ~ gsummulgz . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 7-Jan-2015.) (Revised by AV, 6-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsummulglem {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 c_x: class) (G: class k) (N: class) (V X c_0: class k):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv k) A2)) (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cmpt k A2 X) c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wo (wcel G cabl) (wcel N cn0)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt k A2 (co N X c_x)) cgsu) (co N (co G (cmpt k A2 X) cgsu) c_x)) $;

--| Nonnegative multiple of a group sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Dec-2014.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 7-Jan-2015.) (Revised by AV, 6-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsummulg {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 c_x: class) (G: class k) (N: class) (V X c_0: class k):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv k) A2)) (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cmpt k A2 X) c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt k A2 (co N X c_x)) cgsu) (co N (co G (cmpt k A2 X) cgsu) c_x)) $;

--| Integer multiple of a group sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 7-Jan-2015.) (Revised by AV, 6-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsummulgz {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 c_x: class) (G: class k) (N: class) (V X c_0: class k):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv k) A2)) (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cmpt k A2 X) c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt k A2 (co N X c_x)) cgsu) (co N (co G (cmpt k A2 X) cgsu) c_x)) $;

--| The opposite of a group sum is the same as the original. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 6-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumzoppg (ph: wff) (A2 B2 F G O V c_0 Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G coppg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co O F cgsu) (co G F cgsu)) $;

--| Inverse of a group sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 6-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumzinv (ph: wff) (A2 B2 F G I V c_0 Z: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wceq I (cfv G cminusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cgrp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (ccom I F) cgsu) (cfv (co G F cgsu) I)) $;

--| Inverse of a group sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 15-Dec-2014.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 4-May-2015.) (Revised by AV, 6-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsuminv (ph: wff) (A2 B2 F G I V c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq I (cfv G cminusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (ccom I F) cgsu) (cfv (co G F cgsu) I)) $;

--| Inverse of a group sum expressed as mapping with a finite domain. (Contributed by AV, 23-Jul-2019.)
theorem gsummptfidminv {x3: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (C F G I c_0: class x3):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq I (cfv G cminusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) A2)) (wcel C B2) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt x3 A2 C) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (ccom I F) cgsu) (cfv (co G F cgsu) I)) $;

--| The difference of two group sums. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-Dec-2014.) (Revised by AV, 6-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumsub (ph: wff) (A2 B2 F G H c_mi V c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 H) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr H c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (co F H (cof c_mi)) cgsu) (co (co G F cgsu) (co G H cgsu) c_mi)) $;

--| The difference of two group sums expressed as mappings. (Contributed by AV, 7-Nov-2019.)
theorem gsummptfssub {x3: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (C D F G H: class x3) (c_mi: class) (V c_0: class x3):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) A2)) (wcel C B2) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) A2)) (wcel D B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq F (cmpt x3 A2 C)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq H (cmpt x3 A2 D)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr H c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt x3 A2 (co C D c_mi)) cgsu) (co (co G F cgsu) (co G H cgsu) c_mi)) $;

--| The difference of two group sums expressed as mappings with finite domain. (Contributed by AV, 7-Nov-2019.)
theorem gsummptfidmsub {x3: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (C D F G H: class x3) (c_mi: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) A2)) (wcel C B2) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) A2)) (wcel D B2) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt x3 A2 C) $ >
  $ wceq H (cmpt x3 A2 D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt x3 A2 (co C D c_mi)) cgsu) (co (co G F cgsu) (co G H cgsu) c_mi)) $;

--| Group sum of a singleton, deduction form, using bound-variable hypotheses instead of distinct variable conditions. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 19-Dec-2014.) (Revised by Thierry Arnoux, 28-Mar-2018.) (Revised by AV, 11-Dec-2019.)
theorem gsumsnfd {k: setvar} (ph: wff k) (A2 B2 C G: class k) (M: class) (V: class k):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C B2) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wceq (cv k) M)) (wceq A2 C) $ >
  $ wnf k ph $ >
  $ wnfc k C $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt k (csn M) A2) cgsu) C) $;

--| Group sum of a singleton, deduction form. (Contributed by Thierry Arnoux, 30-Jan-2017.) (Proof shortened by AV, 11-Dec-2019.)
theorem gsumsnd {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class k) (C: class) (G: class k) (M: class) (V: class k):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C B2) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wceq (cv k) M)) (wceq A2 C) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt k (csn M) A2) cgsu) C) $;

--| Group sum of a singleton, using bound-variable hypotheses instead of distinct variable conditions. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 19-Dec-2014.) (Revised by Thierry Arnoux, 28-Mar-2018.) (Proof shortened by AV, 11-Dec-2019.)
theorem gsumsnf {k: setvar} (A2: class k) (B2: class) (C: class k) (G M V: class):
  $ wnfc k C $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv k) M) (wceq A2 C) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G cmnd) (wcel M V) (wcel C B2)) (wceq (co G (cmpt k (csn M) A2) cgsu) C) $;

--| Group sum of a singleton. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 19-Dec-2014.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 24-Apr-2016.) (Proof shortened by AV, 11-Dec-2019.)
theorem gsumsn {k: setvar} (A2: class k) (B2 C G M V: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv k) M) (wceq A2 C) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G cmnd) (wcel M V) (wcel C B2)) (wceq (co G (cmpt k (csn M) A2) cgsu) C) $;

--| Group sum of a pair. (Contributed by AV, 6-Dec-2018.) (Proof shortened by AV, 28-Jul-2019.)
theorem gsumpr {k: setvar} (A2: class k) (B2 C D: class) (c_pl: class k) (G M N V W: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv k) M) (wceq A2 C) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv k) N) (wceq A2 D) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel G ccmn) (w3a (wcel M V) (wcel N W) (wne M N)) (wa (wcel C B2) (wcel D B2))) (wceq (co G (cmpt k (cpr M N) A2) cgsu) (co C D c_pl)) $;

--| Append an element to a finite group sum, more general version of ~ gsumunsnd . (Contributed by AV, 7-Oct-2019.)
theorem gsumzunsnd {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (c_pl F: class k) (G M: class) (V X: class k) (Y: class) (Z: class k):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt k (cun A2 (csn M)) X) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv k) A2)) (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn (wcel M A2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wceq (cv k) M)) (wceq X Y) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G F cgsu) (co (co G (cmpt k A2 X) cgsu) Y c_pl)) $;

--| Append an element to a finite group sum, using bound-variable hypotheses instead of distinct variable conditions. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 19-Dec-2014.) (Revised by AV, 11-Dec-2019.)
theorem gsumunsnfd {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (c_pl: class k) (G M: class) (V X Y: class k):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv k) A2)) (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn (wcel M A2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wceq (cv k) M)) (wceq X Y) $ >
  $ wnfc k Y $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt k (cun A2 (csn M)) X) cgsu) (co (co G (cmpt k A2 X) cgsu) Y c_pl)) $;

--| Append an element to a finite group sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 19-Dec-2014.) (Revised by AV, 2-Jan-2019.) (Proof shortened by AV, 11-Dec-2019.)
theorem gsumunsnd {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (c_pl: class k) (G M: class) (V X: class k) (Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv k) A2)) (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn (wcel M A2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wceq (cv k) M)) (wceq X Y) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt k (cun A2 (csn M)) X) cgsu) (co (co G (cmpt k A2 X) cgsu) Y c_pl)) $;

--| Append an element to a finite group sum, using bound-variable hypotheses instead of distinct variable conditions. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 19-Dec-2014.) (Revised by Thierry Arnoux, 28-Mar-2018.) (Proof shortened by AV, 11-Dec-2019.)
theorem gsumunsnf {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (c_pl: class k) (G M V: class) (X Y: class k):
  $ wnfc k Y $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv k) A2)) (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn (wcel M A2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv k) M) (wceq X Y) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt k (cun A2 (csn M)) X) cgsu) (co (co G (cmpt k A2 X) cgsu) Y c_pl)) $;

--| Append an element to a finite group sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 19-Dec-2014.) (Proof shortened by AV, 8-Mar-2019.)
theorem gsumunsn {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (c_pl: class k) (G M: class) (V X: class k) (Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv k) A2)) (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn (wcel M A2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv k) M) (wceq X Y) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt k (cun A2 (csn M)) X) cgsu) (co (co G (cmpt k A2 X) cgsu) Y c_pl)) $;

--| Extract a summand from a finitely supported group sum. (Contributed by AV, 21-Apr-2019.) (Revised by AV, 28-Jul-2019.)
theorem gsumdifsnd {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (c_pl: class k) (G M: class) (W X: class k) (Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cmpt k A2 X) (cfv G c0g) cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv k) A2)) (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y B2) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wceq (cv k) M)) (wceq X Y) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt k A2 X) cgsu) (co (co G (cmpt k (cdif A2 (csn M)) X) cgsu) Y c_pl)) $;

--| Sum of a family that is nonzero at at most one point. (Contributed by Stefan O'Rear, 7-Feb-2015.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 6-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumpt (ph: wff) (A2 B2 F G V X c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (co F c_0 csupp) (csn X)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G F cgsu) (cfv X F)) $;

--| Re-index a finite group sum using a bijection. (Contributed by Thierry Arnoux, 29-Mar-2018.)
theorem gsummptf1o {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class) (B2: class y1) (C: class x3) (D: class) (E: class y1) (F G H c_0: class x3 y1):
  $ wnfc x3 H $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv x3) E) (wceq C H) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss F B2) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) A2)) (wcel C F) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv y1) D)) (wcel E A2) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) A2)) (wreu y1 (wceq (cv x3) E) D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt x3 A2 C) cgsu) (co G (cmpt y1 D H) cgsu)) $;

--| Group sum of a disjoint union, whereas sums are expressed as mappings. (Contributed by Thierry Arnoux, 28-Mar-2018.) (Proof shortened by AV, 11-Dec-2019.)
theorem gsummptun {x3: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class) (D c_pl W: class x3):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv W cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv W cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel W ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cun A2 C) cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin A2 C) c0) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) (cun A2 C))) (wcel D B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co W (cmpt x3 (cun A2 C) D) cgsu) (co (co W (cmpt x3 A2 D) cgsu) (co W (cmpt x3 C D) cgsu) c_pl)) $;

--| If only one summand in a finite group sum is not zero, the whole sum equals this summand. More general version of ~ gsummptif1n0 . (Contributed by AV, 11-Oct-2019.)
theorem gsummpt1n0 {n: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 F: class n) (G I: class) (W: class n) (X c_0: class):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X I) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt n I (cif (wceq (cv n) X) A2 c_0)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral n (wcel A2 (cfv G cbs)) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G F cgsu) (csb n X A2)) $;

--| If only one summand in a finite group sum is not zero, the whole sum equals this summand. (Contributed by AV, 17-Feb-2019.) (Proof shortened by AV, 11-Oct-2019.)
theorem gsummptif1n0 {n: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class) (F: class n) (G I: class) (W: class n) (X c_0: class):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X I) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt n I (cif (wceq (cv n) X) A2 c_0)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 (cfv G cbs)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G F cgsu) A2) $;

--| Closure of a finite group sum over a finite set as map. (Contributed by AV, 29-Dec-2018.)
theorem gsummptcl {i: setvar} (ph: wff i) (B2: class) (G: class i) (N: class) (X: class i):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral i (wcel X B2) N) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co G (cmpt i N X) cgsu) B2) $;

--| Re-index a finite group sum as map, using a bijection. (Contributed by by AV, 23-Jul-2019.)
theorem gsummptfif1o {i: setvar} (ph: wff i) (B2: class) (C F G H: class i) (N: class) (X: class i):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral i (wcel X B2) N) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt i N X) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf1o C N H) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G F cgsu) (co G (ccom F H) cgsu)) $;

--| Closure of a finite group sum over a finite set of sequential integers as map. (Contributed by AV, 14-Dec-2018.)
theorem gsummptfzcl {i: setvar} (ph: wff i) (B2: class) (G: class i) (I: class) (M N X: class i):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cmnd) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N (cfv M cuz)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq I (co M N cfz)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral i (wcel X B2) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co G (cmpt i I X) cgsu) B2) $;

--| Lemma 1 for ~ gsum2d . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-Dec-2014.) (Revised by AV, 8-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsum2dlem1 {j k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 D F G: class) (V W: class j k) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wrel A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (cdm A2) D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co G (cmpt k (cima A2 (csn (cv j))) (co (cv j) (cv k) F)) cgsu) B2) $;

--| Lemma for ~ gsum2d . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-Dec-2014.) (Revised by AV, 8-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsum2dlem2 {j k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 D F G: class) (V W: class j k) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wrel A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (cdm A2) D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cres F (cres A2 (cdm (co F c_0 csupp)))) cgsu) (co G (cmpt j (cdm (co F c_0 csupp)) (co G (cmpt k (cima A2 (csn (cv j))) (co (cv j) (cv k) F)) cgsu)) cgsu)) $;

--| Write a sum over a two-dimensional region as a double sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-Dec-2014.) (Revised by AV, 8-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsum2d {j k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 D F G: class) (V W: class j k) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wrel A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (cdm A2) D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G F cgsu) (co G (cmpt j D (co G (cmpt k (cima A2 (csn (cv j))) (co (cv j) (cv k) F)) cgsu)) cgsu)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ gsum2d2 : show the function is finitely supported. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-Dec-2014.) (Revised by AV, 9-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsum2d2lem {j k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (C: class j) (U G: class) (V: class k) (W X: class j k) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv j) A2)) (wcel C W) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wcel (cv j) A2) (wcel (cv k) C))) (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cfn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wa (wcel (cv j) A2) (wcel (cv k) C)) (wn (wbr (cv j) (cv k) U)))) (wceq X c_0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cmpo j k A2 C X) c_0 cfsupp) $;

--| Write a group sum over a two-dimensional region as a double sum. Note that ` C ( j ) ` is a function of ` j ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-Dec-2014.)
theorem gsum2d2 {j k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (C: class j) (U G: class) (V: class k) (W X: class j k) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv j) A2)) (wcel C W) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wcel (cv j) A2) (wcel (cv k) C))) (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cfn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wa (wcel (cv j) A2) (wcel (cv k) C)) (wn (wbr (cv j) (cv k) U)))) (wceq X c_0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpo j k A2 C X) cgsu) (co G (cmpt j A2 (co G (cmpt k C X) cgsu)) cgsu)) $;

--| Two-dimensional commutation of a group sum. Note that while ` A ` and ` D ` are constants w.r.t. ` j , k ` , ` C ( j ) ` and ` E ( k ) ` are not. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-Dec-2014.)
theorem gsumcom2 {j k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (C: class j) (D U: class) (E: class k) (G: class) (V: class k) (W X Y: class j k) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv j) A2)) (wcel C W) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wcel (cv j) A2) (wcel (cv k) C))) (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cfn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wa (wcel (cv j) A2) (wcel (cv k) C)) (wn (wbr (cv j) (cv k) U)))) (wceq X c_0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D Y) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wa (wcel (cv j) A2) (wcel (cv k) C)) (wa (wcel (cv k) D) (wcel (cv j) E))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpo j k A2 C X) cgsu) (co G (cmpo k j D E X) cgsu)) $;

--| Write a group sum over a cartesian product as a double sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-Dec-2014.) (Revised by AV, 9-Jun-2019.)
theorem gsumxp {j k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C F G: class) (V: class k) (W: class j k) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf (cxp A2 C) B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G F cgsu) (co G (cmpt j A2 (co G (cmpt k C (co (cv j) (cv k) F)) cgsu)) cgsu)) $;

--| Commute the arguments of a double sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-Dec-2014.)
theorem gsumcom {j k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C U G: class) (V: class k) (W X: class j k) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C W) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wcel (cv j) A2) (wcel (cv k) C))) (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cfn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wa (wcel (cv j) A2) (wcel (cv k) C)) (wn (wbr (cv j) (cv k) U)))) (wceq X c_0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpo j k A2 C X) cgsu) (co G (cmpo k j C A2 X) cgsu)) $;

--| A commutative law for finitely supported iterated sums. (Contributed by Stefan O'Rear, 2-Nov-2015.)
theorem gsumcom3 {j k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C U G: class) (V: class k) (W: class j) (X: class j k) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C W) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wcel (cv j) A2) (wcel (cv k) C))) (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U cfn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wa (wcel (cv j) A2) (wcel (cv k) C)) (wn (wbr (cv j) (cv k) U)))) (wceq X c_0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt j A2 (co G (cmpt k C X) cgsu)) cgsu) (co G (cmpt k C (co G (cmpt j A2 X) cgsu)) cgsu)) $;

--| A commutative law for finite iterated sums. (Contributed by Stefan O'Rear, 5-Sep-2015.)
theorem gsumcom3fi {j k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C G: class) (X: class j k):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cfn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wcel (cv j) A2) (wcel (cv k) C))) (wcel X B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt j A2 (co G (cmpt k C X) cgsu)) cgsu) (co G (cmpt k C (co G (cmpt j A2 X) cgsu)) cgsu)) $;

--| Write a group sum over a cartesian product as a double sum in two ways. This corresponds to the first equation in [Lang] p. 6. (Contributed by AV, 27-Dec-2023.)
theorem gsumxp2 {j k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C F G: class) (V: class k) (W: class j) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf (cxp A2 C) B2 F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt k C (co G (cmpt j A2 (co (cv j) (cv k) F)) cgsu)) cgsu) (co G (cmpt j A2 (co G (cmpt k C (co (cv j) (cv k) F)) cgsu)) cgsu)) $;

--| Finite commutative sums in a product structure are taken componentwise. (Contributed by Stefan O'Rear, 1-Feb-2015.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 3-Jul-2015.) (Revised by AV, 9-Jun-2019.)
theorem prdsgsum {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2 R S U: class x3 y1) (I J: class) (V W X: class x3 y1) (Y: class) (c_0: class x3 y1):
  $ wceq Y (co S (cmpt x3 I R) cprds) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv R cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv Y c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel J W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S X) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) I)) (wcel R ccmn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wcel (cv x3) I) (wcel (cv y1) J))) (wcel U B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cmpt y1 J (cmpt x3 I U)) c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co Y (cmpt y1 J (cmpt x3 I U)) cgsu) (cmpt x3 I (co R (cmpt y1 J U) cgsu))) $;

--| Finite commutative sums in a power structure are taken componentwise. (Contributed by Stefan O'Rear, 1-Feb-2015.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 3-Jul-2015.) (Revised by AV, 9-Jun-2019.)
theorem pwsgsum {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2 R: class) (U: class x3 y1) (I J: class) (V W: class x3 y1) (Y c_0: class):
  $ wceq Y (co R I cpws) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv R cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv Y c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel J W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel R ccmn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wcel (cv x3) I) (wcel (cv y1) J))) (wcel U B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cmpt y1 J (cmpt x3 I U)) c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co Y (cmpt y1 J (cmpt x3 I U)) cgsu) (cmpt x3 I (co R (cmpt y1 J U) cgsu))) $;

--| Replacing a finitely supported function over the nonnegative integers by a function over a finite set of sequential integers in a finite group sum. (Contributed by AV, 9-Oct-2019.)
theorem fsfnn0gsumfsffz {x3: setvar} (ph: wff x3) (B2: class x3) (S F: class) (G H: class x3) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co B2 cn0 cmap)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S cn0) $ >
  $ wceq H (cres F (co cc0 S cfz)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wral x3 (wi (wbr S (cv x3) clt) (wceq (cfv (cv x3) F) c_0)) cn0) (wceq (co G F cgsu) (co G H cgsu))) $;

--| Replacing a finitely supported function over the nonnegative integers by a function over a finite set of sequential integers in a finite group sum. (Contributed by AV, 9-Oct-2019.)
theorem nn0gsumfz {x3 f2 s1: setvar} (ph: wff x3) (B2: class x3 s1) (F: class) (G: class x3 s1) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co B2 cn0 cmap)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wrex s1 (wrex f2 (w3a (wceq (cv f2) (cres F (co cc0 (cv s1) cfz))) (wral x3 (wi (wbr (cv s1) (cv x3) clt) (wceq (cfv (cv x3) F) c_0)) cn0) (wceq (co G F cgsu) (co G (cv f2) cgsu))) (co B2 (co cc0 (cv s1) cfz) cmap)) cn0) $;

--| Replacing a finitely supported function over the nonnegative integers by a function over a finite set of sequential integers in a finite group sum. (Contributed by AV, 9-Oct-2019.)
theorem nn0gsumfz0 {f2 s1: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2: class s1) (F: class) (G: class s1) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co B2 cn0 cmap)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wrex s1 (wrex f2 (wceq (co G F cgsu) (co G (cv f2) cgsu)) (co B2 (co cc0 (cv s1) cfz) cmap)) cn0) $;

--| A final group sum over a function over the nonnegative integers (given as mapping) is equal to a final group sum over a finite interval of nonnegative integers. (Contributed by AV, 10-Oct-2019.) (Revised by AV, 3-Jul-2022.)
theorem gsummptnn0fz {k: setvar} (ph: wff k) (B2: class) (C: class k) (S: class) (G: class k) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral k (wcel C B2) cn0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S cn0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral k (wi (wbr S (cv k) clt) (wceq C c_0)) cn0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt k cn0 C) cgsu) (co G (cmpt k (co cc0 S cfz) C) cgsu)) $;

--| A final group sum over a function over the nonnegative integers (given as mapping to its function values) is equal to a final group sum over a finite interval of nonnegative integers. (Contributed by AV, 10-Oct-2019.)
theorem gsummptnn0fzfv {x3 k: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2: class x3) (S F: class) (G: class x3 k) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G ccmn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F (co B2 cn0 cmap)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S cn0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral x3 (wi (wbr S (cv x3) clt) (wceq (cfv (cv x3) F) c_0)) cn0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt k cn0 (cfv (cv k) F)) cgsu) (co G (cmpt k (co cc0 S cfz) (cfv (cv k) F)) cgsu)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ telgsumfzs (induction step). (Contributed by AV, 23-Nov-2019.)
theorem telgsumfzslem {i k: setvar} (ph: wff k) (y1: setvar) (B2: class) (C G: class k) (M: class) (c_mi: class k):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel (cv y1) (cfv M cuz)) (wa ph (wral k (wcel C B2) (co M (co (co (cv y1) c1 caddc) c1 caddc) cfz)))) (wi (wceq (co G (cmpt i (co M (cv y1) cfz) (co (csb k (cv i) C) (csb k (co (cv i) c1 caddc) C) c_mi)) cgsu) (co (csb k M C) (csb k (co (cv y1) c1 caddc) C) c_mi)) (wceq (co G (cmpt i (co M (co (cv y1) c1 caddc) cfz) (co (csb k (cv i) C) (csb k (co (cv i) c1 caddc) C) c_mi)) cgsu) (co (csb k M C) (csb k (co (co (cv y1) c1 caddc) c1 caddc) C) c_mi))) $;

--| Telescoping group sum ranging over a finite set of sequential integers, using explicit substitution. (Contributed by AV, 23-Nov-2019.)
theorem telgsumfzs {i k: setvar} (ph: wff k) (B2: class) (C G: class k) (M: class) (c_mi: class k) (N: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N (cfv M cuz)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral k (wcel C B2) (co M (co N c1 caddc) cfz)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt i (co M N cfz) (co (csb k (cv i) C) (csb k (co (cv i) c1 caddc) C) c_mi)) cgsu) (co (csb k M C) (csb k (co N c1 caddc) C) c_mi)) $;

--| Telescoping group sum ranging over a finite set of sequential integers, using implicit substitution, analogous to ~ telfsum . (Contributed by AV, 23-Nov-2019.)
theorem telgsumfz {i k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class k) (B2: class) (C D E: class i) (G: class k) (L: class i) (M: class) (c_mi: class k) (N: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N (cfv M cuz)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral k (wcel A2 B2) (co M (co N c1 caddc) cfz)) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv k) (cv i)) (wceq A2 L) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv k) (co (cv i) c1 caddc)) (wceq A2 C) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv k) M) (wceq A2 D) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv k) (co N c1 caddc)) (wceq A2 E) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt i (co M N cfz) (co L C c_mi)) cgsu) (co D E c_mi)) $;

--| Telescoping finite group sum ranging over nonnegative integers, using explicit substitution. (Contributed by AV, 24-Oct-2019.) (Proof shortened by AV, 25-Nov-2019.)
theorem telgsumfz0s {i k: setvar} (ph: wff k) (B2: class) (C: class k) (S: class) (G c_mi: class k):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S cn0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral k (wcel C B2) (co cc0 (co S c1 caddc) cfz)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt i (co cc0 S cfz) (co (csb k (cv i) C) (csb k (co (cv i) c1 caddc) C) c_mi)) cgsu) (co (csb k cc0 C) (csb k (co S c1 caddc) C) c_mi)) $;

--| Telescoping finite group sum ranging over nonnegative integers, using implicit substitution, analogous to ~ telfsum . (Contributed by AV, 23-Nov-2019.)
theorem telgsumfz0 {i k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class k) (B2 C D: class i) (S: class) (E: class i) (G: class k) (K: class) (c_mi: class k):
  $ wceq K (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S cn0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral k (wcel A2 K) (co cc0 (co S c1 caddc) cfz)) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv k) (cv i)) (wceq A2 B2) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv k) (co (cv i) c1 caddc)) (wceq A2 C) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv k) cc0) (wceq A2 D) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv k) (co S c1 caddc)) (wceq A2 E) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt i (co cc0 S cfz) (co B2 C c_mi)) cgsu) (co D E c_mi)) $;

--| Telescoping finitely supported group sum ranging over nonnegative integers, using explicit substitution. (Contributed by AV, 24-Oct-2019.)
theorem telgsums {i k: setvar} (ph: wff k) (B2: class) (C: class k) (S: class) (G c_mi: class k) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral k (wcel C B2) cn0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S cn0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral k (wi (wbr S (cv k) clt) (wceq C c_0)) cn0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt i cn0 (co (csb k (cv i) C) (csb k (co (cv i) c1 caddc) C) c_mi)) cgsu) (csb k cc0 C)) $;

--| Telescoping finitely supported group sum ranging over nonnegative integers, using implicit substitution. (Contributed by AV, 31-Dec-2019.)
theorem telgsum {i k: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class k) (B2: class) (C D: class i) (S: class) (E: class i) (G c_mi: class k) (c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral k (wcel A2 B2) cn0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S cn0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral k (wi (wbr S (cv k) clt) (wceq A2 c_0)) cn0) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv k) (cv i)) (wceq A2 C) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv k) (co (cv i) c1 caddc)) (wceq A2 D) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv k) cc0) (wceq A2 E) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cmpt i cn0 (co C D c_mi)) cgsu) E) $;

--| Internal direct product of a family of subgroups.
term cdprd: class;

--| Projection operator for a direct product.
term cdpj: class;

--| Define the internal direct product of a family of subgroups. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 11-Jul-2019.)
axiom df_dprd {x3 y1 f2 g2 h s1: setvar}:
  $ wceq cdprd (cmpo g2 s1 cgrp (cab h (wa (wf (cdm (cv h)) (cfv (cv g2) csubg) (cv h)) (wral x3 (wa (wral y1 (wss (cfv (cv x3) (cv h)) (cfv (cfv (cv y1) (cv h)) (cfv (cv g2) ccntz))) (cdif (cdm (cv h)) (csn (cv x3)))) (wceq (cin (cfv (cv x3) (cv h)) (cfv (cuni (cima (cv h) (cdif (cdm (cv h)) (csn (cv x3))))) (cfv (cfv (cv g2) csubg) cmrc))) (csn (cfv (cv g2) c0g)))) (cdm (cv h))))) (crn (cmpt f2 (crab h (wbr (cv h) (cfv (cv g2) c0g) cfsupp) (cixp x3 (cdm (cv s1)) (cfv (cv x3) (cv s1)))) (co (cv g2) (cv f2) cgsu)))) $;

--| Define the projection operator for a direct product. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
axiom df_dpj {g2 i s1: setvar}:
  $ wceq cdpj (cmpo g2 s1 cgrp (cima (cdm cdprd) (csn (cv g2))) (cmpt i (cdm (cv s1)) (co (cfv (cv i) (cv s1)) (co (cv g2) (cres (cv s1) (cdif (cdm (cv s1)) (csn (cv i)))) cdprd) (cfv (cv g2) cpj1)))) $;

--| The domain of the internal direct product operation is a relation. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Proof shortened by AV, 11-Jul-2019.)
theorem reldmdprd:
  $ wrel (cdm cdprd) $;

--| The domain of definition of the internal direct product, which states that ` S ` is a family of subgroups that mutually commute and have trivial intersections. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Proof shortened by AV, 11-Jul-2019.)
theorem dmdprd {x3 y1: setvar} (S G I: class) (K: class x3 y1) (V: class) (c_0 Z: class x3 y1):
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv (cfv G csubg) cmrc) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel I V) (wceq (cdm S) I)) (wb (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) (w3a (wcel G cgrp) (wf I (cfv G csubg) S) (wral x3 (wa (wral y1 (wss (cfv (cv x3) S) (cfv (cfv (cv y1) S) Z)) (cdif I (csn (cv x3)))) (wceq (cin (cfv (cv x3) S) (cfv (cuni (cima S (cdif I (csn (cv x3))))) K)) (csn c_0))) I))) $;

--| Show that a given family is a direct product decomposition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 11-Jul-2019.)
theorem dmdprdd {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (S G I: class) (K: class x3 y1) (V: class) (c_0 Z: class x3 y1):
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv (cfv G csubg) cmrc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cgrp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf I (cfv G csubg) S) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (w3a (wcel (cv x3) I) (wcel (cv y1) I) (wne (cv x3) (cv y1)))) (wss (cfv (cv x3) S) (cfv (cfv (cv y1) S) Z)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) I)) (wss (cin (cfv (cv x3) S) (cfv (cuni (cima S (cdif I (csn (cv x3))))) K)) (csn c_0)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $;

--| A family of subgroups indexed by a proper class cannot be a family of subgroups for an internal direct product. (Contributed by AV, 13-Jul-2019.)
theorem dprddomprc (S G: class):
  $ wi (wnel (cdm S) cvv) (wn (wbr G S (cdm cdprd))) $;

--| If a family of subgroups is a family of subgroups for an internal direct product, then it is indexed by a set. (Contributed by AV, 13-Jul-2019.)
theorem dprddomcld (ph: wff) (S G I: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel I cvv) $;

--| The internal direct product of a family of subgroups indexed by a proper class is empty. (Contributed by AV, 13-Jul-2019.)
theorem dprdval0prc (S G: class):
  $ wi (wnel (cdm S) cvv) (wceq (co G S cdprd) c0) $;

--| The value of the internal direct product operation, which is a function mapping the (infinite, but finitely supported) cartesian product of subgroups (which mutually commute and have trivial intersections) to its (group) sum . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 11-Jul-2019.)
theorem dprdval {f2 h i: setvar} (S G I: class) (W c_0: class f2 h i):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) (wceq (cdm S) I)) (wceq (co G S cdprd) (crn (cmpt f2 W (co G (cv f2) cgsu)))) $;

--| A class ` A ` is an internal direct product iff it is the (group) sum of an infinite, but finitely supported cartesian product of subgroups (which mutually commute and have trivial intersections). (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 11-Jul-2019.)
theorem eldprd {f2 h i: setvar} (A2: class h i) (S G I: class) (W c_0: class f2 h i):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cdm S) I) (wb (wcel A2 (co G S cdprd)) (wa (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) (wrex f2 (wceq A2 (co G (cv f2) cgsu)) W))) $;

--| Reverse closure for the internal direct product. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdgrp (S G: class):
  $ wi (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) (wcel G cgrp) $;

--| The function ` S ` is a family of subgroups. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdf (S G: class):
  $ wi (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) (wf (cdm S) (cfv G csubg) S) $;

--| The function ` S ` is a family of subgroups. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdf2 (ph: wff) (S G I: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf I (cfv G csubg) S) $;

--| The function ` S ` is a family having pairwise commuting values. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdcntz (ph: wff) (S G I X Y Z: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne X Y) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (cfv X S) (cfv (cfv Y S) Z)) $;

--| The function ` S ` is a family having trivial intersections. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprddisj (ph: wff) (S G I K X c_0: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X I) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv (cfv G csubg) cmrc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin (cfv X S) (cfv (cuni (cima S (cdif I (csn X)))) K)) (csn c_0)) $;

--| The property of being a finitely supported function in the family ` S ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 11-Jul-2019.)
theorem dprdw {x3 h i: setvar} (ph: wff h i) (S: class) (F: class i) (G: class h i) (I: class) (W: class x3 h i) (c_0: class x3 i):
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wcel F W) (w3a (wfn F I) (wral x3 (wcel (cfv (cv x3) F) (cfv (cv x3) S)) I) (wbr F c_0 cfsupp))) $;

--| A mapping being a finitely supported function in the family ` S ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 11-Jul-2019.) (Proof shortened by OpenAI, 30-Mar-2020.)
theorem dprdwd {x3 h i: setvar} (ph: wff h i) (A2: class x3 i) (S: class) (G: class h i) (I: class) (W: class x3 h i) (c_0: class x3 i):
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) I)) (wcel A2 (cfv (cv x3) S)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cmpt x3 I A2) c_0 cfsupp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 I A2) W) $;

--| A finitely supported function in ` S ` is a function into the base. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 11-Jul-2019.)
theorem dprdff {h i: setvar} (ph: wff h i) (B2: class h i) (S: class) (F: class i) (G: class h i) (I: class) (W: class h i) (c_0: class i):
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F W) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf I B2 F) $;

--| A finitely supported function in ` S ` has its ` X ` -th element in ` S ( X ) ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 11-Jul-2019.)
theorem dprdfcl {h i: setvar} (ph: wff h i) (S: class) (F: class i) (G: class h i) (I: class) (W X: class h i) (c_0: class i):
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F W) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel X I)) (wcel (cfv X F) (cfv X S)) $;

--| A finitely supported function in ` S ` is a finitely supported function. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 11-Jul-2019.)
theorem dprdffsupp {h i: setvar} (ph: wff h i) (S: class) (F: class i) (G: class h i) (I: class) (W: class h i) (c_0: class i):
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F c_0 cfsupp) $;

--| A function on the elements of an internal direct product has pairwise commuting values. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 11-Jul-2019.)
theorem dprdfcntz {h i: setvar} (ph: wff h i) (S: class) (F: class i) (G: class h i) (I: class) (W: class h i) (c_0: class i) (Z: class h i):
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F W) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn F) (cfv (crn F) Z)) $;

--| The internal direct product of a family of subgroups is a subset of the base. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdssv (B2 S G: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wss (co G S cdprd) B2 $;

--| A function mapping all but one arguments to zero sums to the value of this argument in a direct product. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 14-Jul-2019.)
theorem dprdfid {h i n: setvar} (ph: wff h i) (A2: class i) (S: class) (F: class i n) (G I: class) (W: class h i n) (X c_0: class i):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 (cfv X S)) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt n I (cif (wceq (cv n) X) A2 c_0)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel F W) (wceq (co G F cgsu) A2)) $;

--| The domain of definition of the internal direct product, which states that ` S ` is a family of subgroups that mutually commute and have trivial intersections. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 14-Jul-2019.)
theorem eldprdi {h i: setvar} (ph: wff h i) (S: class) (F: class i) (G I: class) (W: class h i) (c_0: class i):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co G F cgsu) (co G S cdprd)) $;

--| Take the inverse of a group sum over a family of elements of disjoint subgroups. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 14-Jul-2019.)
theorem dprdfinv {h i: setvar} (ph: wff h i) (S: class) (F: class i) (G I: class) (N: class i) (W: class h i) (c_0: class i):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F W) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv G cminusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel (ccom N F) W) (wceq (co G (ccom N F) cgsu) (cfv (co G F cgsu) N))) $;

--| Take the sum of group sums over two families of elements of disjoint subgroups. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 14-Jul-2019.)
theorem dprdfadd {h i: setvar} (ph: wff h i) (c_pl: class i) (S: class) (F: class i) (G: class) (H: class i) (I: class) (W: class h i) (c_0: class i):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H W) $ >
  $ wceq c_pl (cfv G cplusg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel (co F H (cof c_pl)) W) (wceq (co G (co F H (cof c_pl)) cgsu) (co (co G F cgsu) (co G H cgsu) c_pl))) $;

--| Take the difference of group sums over two families of elements of disjoint subgroups. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 14-Jul-2019.)
theorem dprdfsub {h i: setvar} (ph: wff h i) (S: class) (F: class i) (G: class) (H: class i) (I: class) (c_mi W: class h i) (c_0: class i):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H W) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv G csg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel (co F H (cof c_mi)) W) (wceq (co G (co F H (cof c_mi)) cgsu) (co (co G F cgsu) (co G H cgsu) c_mi))) $;

--| The zero function is the only function that sums to zero in a direct product. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 14-Jul-2019.)
theorem dprdfeq0 {x3 h i: setvar} (ph: wff h i) (S: class) (F: class i) (G I: class) (W: class x3 h i) (c_0: class i):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (co G F cgsu) c_0) (wceq F (cmpt x3 I c_0))) $;

--| Two group sums over a direct product that give the same value are equal as functions. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 14-Jul-2019.)
theorem dprdf11 {h i: setvar} (ph: wff h i) (S: class) (F: class i) (G: class) (H: class i) (I: class) (W: class h i) (c_0: class i):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel H W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (co G F cgsu) (co G H cgsu)) (wceq F H)) $;

--| The internal direct product of a family of subgroups is a subgroup. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdsubg (S G: class):
  $ wi (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) (wcel (co G S cdprd) (cfv G csubg)) $;

--| Each factor is a subset of the internal direct product. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdub (ph: wff) (S G I X: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (cfv X S) (co G S cdprd)) $;

--| The direct product is smaller than any subgroup which contains the factors. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdlub {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (S T G I: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel T (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv k) I)) (wss (cfv (cv k) S) T) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (co G S cdprd) T) $;

--| The direct product is the span of the union of the factors. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdspan (S G K: class):
  $ wceq K (cfv (cfv G csubg) cmrc) $ >
  $ wi (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) (wceq (co G S cdprd) (cfv (cuni (crn S)) K)) $;

--| Restriction of a direct product (dropping factors). (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdres (ph: wff) (A2 S G I: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss A2 I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wbr G (cres S A2) (cdm cdprd)) (wss (co G (cres S A2) cdprd) (co G S cdprd))) $;

--| Create a direct product by finding subgroups inside each factor of another direct product. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdss {k: setvar} (ph: wff) (S T G I: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G T (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm T) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf I (cfv G csubg) S) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv k) I)) (wss (cfv (cv k) S) (cfv (cv k) T)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) (wss (co G S cdprd) (co G T cdprd))) $;

--| A family consisting entirely of trivial groups is an internal direct product, the product of which is the trivial subgroup. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdz {x3: setvar} (G I V c_0: class):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel G cgrp) (wcel I V)) (wa (wbr G (cmpt x3 I (csn c_0)) (cdm cdprd)) (wceq (co G (cmpt x3 I (csn c_0)) cdprd) (csn c_0))) $;

--| The empty family is an internal direct product, the product of which is the trivial subgroup. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprd0 (G c_0: class):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi (wcel G cgrp) (wa (wbr G c0 (cdm cdprd)) (wceq (co G c0 cdprd) (csn c_0))) $;

--| Rearrange the index set of a direct product family. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdf1o (ph: wff) (S F G I J: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf1o J I F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wbr G (ccom S F) (cdm cdprd)) (wceq (co G (ccom S F) cdprd) (co G S cdprd))) $;

--| Rearrange the index set of a direct product family. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdf1 (ph: wff) (S F G I J: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf1 J I F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wbr G (ccom S F) (cdm cdprd)) (wss (co G (ccom S F) cdprd) (co G S cdprd))) $;

--| A direct product in a subgroup. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-Apr-2016.)
theorem subgdmdprd (A2 S G H: class):
  $ wceq H (co G A2 cress) $ >
  $ wi (wcel A2 (cfv G csubg)) (wb (wbr H S (cdm cdprd)) (wa (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) (wss (crn S) (cpw A2)))) $;

--| A direct product in a subgroup. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-Apr-2016.)
theorem subgdprd (ph: wff) (A2 S G H: class):
  $ wceq H (co G A2 cress) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crn S) (cpw A2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co H S cdprd) (co G S cdprd)) $;

--| A singleton family is an internal direct product, the product of which is the given subgroup. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdsn (A2 S G V: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 V) (wcel S (cfv G csubg))) (wa (wbr G (csn (cop A2 S)) (cdm cdprd)) (wceq (co G (csn (cop A2 S)) cdprd) S)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ dmdprdsplit . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 14-Jul-2019.)
theorem dmdprdsplitlem {h i: setvar} (ph: wff h i) (A2 S: class) (F: class i) (G I: class) (W X: class h i) (c_0: class i):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss A2 I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co G F cgsu) (co G (cres S A2) cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel X (cdif I A2))) (wceq (cfv X F) c_0) $;

--| The function ` S ` is a family of subgroups. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdcntz2 (ph: wff) (C D S G I Z: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss C I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss D I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin C D) c0) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (co G (cres S C) cdprd) (cfv (co G (cres S D) cdprd) Z)) $;

--| The function ` S ` is a family of subgroups. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 14-Jul-2019.)
theorem dprddisj2 (ph: wff) (C D S G I c_0: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss C I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss D I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin C D) c0) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin (co G (cres S C) cdprd) (co G (cres S D) cdprd)) (csn c_0)) $;

--| The direct product of a collection of direct products. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprd2dlem2 {i j: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 S G: class) (I K: class j) (X: class):
  $ wi ph (wrel A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 (cfv G csubg) S) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (cdm A2) I) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv i) I)) (wbr G (cmpt j (cima A2 (csn (cv i))) (co (cv i) (cv j) S)) (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G (cmpt i I (co G (cmpt j (cima A2 (csn (cv i))) (co (cv i) (cv j) S)) cdprd)) (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv (cfv G csubg) cmrc) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel X A2)) (wss (cfv X S) (co G (cmpt j (cima A2 (csn (cfv X c1st))) (co (cfv X c1st) (cv j) S)) cdprd)) $;

--| The direct product of a collection of direct products. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprd2dlem1 {i j: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class) (C: class j) (S G: class) (I K: class j):
  $ wi ph (wrel A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 (cfv G csubg) S) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (cdm A2) I) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv i) I)) (wbr G (cmpt j (cima A2 (csn (cv i))) (co (cv i) (cv j) S)) (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G (cmpt i I (co G (cmpt j (cima A2 (csn (cv i))) (co (cv i) (cv j) S)) cdprd)) (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv (cfv G csubg) cmrc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss C I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv (cuni (cima S (cres A2 C))) K) (co G (cmpt i C (co G (cmpt j (cima A2 (csn (cv i))) (co (cv i) (cv j) S)) cdprd)) cdprd)) $;

--| The direct product of a collection of direct products. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprd2da {i j: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 S G: class) (I K: class j):
  $ wi ph (wrel A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 (cfv G csubg) S) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (cdm A2) I) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv i) I)) (wbr G (cmpt j (cima A2 (csn (cv i))) (co (cv i) (cv j) S)) (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G (cmpt i I (co G (cmpt j (cima A2 (csn (cv i))) (co (cv i) (cv j) S)) cdprd)) (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv (cfv G csubg) cmrc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $;

--| The direct product of a collection of direct products. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprd2db {i j: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 S G: class) (I K: class j):
  $ wi ph (wrel A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf A2 (cfv G csubg) S) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (cdm A2) I) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv i) I)) (wbr G (cmpt j (cima A2 (csn (cv i))) (co (cv i) (cv j) S)) (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G (cmpt i I (co G (cmpt j (cima A2 (csn (cv i))) (co (cv i) (cv j) S)) cdprd)) (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv (cfv G csubg) cmrc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G S cdprd) (co G (cmpt i I (co G (cmpt j (cima A2 (csn (cv i))) (co (cv i) (cv j) S)) cdprd)) cdprd)) $;

--| The direct product of a collection of direct products. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprd2d2 {i j: setvar} (ph: wff) (S: class i j) (G I: class) (J: class i):
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wcel (cv i) I) (wcel (cv j) J))) (wcel S (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv i) I)) (wbr G (cmpt j J S) (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G (cmpt i I (co G (cmpt j J S) cdprd)) (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wbr G (cmpo i j I J S) (cdm cdprd)) (wceq (co G (cmpo i j I J S) cdprd) (co G (cmpt i I (co G (cmpt j J S) cdprd)) cdprd))) $;

--| Lemma for ~ dmdprdsplit . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dmdprdsplit2lem (ph: wff) (C D S G I K X Y c_0 Z: class):
  $ wi ph (wf I (cfv G csubg) S) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin C D) c0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq I (cun C D)) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G (cres S C) (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G (cres S D) (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (co G (cres S C) cdprd) (cfv (co G (cres S D) cdprd) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin (co G (cres S C) cdprd) (co G (cres S D) cdprd)) (csn c_0)) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv (cfv G csubg) cmrc) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel X C)) (wa (wi (wcel Y I) (wi (wne X Y) (wss (cfv X S) (cfv (cfv Y S) Z)))) (wss (cin (cfv X S) (cfv (cuni (cima S (cdif I (csn X)))) K)) (csn c_0))) $;

--| The direct product splits into the direct product of any partition of the index set. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dmdprdsplit2 (ph: wff) (C D S G I c_0 Z: class):
  $ wi ph (wf I (cfv G csubg) S) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin C D) c0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq I (cun C D)) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G (cres S C) (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G (cres S D) (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (co G (cres S C) cdprd) (cfv (co G (cres S D) cdprd) Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin (co G (cres S C) cdprd) (co G (cres S D) cdprd)) (csn c_0)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $;

--| The direct product splits into the direct product of any partition of the index set. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dmdprdsplit (ph: wff) (C D S G I c_0 Z: class):
  $ wi ph (wf I (cfv G csubg) S) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin C D) c0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq I (cun C D)) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) (w3a (wa (wbr G (cres S C) (cdm cdprd)) (wbr G (cres S D) (cdm cdprd))) (wss (co G (cres S C) cdprd) (cfv (co G (cres S D) cdprd) Z)) (wceq (cin (co G (cres S C) cdprd) (co G (cres S D) cdprd)) (csn c_0)))) $;

--| The direct product is the binary subgroup product ("sum") of the direct products of the partition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdsplit (ph: wff) (C D c_po S G I: class):
  $ wi ph (wf I (cfv G csubg) S) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin C D) c0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq I (cun C D)) $ >
  $ wceq c_po (cfv G clsm) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G S cdprd) (co (co G (cres S C) cdprd) (co G (cres S D) cdprd) c_po)) $;

--| A singleton family is an internal direct product, the product of which is the given subgroup. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Apr-2016.)
theorem dmdprdpr (ph: wff) (S T G c_0 Z: class):
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel T (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr G (cpr (cop c0 S) (cop c1o T)) (cdm cdprd)) (wa (wss S (cfv T Z)) (wceq (cin S T) (csn c_0)))) $;

--| A singleton family is an internal direct product, the product of which is the given subgroup. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dprdpr (ph: wff) (c_po S T G c_0 Z: class):
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel T (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wceq c_po (cfv G clsm) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss S (cfv T Z)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin S T) (csn c_0)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cpr (cop c0 S) (cop c1o T)) cdprd) (co S T c_po)) $;

--| Lemma for theorems about direct product projection. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dpjlem (ph: wff) (S G I X: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G (cres S (csn X)) cdprd) (cfv X S)) $;

--| The two subgroups that appear in ~ dpjval commute. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dpjcntz (ph: wff) (S G I X Z: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X I) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv G ccntz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (cfv X S) (cfv (co G (cres S (cdif I (csn X))) cdprd) Z)) $;

--| The two subgroups that appear in ~ dpjval are disjoint. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dpjdisj (ph: wff) (S G I X c_0: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X I) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin (cfv X S) (co G (cres S (cdif I (csn X))) cdprd)) (csn c_0)) $;

--| The two subgroups that appear in ~ dpjval add to the full direct product. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dpjlsm (ph: wff) (c_po S G I X: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X I) $ >
  $ wceq c_po (cfv G clsm) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G S cdprd) (co (cfv X S) (co G (cres S (cdif I (csn X))) cdprd) c_po)) $;

--| Value of the direct product projection (defined in terms of binary projection). (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dpjfval {i: setvar} (ph: wff) (P Q: class i) (S G I: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wceq P (co G S cdpj) $ >
  $ wceq Q (cfv G cpj1) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq P (cmpt i I (co (cfv (cv i) S) (co G (cres S (cdif I (csn (cv i)))) cdprd) Q))) $;

--| Value of the direct product projection (defined in terms of binary projection). (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dpjval (ph: wff) (P Q S G I X: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wceq P (co G S cdpj) $ >
  $ wceq Q (cfv G cpj1) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv X P) (co (cfv X S) (co G (cres S (cdif I (csn X))) cdprd) Q)) $;

--| The ` X ` -th index projection is a function from the direct product to the ` X ` -th factor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dpjf (ph: wff) (P S G I X: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wceq P (co G S cdpj) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf (co G S cdprd) (cfv X S) (cfv X P)) $;

--| The key property of projections: the sum of all the projections of ` A ` is ` A ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 14-Jul-2019.)
theorem dpjidcl {x3 h i: setvar} (ph: wff h) (A2 P: class i) (S G I: class) (W: class h i) (c_0: class i):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wceq P (co G S cdpj) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 (co G S cdprd)) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel (cmpt x3 I (cfv A2 (cfv (cv x3) P))) W) (wceq A2 (co G (cmpt x3 I (cfv A2 (cfv (cv x3) P))) cgsu))) $;

--| Decompose a group sum into projections. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.) (Revised by AV, 14-Jul-2019.)
theorem dpjeq {x3 h i: setvar} (ph: wff h) (A2: class i) (C: class x3 i) (P: class i) (S G I: class) (W: class h i) (c_0: class i):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wceq P (co G S cdpj) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 (co G S cdprd)) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab h (wbr (cv h) c_0 cfsupp) (cixp i I (cfv (cv i) S))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 I C) W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq A2 (co G (cmpt x3 I C) cgsu)) (wral x3 (wceq (cfv A2 (cfv (cv x3) P)) C) I)) $;

--| The key property of projections: the sum of all the projections of ` A ` is ` A ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dpjid {x3: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 P S G I: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wceq P (co G S cdpj) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 (co G S cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 (co G (cmpt x3 I (cfv A2 (cfv (cv x3) P))) cgsu)) $;

--| The ` X ` -th index projection acts as the identity on elements of the ` X ` -th factor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dpjlid (ph: wff) (A2 P S G I X: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wceq P (co G S cdpj) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 (cfv X S)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv A2 (cfv X P)) A2) $;

--| The ` Y ` -th index projection annihilates elements of other factors. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dpjrid (ph: wff) (A2 P S G I X Y c_0: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wceq P (co G S cdpj) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 (cfv X S)) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne Y X) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv A2 (cfv Y P)) c_0) $;

--| The direct product is the binary subgroup product ("sum") of the direct products of the partition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dpjghm (ph: wff) (P S G I X: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wceq P (co G S cdpj) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cfv X P) (co (co G (co G S cdprd) cress) G cghm)) $;

--| The direct product is the binary subgroup product ("sum") of the direct products of the partition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem dpjghm2 (ph: wff) (P S G I X: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm S) I) $ >
  $ wceq P (co G S cdpj) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X I) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cfv X P) (co (co G (co G S cdprd) cress) (co G (cfv X S) cress) cghm)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ ablfacrp2 . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 19-Apr-2016.)
theorem ablfacrplem {x3: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2 G: class) (K L: class x3) (M N O: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wceq K (crab x3 (wbr (cfv (cv x3) O) M cdvds) B2) $ >
  $ wceq L (crab x3 (wbr (cfv (cv x3) O) N cdvds) B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co M N cgcd) c1) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv B2 chash) (co M N cmul)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (cfv K chash) N cgcd) c1) $;

--| A finite abelian group whose order factors into relatively prime integers, itself "factors" into two subgroups ` K , L ` that have trivial intersection and whose product is the whole group. Lemma 6.1C.2 of [Shapiro], p. 199. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 19-Apr-2016.)
theorem ablfacrp {x3: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2: class) (c_po: class x3) (G: class) (K L: class x3) (M N O c_0: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wceq K (crab x3 (wbr (cfv (cv x3) O) M cdvds) B2) $ >
  $ wceq L (crab x3 (wbr (cfv (cv x3) O) N cdvds) B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co M N cgcd) c1) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv B2 chash) (co M N cmul)) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_po (cfv G clsm) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wceq (cin K L) (csn c_0)) (wceq (co K L c_po) B2)) $;

--| The factors ` K , L ` of ~ ablfacrp have the expected orders (which allows for repeated application to decompose ` G ` into subgroups of prime-power order). Lemma 6.1C.2 of [Shapiro], p. 199. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem ablfacrp2 {x3: setvar} (ph: wff) (B2 G: class) (K L: class x3) (M N O: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wceq K (crab x3 (wbr (cfv (cv x3) O) M cdvds) B2) $ >
  $ wceq L (crab x3 (wbr (cfv (cv x3) O) N cdvds) B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co M N cgcd) c1) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv B2 chash) (co M N cmul)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wceq (cfv K chash) M) (wceq (cfv L chash) N)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ ablfac1b . Satisfy the assumptions of ablfacrp. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem ablfac1lem {x3 p: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 P: class) (S: class x3 p) (G: class) (M N: class x3 p) (O: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wceq S (cmpt p A2 (crab x3 (wbr (cfv (cv x3) O) (co (cv p) (co (cv p) (cfv B2 chash) cpc) cexp) cdvds) B2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss A2 cprime) $ >
  $ wceq M (co P (co P (cfv B2 chash) cpc) cexp) $ >
  $ wceq N (co (cfv B2 chash) M cdiv) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel P A2)) (w3a (wa (wcel M cn) (wcel N cn)) (wceq (co M N cgcd) c1) (wceq (cfv B2 chash) (co M N cmul))) $;

--| The factors of ~ ablfac1b are of prime power order. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 26-Apr-2016.)
theorem ablfac1a {x3 p: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2 P: class) (S: class x3 p) (G O: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wceq S (cmpt p A2 (crab x3 (wbr (cfv (cv x3) O) (co (cv p) (co (cv p) (cfv B2 chash) cpc) cexp) cdvds) B2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss A2 cprime) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel P A2)) (wceq (cfv (cfv P S) chash) (co P (co P (cfv B2 chash) cpc) cexp)) $;

--| Any abelian group is the direct product of factors of prime power order (with the exact order further matching the prime factorization of the group order). (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem ablfac1b {x3 p: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (S: class x3 p) (G O: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wceq S (cmpt p A2 (crab x3 (wbr (cfv (cv x3) O) (co (cv p) (co (cv p) (cfv B2 chash) cpc) cexp) cdvds) B2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss A2 cprime) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr G S (cdm cdprd)) $;

--| The factors of ~ ablfac1b cover the entire group. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem ablfac1c {x3 w p: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class w) (B2: class) (D: class w) (S: class x3 w p) (G O: class w):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wceq S (cmpt p A2 (crab x3 (wbr (cfv (cv x3) O) (co (cv p) (co (cv p) (cfv B2 chash) cpc) cexp) cdvds) B2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss A2 cprime) $ >
  $ wceq D (crab w (wbr (cv w) (cfv B2 chash) cdvds) cprime) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss D A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co G S cdprd) B2) $;

--| Lemma for ~ ablfac1eu . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-Apr-2016.)
theorem ablfac1eulem {x3 w q p: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class w) (B2: class) (C: class x3 w q p) (D P: class w) (S: class x3 w p) (T: class w p) (G O: class w):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wceq S (cmpt p A2 (crab x3 (wbr (cfv (cv x3) O) (co (cv p) (co (cv p) (cfv B2 chash) cpc) cexp) cdvds) B2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss A2 cprime) $ >
  $ wceq D (crab w (wbr (cv w) (cfv B2 chash) cdvds) cprime) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss D A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wbr G T (cdm cdprd)) (wceq (co G T cdprd) B2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm T) A2) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv q) A2)) (wcel C cn0) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv q) A2)) (wceq (cfv (cfv (cv q) T) chash) (co (cv q) C cexp)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel P cprime) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn (wbr P (cfv (co G (cres T (cdif A2 (csn P))) cdprd) chash) cdvds)) $;

--| The factorization of ~ ablfac1b is unique, in that any other factorization into prime power factors (even if the exponents are different) must be equal to ` S ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 21-Apr-2016.)
theorem ablfac1eu {x3 w q p: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class w) (B2: class) (C: class x3 w q p) (D: class w) (S: class x3 w p) (T: class w p) (G O: class w):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wceq S (cmpt p A2 (crab x3 (wbr (cfv (cv x3) O) (co (cv p) (co (cv p) (cfv B2 chash) cpc) cexp) cdvds) B2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss A2 cprime) $ >
  $ wceq D (crab w (wbr (cv w) (cfv B2 chash) cdvds) cprime) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss D A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wbr G T (cdm cdprd)) (wceq (co G T cdprd) B2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cdm T) A2) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv q) A2)) (wcel C cn0) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv q) A2)) (wceq (cfv (cfv (cv q) T) chash) (co (cv q) C cexp)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq T S) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pgpfac1 . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-Apr-2016.)
theorem pgpfac1lem1 {w: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class) (B2: class w) (C P c_po S U: class) (E: class w) (G K: class) (O: class w) (W: class) (c_0: class w):
  $ wceq K (cfv (cfv G csubg) cmrc) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv (csn A2) K) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv G cgex) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_po (cfv G clsm) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr P G cpgp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv A2 O) E) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel W (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin S W) (csn c_0)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (co S W c_po) U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral w (wi (wa (wpss (cv w) U) (wcel A2 (cv w))) (wn (wpss (co S W c_po) (cv w)))) (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel C (cdif U (co S W c_po)))) (wceq (co (co S W c_po) (cfv (csn C) K) c_po) U) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pgpfac1 . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-Apr-2016.)
theorem pgpfac1lem2 {w: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class) (B2: class w) (C P c_po S c_x U: class) (E: class w) (G K: class) (O: class w) (W: class) (c_0: class w):
  $ wceq K (cfv (cfv G csubg) cmrc) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv (csn A2) K) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv G cgex) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_po (cfv G clsm) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr P G cpgp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv A2 O) E) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel W (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin S W) (csn c_0)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (co S W c_po) U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral w (wi (wa (wpss (cv w) U) (wcel A2 (cv w))) (wn (wpss (co S W c_po) (cv w)))) (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C (cdif U (co S W c_po))) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co P C c_x) (co S W c_po)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pgpfac1 . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 4-Jun-2016.)
theorem pgpfac1lem3a {w: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class) (B2: class w) (C P c_po S c_x U: class) (E: class w) (G K: class) (M O: class w) (W: class) (c_0: class w):
  $ wceq K (cfv (cfv G csubg) cmrc) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv (csn A2) K) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv G cgex) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_po (cfv G clsm) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr P G cpgp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv A2 O) E) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel W (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin S W) (csn c_0)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (co S W c_po) U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral w (wi (wa (wpss (cv w) U) (wcel A2 (cv w))) (wn (wpss (co S W c_po) (cv w)))) (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C (cdif U (co S W c_po))) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M cz) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co (co P C c_x) (co M A2 c_x) (cfv G cplusg)) W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wbr P E cdvds) (wbr P M cdvds)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pgpfac1 . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-Apr-2016.)
theorem pgpfac1lem3 {w t: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class) (B2: class w) (C D P c_po S c_x U: class) (E: class w t) (G K: class) (M O: class w t) (W: class) (c_0: class w):
  $ wceq K (cfv (cfv G csubg) cmrc) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv (csn A2) K) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv G cod) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv G cgex) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq c_po (cfv G clsm) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr P G cpgp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel G cabl) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cfn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv A2 O) E) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel W (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cin S W) (csn c_0)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (co S W c_po) U) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral w (wi (wa (wpss (cv w) U) (wcel A2 (cv w))) (wn (wpss (co S W c_po) (cv w)))) (cfv G csubg)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C (cdif U (co S W c_po))) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv G cmg) $ >
