--| Write a scalar matrix over polynomials (over a commutative ring) as a sum of the product of variable powers and constant scalar matrices with scalar entries. (Contributed by AV, 2-Nov-2019.) (Revised by AV, 4-Dec-2019.)
theorem pmatcollpwscmat {n: setvar} (A2: class n) (B2: class) (C D: class n) (P Q R: class) (S T U c_1: class n) (E c_ex: class) (c_as K: class n) (M N X: class):
  $ wceq P (cfv R cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq C (co N P cmat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_as (cfv C cvsca) $ >
  $ wceq c_ex (cfv (cfv P cmgp) cmg) $ >
