  $ wceq A2 (co N R cmat) $ >
  $ wceq Q (cfv A2 cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq T (co N R cpm2mp) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel N cfn) (wcel R crg)) (wral x3 (wral y1 (wceq (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv y1) (cfv C cmulr)) T) (co (cfv (cv x3) T) (cfv (cv y1) T) (cfv Q cmulr))) B2) B2) $;

--| The transformation of polynomial matrices into polynomials over matrices is a homomorphism of multiplicative monoids. (Contributed by AV, 22-Oct-2019.) (Revised by AV, 6-Dec-2019.)
theorem pm2mpmhm (A2 C P Q R T N: class):
  $ wceq P (cfv R cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq C (co N P cmat) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (co N R cmat) $ >
  $ wceq Q (cfv A2 cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq T (co N R cpm2mp) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel N cfn) (wcel R crg)) (wcel T (co (cfv C cmgp) (cfv Q cmgp) cmhm)) $;

--| The transformation of polynomial matrices into polynomials over matrices is a ring homomorphism. (Contributed by AV, 22-Oct-2019.)
theorem pm2mprhm (A2 C P Q R T N: class):
  $ wceq P (cfv R cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq C (co N P cmat) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (co N R cmat) $ >
  $ wceq Q (cfv A2 cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq T (co N R cpm2mp) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel N cfn) (wcel R crg)) (wcel T (co C Q crh)) $;

--| The transformation of polynomial matrices into polynomials over matrices is a ring isomorphism. (Contributed by AV, 22-Oct-2019.)
theorem pm2mprngiso (A2 C P Q R T N: class):
  $ wceq P (cfv R cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq C (co N P cmat) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (co N R cmat) $ >
  $ wceq Q (cfv A2 cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq T (co N R cpm2mp) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel N cfn) (wcel R crg)) (wcel T (co C Q crs)) $;

--| The ring of polynomial matrices over a ring is isomorphic to the ring of polynomials over matrices of the same dimension over the same ring. (Contributed by AV, 30-Dec-2019.)
theorem pmmpric (A2 C P Q R N: class):
  $ wceq P (cfv R cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq C (co N P cmat) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (co N R cmat) $ >
  $ wceq Q (cfv A2 cpl1) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel N cfn) (wcel R crg)) (wbr C Q cric) $;

--| The transformation of a polynomial matrix having scaled monomials with the same power as entries into a scaled monomial as a polynomial over matrices. (Contributed by AV, 11-Nov-2019.) (Revised by AV, 7-Dec-2019.)
theorem monmat2matmon (A2 B2 C P Q R T c_x E c_ex I c_as K L M N X Y: class):
  $ wceq P (cfv R cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq C (co N P cmat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_as (cfv Q cvsca) $ >
  $ wceq c_ex (cfv (cfv Q cmgp) cmg) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv A2 cv1) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (co N R cmat) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv A2 cbs) $ >
  $ wceq Q (cfv A2 cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq I (co N R cpm2mp) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv (cfv P cmgp) cmg) $ >
  $ wceq Y (cfv R cv1) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv C cvsca) $ >
  $ wceq T (co N R cmat2pmat) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel N cfn) (wcel R ccrg)) (wa (wcel M K) (wcel L cn0))) (wceq (cfv (co (co L Y E) (cfv M T) c_x) I) (co M (co L X c_ex) c_as)) $;

--| The transformation of a sum of matrices having scaled monomials with the same power as entries into a sum of scaled monomials as a polynomial over matrices. (Contributed by AV, 12-Nov-2019.) (Revised by AV, 7-Dec-2019.)
theorem pm2mp {n: setvar} (A2 B2: class) (C P Q: class n) (R T c_x E: class) (c_ex: class n) (I: class) (c_as: class n) (K M N: class) (X: class n) (Y: class):
  $ wceq P (cfv R cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq C (co N P cmat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_as (cfv Q cvsca) $ >
  $ wceq c_ex (cfv (cfv Q cmgp) cmg) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv A2 cv1) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (co N R cmat) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv A2 cbs) $ >
  $ wceq Q (cfv A2 cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq I (co N R cpm2mp) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv (cfv P cmgp) cmg) $ >
  $ wceq Y (cfv R cv1) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv C cvsca) $ >
  $ wceq T (co N R cmat2pmat) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel N cfn) (wcel R ccrg)) (wa (wcel M (co K cn0 cmap)) (wbr M (cfv A2 c0g) cfsupp))) (wceq (cfv (co C (cmpt n cn0 (co (co (cv n) Y E) (cfv (cfv (cv n) M) T) c_x)) cgsu) I) (co Q (cmpt n cn0 (co (cfv (cv n) M) (co (cv n) X c_ex) c_as)) cgsu)) $;

--| Extend class notation with the characteristic polynomial.
term cchpmat: class;

--| Define the characteristic polynomial of a square matrix. According to Wikipedia ("Characteristic polynomial", 31-Jul-2019, ~ https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Characteristic_polynomial ): "The characteristic polynomial of [an n x n matrix] A, denoted by p_A(t), is the polynomial defined by p_A ( t ) = det ( t I - A ) where I denotes the n-by-n identity matrix.". In addition, however, the underlying ring must be commutative, see definition in [Lang], p. 561: " Let k be a commutative ring ... Let M be any n x n matrix in k ... We define the characteristic polynomial P_M(t) to be the determinant det ( t I_n - M ) where I_n is the unit n x n matrix." To be more precise, the matrices A and I on the right hand side are matrices with coefficients of a polynomial ring. Therefore, the original matrix A over a given commutative ring must be transformed into corresponding matrices over the polynomial ring over the given ring. (Contributed by AV, 2-Aug-2019.)
axiom df_chpmat {m n r: setvar}:
  $ wceq cchpmat (cmpo n r cfn cvv (cmpt m (cfv (co (cv n) (cv r) cmat) cbs) (cfv (co (co (cfv (cv r) cv1) (cfv (co (cv n) (cfv (cv r) cpl1) cmat) cur) (cfv (co (cv n) (cfv (cv r) cpl1) cmat) cvsca)) (cfv (cv m) (co (cv n) (cv r) cmat2pmat)) (cfv (co (cv n) (cfv (cv r) cpl1) cmat) csg)) (co (cv n) (cfv (cv r) cpl1) cmdat)))) $;

--| Closure of the characteristic matrix of a matrix. (Contributed by AV, 25-Oct-2019.) (Proof shortened by AV, 29-Nov-2019.)
theorem chmatcl (A2 B2 P R T c_x c_1 H M c_mi N X Y: class):
  $ wceq A2 (co N R cmat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv A2 cbs) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv R cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq Y (co N P cmat) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv R cv1) $ >
  $ wceq T (co N R cmat2pmat) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv Y csg) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv Y cvsca) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv Y cur) $ >
  $ wceq H (co (co X c_1 c_x) (cfv M T) c_mi) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel N cfn) (wcel R crg) (wcel M B2)) (wcel H (cfv Y cbs)) $;

--| The entries of the characteristic matrix of a matrix. (Contributed by AV, 2-Aug-2019.) (Proof shortened by AV, 10-Dec-2019.)
theorem chmatval (A2 B2 P c_sm R T c_x c_1 H I J M c_mi N X Y c_0: class):
  $ wceq A2 (co N R cmat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv A2 cbs) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv R cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq Y (co N P cmat) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv R cv1) $ >
  $ wceq T (co N R cmat2pmat) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv Y csg) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv Y cvsca) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv Y cur) $ >
  $ wceq H (co (co X c_1 c_x) (cfv M T) c_mi) $ >
  $ wceq c_sm (cfv P csg) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv P c0g) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel N cfn) (wcel R crg) (wcel M B2)) (wa (wcel I N) (wcel J N))) (wceq (co I J H) (cif (wceq I J) (co X (co I J (cfv M T)) c_sm) (co c_0 (co I J (cfv M T)) c_sm))) $;

--| Value of the characteristic polynomial function. (Contributed by AV, 2-Aug-2019.)
theorem chpmatfval {m: setvar} (A2: class m) (B2: class) (C: class m) (D: class) (P: class m) (R T c_x c_1 c_mi N: class) (V: class m) (X: class) (Y: class m):
  $ wceq C (co N R cchpmat) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (co N R cmat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv A2 cbs) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv R cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq Y (co N P cmat) $ >
  $ wceq D (co N P cmdat) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv Y csg) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv R cv1) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv Y cvsca) $ >
  $ wceq T (co N R cmat2pmat) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv Y cur) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel N cfn) (wcel R V)) (wceq C (cmpt m B2 (cfv (co (co X c_1 c_x) (cfv (cv m) T) c_mi) D))) $;

--| The characteristic polynomial of a (square) matrix (expressed with a determinant). (Contributed by AV, 2-Aug-2019.)
theorem chpmatval (A2 B2 C D P R T c_x c_1 M c_mi N V X Y: class):
  $ wceq C (co N R cchpmat) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (co N R cmat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv A2 cbs) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv R cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq Y (co N P cmat) $ >
  $ wceq D (co N P cmdat) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv Y csg) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv R cv1) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv Y cvsca) $ >
  $ wceq T (co N R cmat2pmat) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv Y cur) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel N cfn) (wcel R V) (wcel M B2)) (wceq (cfv M C) (cfv (co (co X c_1 c_x) (cfv M T) c_mi) D)) $;

--| The characteristic polynomial of a (square) matrix over a commutative ring is a polynomial, see also the following remark in [Lang], p. 561: "[the characteristic polynomial] is an element of k[[t]". (Contributed by AV, 2-Aug-2019.) (Proof shortened by AV, 29-Nov-2019.)
theorem chpmatply1 (A2 B2 C P R E M N: class):
  $ wceq C (co N R cchpmat) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (co N R cmat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv A2 cbs) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv R cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv P cbs) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel N cfn) (wcel R ccrg) (wcel M B2)) (wcel (cfv M C) E) $;

--| The characteristic polynomial of a (square) matrix (expressed with the Leibnitz formula for the determinant). (Contributed by AV, 2-Aug-2019.)
theorem chpmatval2 {x3 p: setvar} (A2 B2 C: class x3 p) (P: class) (R S: class x3 p) (T c_x: class) (c_xp U: class x3 p) (c_1: class) (G H: class x3 p) (M c_mi N X: class) (Y Z: class x3 p):
  $ wceq C (co N R cchpmat) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (co N R cmat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv A2 cbs) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv R cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq Y (co N P cmat) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv Y csg) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv R cv1) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv Y cvsca) $ >
  $ wceq T (co N R cmat2pmat) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv Y cur) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N csymg) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq Z (cfv P czrh) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv N cpsgn) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv P cmgp) $ >
  $ wceq c_xp (cfv P cmulr) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel N cfn) (wcel R crg) (wcel M B2)) (wceq (cfv M C) (co P (cmpt p H (co (cfv (cv p) (ccom Z S)) (co U (cmpt x3 N (co (cfv (cv x3) (cv p)) (cv x3) (co (co X c_1 c_x) (cfv M T) c_mi))) cgsu) c_xp)) cgsu)) $;

--| The characteristic polynomial of the empty matrix. (Contributed by AV, 6-Aug-2019.)
theorem chpmat0d (C R: class):
  $ wceq C (co c0 R cchpmat) $ >
  $ wi (wcel R crg) (wceq (cfv c0 C) (cfv (cfv R cpl1) cur)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ chpmat1d . (Contributed by AV, 7-Aug-2019.)
theorem chpmat1dlem (A2 B2 C P R S T G I M c_mi N V X: class):
  $ wceq C (co N R cchpmat) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv R cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (co N R cmat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv A2 cbs) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv R cv1) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv P csg) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv P cascl) $ >
  $ wceq G (co N P cmat) $ >
  $ wceq T (co N R cmat2pmat) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel R crg) (wa (wceq N (csn I)) (wcel I V)) (wcel M B2)) (wceq (co I I (co (co X (cfv G cur) (cfv G cvsca)) (cfv M T) (cfv G csg))) (co X (cfv (co I I M) S) c_mi)) $;

--| The characteristic polynomial of a matrix with dimension 1. (Contributed by AV, 7-Aug-2019.)
theorem chpmat1d (A2 B2 C P R S I M c_mi N V X: class):
  $ wceq C (co N R cchpmat) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv R cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (co N R cmat) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv A2 cbs) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv R cv1) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv P csg) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv P cascl) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel R ccrg) (wa (wceq N (csn I)) (wcel I V)) (wcel M B2)) (wceq (cfv M C) (co X (cfv (co I I M) S) c_mi)) $;

--| Lemma 0 for ~ chpdmat . (Contributed by AV, 18-Aug-2019.)
theorem chpdmatlem0 (A2 B2 C P Q R S c_x c_1 G c_mi N X c_0: class):
  $ wceq C (co N R cchpmat) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv R cpl1) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (co N R cmat) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv P cascl) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv A2 cbs) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv R cv1) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv R c0g) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv P cmgp) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv P csg) $ >
  $ wceq Q (co N P cmat) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv Q cur) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv Q cvsca) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel N cfn) (wcel R crg)) (wcel (co X c_1 c_x) (cfv Q cbs)) $;

