  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 crp (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cfv (cv n) L) X) (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cv n) cdiv) cmul)) (cif (wceq S cc0) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cc0) caddc)) co1) $;

--| The set ` W ` is the collection of all non-principal Dirichlet characters such that the sum ` sum_ n e. NN , X ( n ) / n ` is equal to zero. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 5-May-2016.)
theorem dchrvmaeq0 {y1 m a: setvar} (ph: wff y1 a) (C D S c_1 F: class a) (G: class y1 m a) (L: class) (N: class a) (W: class y1 m a) (X: class) (Z: class a):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne X c_1) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt a cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv a) L) X) (cv a) cdiv)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C (co cc0 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cseq caddc F c1) S cli) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cfv (cv y1) cfl) (cseq caddc F c1)) S cmin) cabs) (co C (cv y1) cdiv) cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab y1 (wceq (csu m cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv m) L) (cv y1)) (cv m) cdiv)) cc0) (cdif D (csn c_1))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wcel X W) (wceq S cc0)) $;

--| Value of the function ` F ` , the divisor sum of a Dirichlet character. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 5-May-2016.)
theorem dchrisum0fval {v t q b: setvar} (ph: wff v q b) (A2: class) (D c_1 F: class v q b) (G: class v t q b) (L: class q) (N: class v b) (X: class q) (Z: class v t q b):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt b cn (csu v (crab q (wbr (cv q) (cv b) cdvds) cn) (cfv (cfv (cv v) L) X))) $ >
  $ wi (wcel A2 cn) (wceq (cfv A2 F) (csu t (crab q (wbr (cv q) A2 cdvds) cn) (cfv (cfv (cv t) L) X))) $;

--| The function ` F ` , the divisor sum of a Dirichlet character, is a multiplicative function (but not completely multiplicative). Equation 9.4.27 of [Shapiro], p. 382. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 5-May-2016.)
theorem dchrisum0fmul {v q b: setvar} (ph: wff v q b) (A2 B2: class) (D c_1 F G: class v q b) (L: class q) (N: class v b) (X: class q) (Z: class v q b):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt b cn (csu v (crab q (wbr (cv q) (cv b) cdvds) cn) (cfv (cfv (cv v) L) X))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 B2 cgcd) c1) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv (co A2 B2 cmul) F) (co (cfv A2 F) (cfv B2 F) cmul)) $;

--| The function ` F ` is a real function. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 5-May-2016.)
theorem dchrisum0ff {v q b: setvar} (ph: wff v q b) (D c_1 F G: class v q b) (L: class q) (N: class v b) (X: class q) (Z: class v q b):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt b cn (csu v (crab q (wbr (cv q) (cv b) cdvds) cn) (cfv (cfv (cv v) L) X))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf (cfv Z cbs) cr X) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf cn cr F) $;

--| Lemma for ~ dchrisum0flb . Base case, prime power. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 5-May-2016.)
theorem dchrisum0flblem1 {v q b: setvar} (ph: wff v q b) (A2: class) (D: class v q b) (P: class) (c_1 F G: class v q b) (L: class q) (N: class v b) (X: class q) (Z: class v q b):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt b cn (csu v (crab q (wbr (cv q) (cv b) cdvds) cn) (cfv (cfv (cv v) L) X))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf (cfv Z cbs) cr X) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel P cprime) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cn0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cif (wcel (cfv (co P A2 cexp) csqrt) cn) c1 cc0) (cfv (co P A2 cexp) F) cle) $;

--| Lemma for ~ dchrisum0flb . Induction over relatively prime factors, with the prime power case handled in dchrisum0flblem1 . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 5-May-2016.) Replace reference to OLD theorem. (Revised by Wolf Lammen, 8-Sep-2020.)
theorem dchrisum0flblem2 {y1 v q b: setvar} (ph: wff y1 v q b) (A2: class) (D: class v q b) (P: class) (c_1 F: class v q b) (G: class y1 v q b) (L: class q) (N: class v b) (X: class q) (Z: class v q b):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt b cn (csu v (crab q (wbr (cv q) (cv b) cdvds) cn) (cfv (cfv (cv v) L) X))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf (cfv Z cbs) cr X) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 (cfv c2 cuz)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel P cprime) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr P A2 cdvds) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cif (wcel (cfv (cv y1) csqrt) cn) c1 cc0) (cfv (cv y1) F) cle) (co c1 A2 cfzo)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cif (wcel (cfv A2 csqrt) cn) c1 cc0) (cfv A2 F) cle) $;

--| The divisor sum of a real Dirichlet character, is lower bounded by zero everywhere and one at the squares. Equation 9.4.29 of [Shapiro], p. 382. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 5-May-2016.)
theorem dchrisum0flb {v q b: setvar} (ph: wff v q b) (A2: class) (D c_1 F G: class v q b) (L: class q) (N: class v b) (X: class q) (Z: class v q b):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt b cn (csu v (crab q (wbr (cv q) (cv b) cdvds) cn) (cfv (cfv (cv v) L) X))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf (cfv Z cbs) cr X) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cif (wcel (cfv A2 csqrt) cn) c1 cc0) (cfv A2 F) cle) $;

--| The sum ` sum_ k <_ x , F ( x ) / sqrt k ` is divergent (i.e. not eventually bounded). Equation 9.4.30 of [Shapiro], p. 383. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 5-May-2016.)
theorem dchrisum0fno1 {x3 v k q b: setvar} (ph: wff v q b) (D c_1 F: class v q b) (G: class x3 v k q b) (L: class q) (N: class v b) (X: class q) (Z: class v q b):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt b cn (csu v (crab q (wbr (cv q) (cv b) cdvds) cn) (cfv (cfv (cv v) L) X))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf (cfv Z cbs) cr X) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 crp (csu k (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv k) F) (cfv (cv k) csqrt) cdiv))) co1) $ >
  $ wn ph $;

--| A partial result along the lines of ~ rpvmasum . The sum of the von Mangoldt function over those integers ` n == A ` (mod ` N ` ) is asymptotic to ` ( 1 - M ) ( log x / phi ( x ) ) + O(1) ` , where ` M ` is the number of non-principal Dirichlet characters with ` sum_ n e. NN , X ( n ) / n = 0 ` . Our goal is to show this set is empty. Equation 9.4.3 of [Shapiro], p. 375. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 5-May-2016.)
theorem rpvmasum2 {x3 y1 f2 m n: setvar} (ph: wff y1) (A2 D: class) (T: class f2) (U: class y1 f2) (c_1: class) (G: class x3 y1 m n) (L N: class) (W: class y1 m n) (Z: class):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab y1 (wceq (csu m cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv m) L) (cv y1)) (cv m) cdiv)) cc0) (cdif D (csn c_1))) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv Z cui) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 U) $ >
  $ wceq T (cima (ccnv L) (csn A2)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv f2) W)) (wceq A2 (cfv Z cur)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 crp (co (co (cfv N cphi) (csu n (cin (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) T) (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cv n) cdiv)) cmul) (co (cfv (cv x3) clog) (co c1 (cfv W chash) cmin) cmul) cmin)) co1) $;

--| Suppose ` X ` is a non-principal Dirichlet character with ` sum_ n e. NN , X ( n ) / n = 0 ` . Then ` X ` is a real character. Part of Lemma 9.4.4 of [Shapiro], p. 382. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 5-May-2016.)
theorem dchrisum0re {y1 m: setvar} (ph: wff y1) (D c_1: class) (G: class y1 m) (L N: class) (W: class y1 m) (X Z: class):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab y1 (wceq (csu m cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv m) L) (cv y1)) (cv m) cdiv)) cc0) (cdif D (csn c_1))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X W) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf (cfv Z cbs) cr X) $;

--| Lemma for ~ dchrisum0 . Apply ~ dchrisum for the function ` 1 / sqrt y ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 10-May-2016.)
theorem dchrisum0lema {y1 t m a c: setvar} (ph: wff y1 a) (D c_1 F: class a) (G: class y1 t m a c) (L: class) (N: class a) (W: class y1 m a) (X: class) (Z: class t a c):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab y1 (wceq (csu m cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv m) L) (cv y1)) (cv m) cdiv)) cc0) (cdif D (csn c_1))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X W) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt a cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv a) L) X) (cfv (cv a) csqrt) cdiv)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wex t (wrex c (wa (wbr (cseq caddc F c1) (cv t) cli) (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cfv (cv y1) cfl) (cseq caddc F c1)) (cv t) cmin) cabs) (co (cv c) (cfv (cv y1) csqrt) cdiv) cle) (co c1 cpnf cico))) (co cc0 cpnf cico))) $;

--| Lemma for ~ dchrisum0lem1 . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 7-Jun-2016.)
theorem dchrisum0lem1b {y1 m a: setvar} (ph: wff y1 a) (x3: setvar) (C D S c_1 F: class a) (G: class y1 m a) (L: class) (N: class a) (W: class y1 m a) (X: class) (Z: class a) (d: setvar):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab y1 (wceq (csu m cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv m) L) (cv y1)) (cv m) cdiv)) cc0) (cdif D (csn c_1))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X W) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt a cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv a) L) X) (cfv (cv a) csqrt) cdiv)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C (co cc0 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cseq caddc F c1) S cli) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cfv (cv y1) cfl) (cseq caddc F c1)) S cmin) cabs) (co C (cfv (cv y1) csqrt) cdiv) cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) crp)) (wcel (cv d) (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz))) (wbr (cfv (csu m (co (co (cfv (cv x3) cfl) c1 caddc) (cfv (co (co (cv x3) c2 cexp) (cv d) cdiv) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cfv (cv m) L) X) (cfv (cv m) csqrt) cdiv)) cabs) (co (co c2 C cmul) (cfv (cv x3) csqrt) cdiv) cle) $;

--| Lemma for ~ dchrisum0 . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-May-2016.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 7-Jun-2016.)
theorem dchrisum0lem1 {x3 y1 m a d: setvar} (ph: wff y1 a) (C: class a) (D: class a d) (S: class a) (c_1: class a d) (F: class a) (G: class x3 y1 m a d) (L: class) (N: class a d) (W: class y1 m a d) (X: class) (Z: class a d):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab y1 (wceq (csu m cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv m) L) (cv y1)) (cv m) cdiv)) cc0) (cdif D (csn c_1))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X W) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt a cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv a) L) X) (cfv (cv a) csqrt) cdiv)) $ >
