  $ wi ph (wbr (cseq caddc F c1) S cli) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cfv (cv y1) cfl) (cseq caddc F c1)) S cmin) cabs) (co C (cfv (cv y1) csqrt) cdiv) cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 crp (csu m (co (co (cfv (cv x3) cfl) c1 caddc) (cfv (co (cv x3) c2 cexp) cfl) cfz) (csu d (co c1 (cfv (co (co (cv x3) c2 cexp) (cv m) cdiv) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cfv (cv m) L) X) (cfv (cv m) csqrt) cdiv) (cfv (cv d) csqrt) cdiv)))) co1) $;

--| Lemma for ~ dchrisum0 . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-May-2016.)
theorem dchrisum0lem2a {x3 y1 m a d: setvar} (ph: wff y1 a) (C: class a) (D: class a d) (S: class a) (U: class y1 a d) (c_1: class a d) (F: class a) (G H: class x3 y1 m a d) (L: class) (N: class a d) (W: class y1 m a d) (X: class) (Z: class a d):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab y1 (wceq (csu m cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv m) L) (cv y1)) (cv m) cdiv)) cc0) (cdif D (csn c_1))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X W) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt a cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv a) L) X) (cfv (cv a) csqrt) cdiv)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C (co cc0 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cseq caddc F c1) S cli) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cfv (cv y1) cfl) (cseq caddc F c1)) S cmin) cabs) (co C (cfv (cv y1) csqrt) cdiv) cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wceq H (cmpt y1 crp (co (csu d (co c1 (cfv (cv y1) cfl) cfz) (co c1 (cfv (cv d) csqrt) cdiv)) (co c2 (cfv (cv y1) csqrt) cmul) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr H U crli) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 crp (csu m (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cfv (cv m) L) X) (cfv (cv m) csqrt) cdiv) (cfv (co (co (cv x3) c2 cexp) (cv m) cdiv) H) cmul))) co1) $;

--| Lemma for ~ dchrisum0 . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-May-2016.)
theorem dchrisum0lem2 {x3 y1 m a d: setvar} (ph: wff y1 a) (C: class a) (D: class a d) (S T: class a) (U: class y1 a d) (c_1: class a d) (E F: class a) (G H: class x3 y1 m a d) (K: class x3 a d) (L: class) (N: class a d) (W: class y1 m a d) (X: class) (Z: class a d):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab y1 (wceq (csu m cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv m) L) (cv y1)) (cv m) cdiv)) cc0) (cdif D (csn c_1))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X W) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt a cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv a) L) X) (cfv (cv a) csqrt) cdiv)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C (co cc0 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cseq caddc F c1) S cli) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cfv (cv y1) cfl) (cseq caddc F c1)) S cmin) cabs) (co C (cfv (cv y1) csqrt) cdiv) cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wceq H (cmpt y1 crp (co (csu d (co c1 (cfv (cv y1) cfl) cfz) (co c1 (cfv (cv d) csqrt) cdiv)) (co c2 (cfv (cv y1) csqrt) cmul) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr H U crli) $ >
  $ wceq K (cmpt a cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv a) L) X) (cv a) cdiv)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E (co cc0 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cseq caddc K c1) T cli) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cfv (cv y1) cfl) (cseq caddc K c1)) T cmin) cabs) (co E (cv y1) cdiv) cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 crp (csu m (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (csu d (co c1 (cfv (co (co (cv x3) c2 cexp) (cv m) cdiv) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cfv (cv m) L) X) (cfv (cv m) csqrt) cdiv) (cfv (cv d) csqrt) cdiv)))) co1) $;

--| Lemma for ~ dchrisum0 . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-May-2016.)
theorem dchrisum0lem3 {x3 y1 m a d: setvar} (ph: wff y1 a) (C: class a) (D: class a d) (S: class a) (c_1: class a d) (F: class a) (G: class x3 y1 m a d) (L: class) (N: class a d) (W: class y1 m a d) (X: class) (Z: class a d):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab y1 (wceq (csu m cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv m) L) (cv y1)) (cv m) cdiv)) cc0) (cdif D (csn c_1))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X W) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt a cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv a) L) X) (cfv (cv a) csqrt) cdiv)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C (co cc0 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cseq caddc F c1) S cli) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cfv (cv y1) cfl) (cseq caddc F c1)) S cmin) cabs) (co C (cfv (cv y1) csqrt) cdiv) cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 crp (csu m (co c1 (cfv (co (cv x3) c2 cexp) cfl) cfz) (csu d (co c1 (cfv (co (co (cv x3) c2 cexp) (cv m) cdiv) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cfv (cv m) L) X) (cfv (co (cv m) (cv d) cmul) csqrt) cdiv)))) co1) $;

--| The sum ` sum_ n e. NN , X ( n ) / n ` is nonzero for all non-principal Dirichlet characters (i.e. the assumption ` X e. W ` is contradictory). This is the key result that allows to eliminate the conditionals from ~ dchrmusum2 and ~ dchrvmasumif . Lemma 9.4.4 of [Shapiro], p. 382. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-May-2016.)
theorem dchrisum0 {y1 m: setvar} (ph: wff y1) (D c_1: class) (G: class y1 m) (L N: class) (W: class y1 m) (X Z: class):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wceq W (crab y1 (wceq (csu m cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv m) L) (cv y1)) (cv m) cdiv)) cc0) (cdif D (csn c_1))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X W) $ >
  $ wn ph $;

--| The sum ` sum_ n e. NN , X ( n ) / n ` is nonzero for all non-principal Dirichlet characters (i.e. the assumption ` X e. W ` is contradictory). This is the key result that allows to eliminate the conditionals from ~ dchrmusum2 and ~ dchrvmasumif . Lemma 9.4.4 of [Shapiro], p. 382. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-May-2016.)
theorem dchrisumn0 {y1 a: setvar} (ph: wff y1 a) (C D T c_1 F: class a) (G: class y1 a) (L: class) (N: class a) (X: class) (Z: class a):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne X c_1) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt a cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv a) L) X) (cv a) cdiv)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C (co cc0 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cseq caddc F c1) T cli) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cfv (cv y1) cfl) (cseq caddc F c1)) T cmin) cabs) (co C (cv y1) cdiv) cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne T cc0) $;

--| The sum of the M&ouml;bius function multiplied by a non-principal Dirichlet character, divided by ` n ` , is bounded. Equation 9.4.16 of [Shapiro], p. 379. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-May-2016.)
theorem dchrmusumlem {x3 y1 n a: setvar} (ph: wff y1 a) (C D T c_1 F: class a) (G: class x3 y1 n a) (L: class) (N: class a) (X: class) (Z: class a):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne X c_1) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt a cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv a) L) X) (cv a) cdiv)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C (co cc0 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cseq caddc F c1) T cli) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cfv (cv y1) cfl) (cseq caddc F c1)) T cmin) cabs) (co C (cv y1) cdiv) cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 crp (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cfv (cv n) L) X) (co (cfv (cv n) cmu) (cv n) cdiv) cmul))) co1) $;

--| The sum of the M&ouml;bius function multiplied by a non-principal Dirichlet character, divided by ` n ` , is bounded. Equation 9.4.16 of [Shapiro], p. 379. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-May-2016.)
theorem dchrvmasumlem {x3 y1 n a: setvar} (ph: wff y1 a) (C D T c_1 F: class a) (G: class x3 y1 n a) (L: class) (N: class a) (X: class) (Z: class a):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne X c_1) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt a cn (co (cfv (cfv (cv a) L) X) (cv a) cdiv)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C (co cc0 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cseq caddc F c1) T cli) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cfv (cv y1) cfl) (cseq caddc F c1)) T cmin) cabs) (co C (cv y1) cdiv) cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 crp (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cfv (cv n) L) X) (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cv n) cdiv) cmul))) co1) $;

--| The sum of the M&ouml;bius function multiplied by a non-principal Dirichlet character, divided by ` n ` , is bounded. Equation 9.4.16 of [Shapiro], p. 379. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-May-2016.)
theorem dchrmusum {x3 n: setvar} (ph: wff) (D c_1: class) (G: class x3 n) (L N X Z: class):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne X c_1) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 crp (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cfv (cv n) L) X) (co (cfv (cv n) cmu) (cv n) cdiv) cmul))) co1) $;

--| The sum of the von Mangoldt function multiplied by a non-principal Dirichlet character, divided by ` n ` , is bounded. Equation 9.4.8 of [Shapiro], p. 376. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-May-2016.)
theorem dchrvmasum {x3 n: setvar} (ph: wff) (D c_1: class) (G: class x3 n) (L N X Z: class):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq G (cfv N cdchr) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv G cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv G c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X D) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne X c_1) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 crp (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cfv (cv n) L) X) (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cv n) cdiv) cmul))) co1) $;

--| The sum of the von Mangoldt function over those integers ` n == A ` (mod ` N ` ) is asymptotic to ` log x / phi ( x ) + O(1) ` . Equation 9.4.3 of [Shapiro], p. 375. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 2-May-2016.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 26-May-2016.)
theorem rpvmasum {x3 n: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 T U L N Z: class):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv Z cui) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 U) $ >
  $ wceq T (cima (ccnv L) (csn A2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 crp (co (co (cfv N cphi) (csu n (cin (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) T) (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cv n) cdiv)) cmul) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmin)) co1) $;

--| The sum of ` log p / p ` over the primes ` p == A ` (mod ` N ` ) is asymptotic to ` log x / phi ( x ) + O(1) ` . Equation 9.4.3 of [Shapiro], p. 375. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 16-Apr-2016.)
theorem rplogsum {x3 p: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 T U L N Z: class):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv Z cui) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 U) $ >
  $ wceq T (cima (ccnv L) (csn A2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 crp (co (co (cfv N cphi) (csu p (cin (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (cin cprime T)) (co (cfv (cv p) clog) (cv p) cdiv)) cmul) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmin)) co1) $;

--| Dirichlet's theorem: there are infinitely many primes in any arithmetic progression coprime to ` N ` . Theorem 9.4.1 of [Shapiro], p. 375. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-Apr-2016.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 26-May-2016.)
theorem dirith2 (ph: wff) (A2 T U L N Z: class):
  $ wceq Z (cfv N czn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv Z czrh) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv Z cui) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 U) $ >
  $ wceq T (cima (ccnv L) (csn A2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cin cprime T) cn cen) $;

--| Dirichlet's theorem: there are infinitely many primes in any arithmetic progression coprime to ` N ` . Theorem 9.4.1 of [Shapiro], p. 375. See ~ https://metamath-blog.blogspot.com/2016/05/dirichlets-theorem.html for an informal exposition. This is Metamath 100 proof #48. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 12-May-2016.)
theorem dirith {p: setvar} (A2 N: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel N cn) (wcel A2 cz) (wceq (co A2 N cgcd) c1)) (wbr (crab p (wbr N (co (cv p) A2 cmin) cdvds) cprime) cn cen) $;

--| Asymptotic formula for ` sum_ n <_ x , mmu ( n ) / n = O(1) ` . Equation 10.2.1 of [Shapiro], p. 405. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 14-May-2016.)
theorem mudivsum {x3 n: setvar}:
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 crp (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) cmu) (cv n) cdiv))) co1 $;

--| Lemma for ~ mulogsum . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 14-May-2016.)
theorem mulogsumlem {x3 m n: setvar}:
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 crp (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cv n) cmu) (cv n) cdiv) (co (csu m (co c1 (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) cfl) cfz) (co c1 (cv m) cdiv)) (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) clog) cmin) cmul))) co1 $;

--| Asymptotic formula for ` sum_ n <_ x , ( mmu ( n ) / n ) log ( x / n ) = O(1) ` . Equation 10.2.6 of [Shapiro], p. 406. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 14-May-2016.)
theorem mulogsum {x3 n: setvar}:
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 crp (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cv n) cmu) (cv n) cdiv) (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) clog) cmul))) co1 $;

--| Asymptotic analysis of ` sum_ n <_ x , log n / n = ( log x ) ^ 2 / 2 + L + O ( log x / x ) ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 18-May-2016.)
theorem logdivsum {y1 i: setvar} (A2: class) (F L: class y1 i):
  $ wceq F (cmpt y1 crp (co (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv y1) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) clog) (cv i) cdiv)) (co (co (cfv (cv y1) clog) c2 cexp) c2 cdiv) cmin)) $ >
  $ w3a (wf crp cr F) (wcel F (cdm crli)) (wi (w3a (wbr F L crli) (wcel A2 crp) (wbr ceu A2 cle)) (wbr (cfv (co (cfv A2 F) L cmin) cabs) (co (cfv A2 clog) A2 cdiv) cle)) $;

--| Asymptotic formula for ` sum_ n <_ x , log ( x / n ) / n = ( 1 / 2 ) log ^ 2 ( x ) + ` ` gamma x. log x - L + O ( log x / x ) ` , with explicit constants. Equation 10.2.7 of [Shapiro], p. 407. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 18-May-2016.)
theorem mulog2sumlem1 {y1 i m: setvar} (ph: wff y1 i) (A2: class) (F L: class y1 i m):
  $ wceq F (cmpt y1 crp (co (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv y1) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) clog) (cv i) cdiv)) (co (co (cfv (cv y1) clog) c2 cexp) c2 cdiv) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F L crli) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr ceu A2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cfv (co (csu m (co c1 (cfv A2 cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (co A2 (cv m) cdiv) clog) (cv m) cdiv)) (co (co (co (cfv A2 clog) c2 cexp) c2 cdiv) (co (co cem (cfv A2 clog) cmul) L cmin) caddc) cmin) cabs) (co c2 (co (cfv A2 clog) A2 cdiv) cmul) cle) $;

--| Lemma for ~ mulog2sum . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 19-May-2016.)
theorem mulog2sumlem2 {x3 y1 i m n: setvar} (ph: wff y1 i) (R: class y1 i m) (T: class x3 y1 i m n) (F: class y1 i m n) (L: class y1 i m):
  $ wceq F (cmpt y1 crp (co (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv y1) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) clog) (cv i) cdiv)) (co (co (cfv (cv y1) clog) c2 cexp) c2 cdiv) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F L crli) $ >
  $ wceq T (co (co (co (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) clog) c2 cexp) c2 cdiv) (co (co cem (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) clog) cmul) L cmin) caddc) $ >
  $ wceq R (co (co (co c1 c2 cdiv) (co cem (cfv L cabs) caddc) caddc) (csu m (co c1 c2 cfz) (co (cfv (co ceu (cv m) cdiv) clog) (cv m) cdiv)) caddc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 crp (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cv n) cmu) (cv n) cdiv) T cmul)) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmin)) co1) $;

--| Lemma for ~ mulog2sum . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-May-2016.)
theorem mulog2sumlem3 {x3 y1 i n: setvar} (ph: wff y1 i) (F: class y1 i n) (L: class y1 i):
  $ wceq F (cmpt y1 crp (co (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv y1) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) clog) (cv i) cdiv)) (co (co (cfv (cv y1) clog) c2 cexp) c2 cdiv) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr F L crli) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 crp (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cv n) cmu) (cv n) cdiv) (co (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) clog) c2 cexp) cmul)) (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) cmin)) co1) $;

--| Asymptotic formula for ` sum_ n <_ x , ( mmu ( n ) / n ) log ^ 2 ( x / n ) ` ` = 2 log x + O(1) ` . Equation 10.2.8 of [Shapiro], p. 407. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 19-May-2016.)
theorem mulog2sum {x3 n: setvar}:
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 crp (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cv n) cmu) (cv n) cdiv) (co (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) clog) c2 cexp) cmul)) (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) cmin)) co1 $;

--| The sum ` sum_ n <_ x , Lam ( n ) log ( x / n ) / n ` is asymptotic to ` log ^ 2 ( x ) / 2 + O ( log x ) ` . Exercise 9.1.7 of [Shapiro], p. 336. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem vmalogdivsum2 {x3 n: setvar}:
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cv n) cdiv) (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) clog) cmul)) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) (co (cfv (cv x3) clog) c2 cdiv) cmin)) co1 $;

--| The sum ` sum_ n <_ x , Lam ( n ) log n / n ` is asymptotic to ` log ^ 2 ( x ) / 2 + O ( log x ) ` . Exercise 9.1.7 of [Shapiro], p. 336. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem vmalogdivsum {x3 n: setvar}:
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cv n) cdiv) (cfv (cv n) clog) cmul)) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) (co (cfv (cv x3) clog) c2 cdiv) cmin)) co1 $;

--| Lemma for ~ 2vmadivsum . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem _2vmadivsumlem {x3 y1 i m n: setvar} (ph: wff y1 i) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv y1) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) cvma) (cv i) cdiv)) (cfv (cv y1) clog) cmin) cabs) A2 cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cv n) cdiv) (csu m (co c1 (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv m) cvma) (cv m) cdiv)) cmul)) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) (co (cfv (cv x3) clog) c2 cdiv) cmin)) co1) $;

--| The sum ` sum_ m n <_ x , Lam ( m ) Lam ( n ) / m n ` is asymptotic to ` log ^ 2 ( x ) / 2 + O ( log x ) ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem _2vmadivsum {x3 m n: setvar}:
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cv n) cdiv) (csu m (co c1 (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv m) cvma) (cv m) cdiv)) cmul)) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) (co (cfv (cv x3) clog) c2 cdiv) cmin)) co1 $;

--| A formula for ` log ^ 2 ( N ) ` in terms of the primes. Equation 10.4.6 of [Shapiro], p. 418. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-May-2016.)
theorem logsqvma {x3 u d: setvar} (N: class):
  $ wi (wcel N cn) (wceq (csu d (crab x3 (wbr (cv x3) N cdvds) cn) (co (csu u (crab x3 (wbr (cv x3) (cv d) cdvds) cn) (co (cfv (cv u) cvma) (cfv (co (cv d) (cv u) cdiv) cvma) cmul)) (co (cfv (cv d) cvma) (cfv (cv d) clog) cmul) caddc)) (co (cfv N clog) c2 cexp)) $;

--| The M&ouml;bius inverse of ~ logsqvma . Equation 10.4.8 of [Shapiro], p. 418. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-May-2016.)
theorem logsqvma2 {x3 d: setvar} (N: class):
  $ wi (wcel N cn) (wceq (csu d (crab x3 (wbr (cv x3) N cdvds) cn) (co (cfv (cv d) cmu) (co (cfv (co N (cv d) cdiv) clog) c2 cexp) cmul)) (co (csu d (crab x3 (wbr (cv x3) N cdvds) cn) (co (cfv (cv d) cvma) (cfv (co N (cv d) cdiv) cvma) cmul)) (co (cfv N cvma) (cfv N clog) cmul) caddc)) $;

--| Bound on the difference between ` sum_ n <_ A , log ^ 2 ( n ) ` and the equivalent integral. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 20-May-2016.)
theorem log2sumbnd {n: setvar} (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 crp) (wbr c1 A2 cle)) (wbr (cfv (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv A2 cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) clog) c2 cexp)) (co A2 (co (co (cfv A2 clog) c2 cexp) (co c2 (co c2 (cfv A2 clog) cmul) cmin) caddc) cmul) cmin) cabs) (co (co (cfv A2 clog) c2 cexp) c2 caddc) cle) $;

--| Lemma for ~ selberg . Estimation of the asymptotic part of ~ selberglem3 . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 20-May-2016.)
theorem selberglem1 {x3 n: setvar} (T: class x3 n):
  $ wceq T (co (co (co (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) clog) c2 cexp) (co c2 (co c2 (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) clog) cmul) cmin) caddc) (cv n) cdiv) $ >
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 crp (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) cmu) T cmul)) (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) cmin)) co1 $;

--| Lemma for ~ selberg . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 23-May-2016.)
theorem selberglem2 {x3 m n: setvar} (T: class x3 m n):
  $ wceq T (co (co (co (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) clog) c2 cexp) (co c2 (co c2 (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) clog) cmul) cmin) caddc) (cv n) cdiv) $ >
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 crp (co (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (csu m (co c1 (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) cmu) (co (cfv (cv m) clog) c2 cexp) cmul))) (cv x3) cdiv) (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) cmin)) co1 $;

--| Lemma for ~ selberg . Estimation of the left-hand side of ~ logsqvma2 . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 23-May-2016.)
theorem selberglem3 {x3 y1 n d: setvar}:
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 crp (co (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (csu d (crab y1 (wbr (cv y1) (cv n) cdvds) cn) (co (cfv (cv d) cmu) (co (cfv (co (cv n) (cv d) cdiv) clog) c2 cexp) cmul))) (cv x3) cdiv) (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) cmin)) co1 $;

--| Selberg's symmetry formula. The statement has many forms, and this one is equivalent to the statement that ` sum_ n <_ x , Lam ( n ) log n + ` ` sum_ m x. n <_ x , Lam ( m ) Lam ( n ) = 2 x log x + O ( x ) ` . Equation 10.4.10 of [Shapiro], p. 419. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 23-May-2016.)
theorem selberg {x3 n: setvar}:
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 crp (co (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (co (cfv (cv n) clog) (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) cchp) caddc) cmul)) (cv x3) cdiv) (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) cmin)) co1 $;

--| Convert eventual boundedness in ~ selberg to boundedness on ` [ 1 , +oo ) ` . (We have to bound away from zero because the log terms diverge at zero.) (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem selbergb {x3 n c: setvar}:
  $ wrex c (wral x3 (wbr (cfv (co (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (co (cfv (cv n) clog) (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) cchp) caddc) cmul)) (cv x3) cdiv) (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) cmin) cabs) (cv c) cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) crp $;

--| Lemma for ~ selberg2 . Equation 10.4.12 of [Shapiro], p. 420. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 23-May-2016.)
theorem selberg2lem {x3 n: setvar}:
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 crp (co (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cfv (cv n) clog) cmul)) (co (cfv (cv x3) cchp) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) cmin) (cv x3) cdiv)) co1 $;

--| Selberg's symmetry formula, using the second Chebyshev function. Equation 10.4.14 of [Shapiro], p. 420. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 23-May-2016.)
theorem selberg2 {x3 n: setvar}:
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 crp (co (co (co (co (cfv (cv x3) cchp) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) cchp) cmul)) caddc) (cv x3) cdiv) (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) cmin)) co1 $;

--| Convert eventual boundedness in ~ selberg2 to boundedness on any interval ` [ A , +oo ) ` . (We have to bound away from zero because the log terms diverge at zero.) (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-May-2016.)
theorem selberg2b {x3 n c: setvar}:
  $ wrex c (wral x3 (wbr (cfv (co (co (co (co (cfv (cv x3) cchp) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) cchp) cmul)) caddc) (cv x3) cdiv) (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) cmin) cabs) (cv c) cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) crp $;

--| Lemma for ~ chpdifbnd . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-May-2016.)
theorem chpdifbndlem1 {z m: setvar} (ph: wff z m) (A2: class z m) (B2: class m) (C: class) (X Y: class m):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr c1 A2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral z (wbr (cfv (co (co (co (co (cfv (cv z) cchp) (cfv (cv z) clog) cmul) (csu m (co c1 (cfv (cv z) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv m) cvma) (cfv (co (cv z) (cv m) cdiv) cchp) cmul)) caddc) (cv z) cdiv) (co c2 (cfv (cv z) clog) cmul) cmin) cabs) B2 cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wceq C (co (co B2 (co A2 c1 caddc) cmul) (co (co c2 A2 cmul) (cfv A2 clog) cmul) caddc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X (co c1 cpnf cioo)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y (co X (co A2 X cmul) cicc)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co (cfv Y cchp) (cfv X cchp) cmin) (co (co c2 (co Y X cmin) cmul) (co C (co X (cfv X clog) cdiv) cmul) caddc) cle) $;

--| Lemma for ~ chpdifbnd . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-May-2016.)
theorem chpdifbndlem2 {x3 y1 z m c: setvar} (ph: wff z m c) (A2: class x3 y1 z m) (B2: class x3 y1 m c) (C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr c1 A2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral z (wbr (cfv (co (co (co (co (cfv (cv z) cchp) (cfv (cv z) clog) cmul) (csu m (co c1 (cfv (cv z) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv m) cvma) (cfv (co (cv z) (cv m) cdiv) cchp) cmul)) caddc) (cv z) cdiv) (co c2 (cfv (cv z) clog) cmul) cmin) cabs) B2 cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wceq C (co (co B2 (co A2 c1 caddc) cmul) (co (co c2 A2 cmul) (cfv A2 clog) cmul) caddc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wrex c (wral x3 (wral y1 (wbr (co (cfv (cv y1) cchp) (cfv (cv x3) cchp) cmin) (co (co c2 (co (cv y1) (cv x3) cmin) cmul) (co (cv c) (co (cv x3) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) cmul) caddc) cle) (co (cv x3) (co A2 (cv x3) cmul) cicc)) (co c1 cpnf cioo)) crp) $;

--| A bound on the difference of nearby ` psi ` values. Theorem 10.5.2 of [Shapiro], p. 427. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-May-2016.)
theorem chpdifbnd {x3 y1 c: setvar} (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr c1 A2 cle)) (wrex c (wral x3 (wral y1 (wbr (co (cfv (cv y1) cchp) (cfv (cv x3) cchp) cmin) (co (co c2 (co (cv y1) (cv x3) cmin) cmul) (co (cv c) (co (cv x3) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) cmul) caddc) cle) (co (cv x3) (co A2 (cv x3) cmul) cicc)) (co c1 cpnf cioo)) crp) $;

--| A bound on a sum of logs, used in ~ pntlemk . This is not as precise as ~ logdivsum in its asymptotic behavior, but it is valid for all ` N ` and does not require a limit value. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Apr-2016.)
theorem logdivbnd {n: setvar} (N: class):
  $ wi (wcel N cn) (wbr (csu n (co c1 N cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) clog) (cv n) cdiv)) (co (co (co (cfv N clog) c1 caddc) c2 cexp) c2 cdiv) cle) $;

--| Introduce a log weighting on the summands of ` sum_ m x. n <_ x , Lam ( m ) Lam ( n ) ` , the core of ~ selberg2 (written here as ` sum_ n <_ x , Lam ( n ) psi ( x / n ) ` ). Equation 10.4.21 of [Shapiro], p. 422. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem selberg3lem1 {x3 y1 k n: setvar} (ph: wff y1 k) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (co (csu k (co c1 (cfv (cv y1) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv k) cvma) (cfv (cv k) clog) cmul)) (co (cfv (cv y1) cchp) (cfv (cv y1) clog) cmul) cmin) (cv y1) cdiv) cabs) A2 cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (co (co (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) cchp) cmul) (cfv (cv n) clog) cmul)) cmul) (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) cchp) cmul)) cmin) (cv x3) cdiv)) co1) $;

--| Lemma for ~ selberg3 . Equation 10.4.21 of [Shapiro], p. 422. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem selberg3lem2 {x3 n: setvar}:
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (co (co (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) cchp) cmul) (cfv (cv n) clog) cmul)) cmul) (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) cchp) cmul)) cmin) (cv x3) cdiv)) co1 $;

--| Introduce a log weighting on the summands of ` sum_ m x. n <_ x , Lam ( m ) Lam ( n ) ` , the core of ~ selberg2 (written here as ` sum_ n <_ x , Lam ( n ) psi ( x / n ) ` ). Equation 10.6.7 of [Shapiro], p. 422. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem selberg3 {x3 n: setvar}:
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (co (co (co (cfv (cv x3) cchp) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) (co (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) cchp) cmul) (cfv (cv n) clog) cmul)) cmul) caddc) (cv x3) cdiv) (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) cmin)) co1 $;

--| Lemma for ~ selberg4 . Equation 10.4.20 of [Shapiro], p. 422. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem selberg4lem1 {x3 y1 i m n: setvar} (ph: wff y1 i) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (co (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv y1) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) cvma) (co (cfv (cv i) clog) (cfv (co (cv y1) (cv i) cdiv) cchp) caddc) cmul)) (cv y1) cdiv) (co c2 (cfv (cv y1) clog) cmul) cmin) cabs) A2 cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (csu m (co c1 (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv m) cvma) (co (cfv (cv m) clog) (cfv (co (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) (cv m) cdiv) cchp) caddc) cmul)) cmul)) (co (cv x3) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) cdiv) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmin)) co1) $;

--| The Selberg symmetry formula for products of three primes, instead of two. The sum here can also be written in the symmetric form ` sum_ i j k <_ x , Lam ( i ) Lam ( j ) Lam ( k ) ` ; we eliminate one of the nested sums by using the definition of ` psi ( x ) = sum_ k <_ x , Lam ( k ) ` . This statement can thus equivalently be written ` psi ( x ) log ^ 2 ( x ) = ` ` 2 sum_ i j k <_ x , Lam ( i ) Lam ( j ) Lam ( k ) + O ( x log x ) ` . Equation 10.4.23 of [Shapiro], p. 422. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem selberg4 {x3 m n: setvar}:
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (co (co (cfv (cv x3) cchp) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) (co (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (csu m (co c1 (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv m) cvma) (cfv (co (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) (cv m) cdiv) cchp) cmul)) cmul)) cmul) cmin) (cv x3) cdiv)) co1 $;

--| Define the residual of the second Chebyshev function. The goal is to have ` R ( x ) e. o ( x ) ` , or ` R ( x ) / x ~~>r 0 ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 8-Apr-2016.)
theorem pntrval {a: setvar} (A2: class) (R: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi (wcel A2 crp) (wceq (cfv A2 R) (co (cfv A2 cchp) A2 cmin)) $;

--| Functionality of the residual. Lemma for ~ pnt . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 8-Apr-2016.)
theorem pntrf {a: setvar} (R: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wf crp cr R $;

--| There is a bound on the residual valid for all ` x ` . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 9-Apr-2016.)
theorem pntrmax {x3 a c: setvar} (R: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wrex c (wral x3 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cv x3) R) (cv x3) cdiv) cabs) (cv c) cle) crp) crp $;

--| A bound on a sum over ` R ` . Equation 10.1.16 of [Shapiro], p. 403. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-May-2016.)
theorem pntrsumo1 {x3 n a: setvar} (R: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 cr (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) R) (co (cv n) (co (cv n) c1 caddc) cmul) cdiv))) co1 $;

--| A bound on a sum over ` R ` . Equation 10.1.16 of [Shapiro], p. 403. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-May-2016.)
theorem pntrsumbnd {m n a c: setvar} (R: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wrex c (wral m (wbr (cfv (csu n (co c1 (cv m) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) R) (co (cv n) (co (cv n) c1 caddc) cmul) cdiv)) cabs) (cv c) cle) cz) crp $;

--| A bound on a sum over ` R ` . Equation 10.1.16 of [Shapiro], p. 403. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 14-Apr-2016.)
theorem pntrsumbnd2 {k m n a c: setvar} (R: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wrex c (wral k (wral m (wbr (cfv (csu n (co (cv k) (cv m) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) R) (co (cv n) (co (cv n) c1 caddc) cmul) cdiv)) cabs) (cv c) cle) cz) cn) crp $;

--| Selberg's symmetry formula, using the residual of the second Chebyshev function. Equation 10.6.2 of [Shapiro], p. 428. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 16-Apr-2016.)
theorem selbergr {x3 a d: setvar} (R: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 crp (co (co (co (cfv (cv x3) R) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) (csu d (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv d) cvma) (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv d) cdiv) R) cmul)) caddc) (cv x3) cdiv)) co1 $;

--| Selberg's symmetry formula, using the residual of the second Chebyshev function. Equation 10.6.8 of [Shapiro], p. 429. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem selberg3r {x3 n a: setvar} (R: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (co (co (cfv (cv x3) R) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) (co (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) R) cmul) (cfv (cv n) clog) cmul)) cmul) caddc) (cv x3) cdiv)) co1 $;

--| Selberg's symmetry formula, using the residual of the second Chebyshev function. Equation 10.6.11 of [Shapiro], p. 430. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem selberg4r {x3 m n a: setvar} (R: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (co (co (cfv (cv x3) R) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) (co (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (csu m (co c1 (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv m) cvma) (cfv (co (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) (cv m) cdiv) R) cmul)) cmul)) cmul) cmin) (cv x3) cdiv)) co1 $;

--| The sum of ~ selberg3r and ~ selberg4r . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 31-May-2016.)
theorem selberg34r {x3 y1 m n a: setvar} (R: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (co (co (cfv (cv x3) R) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) R) (co (csu m (crab y1 (wbr (cv y1) (cv n) cdvds) cn) (co (cfv (cv m) cvma) (cfv (co (cv n) (cv m) cdiv) cvma) cmul)) (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cfv (cv n) clog) cmul) cmin) cmul)) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) cmin) (cv x3) cdiv)) co1 $;

--| Define the "Selberg function", whose asymptotic behavior is the content of ~ selberg . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 31-May-2016.)
theorem pntsval {i n a: setvar} (A2: class) (S: class i a):
  $ wceq S (cmpt a cr (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv a) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) cvma) (co (cfv (cv i) clog) (cfv (co (cv a) (cv i) cdiv) cchp) caddc) cmul))) $ >
  $ wi (wcel A2 cr) (wceq (cfv A2 S) (csu n (co c1 (cfv A2 cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (co (cfv (cv n) clog) (cfv (co A2 (cv n) cdiv) cchp) caddc) cmul))) $;

--| Functionality of the Selberg function. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 31-May-2016.)
theorem pntsf {i a: setvar} (S: class i a):
  $ wceq S (cmpt a cr (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv a) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) cvma) (co (cfv (cv i) clog) (cfv (co (cv a) (cv i) cdiv) cchp) caddc) cmul))) $ >
  $ wf cr cr S $;

--| Selberg's symmetry formula, using the definition of the Selberg function. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 31-May-2016.)
theorem selbergs {x3 i a: setvar} (S: class i a):
  $ wceq S (cmpt a cr (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv a) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) cvma) (co (cfv (cv i) clog) (cfv (co (cv a) (cv i) cdiv) cchp) caddc) cmul))) $ >
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 crp (co (co (cfv (cv x3) S) (cv x3) cdiv) (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) cmin)) co1 $;

--| Selberg's symmetry formula, using the definition of the Selberg function. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 31-May-2016.)
theorem selbergsb {x3 i a c: setvar} (S: class i a):
  $ wceq S (cmpt a cr (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv a) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) cvma) (co (cfv (cv i) clog) (cfv (co (cv a) (cv i) cdiv) cchp) caddc) cmul))) $ >
  $ wrex c (wral x3 (wbr (cfv (co (co (cfv (cv x3) S) (cv x3) cdiv) (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) cmin) cabs) (cv c) cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) crp $;

--| The Selberg function can be expressed using the convolution product of the von Mangoldt function with itself. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 31-May-2016.)
theorem pntsval2 {y1 i m n a: setvar} (A2: class) (S: class i a):
  $ wceq S (cmpt a cr (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv a) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) cvma) (co (cfv (cv i) clog) (cfv (co (cv a) (cv i) cdiv) cchp) caddc) cmul))) $ >
  $ wi (wcel A2 cr) (wceq (cfv A2 S) (csu n (co c1 (cfv A2 cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cv n) cvma) (cfv (cv n) clog) cmul) (csu m (crab y1 (wbr (cv y1) (cv n) cdvds) cn) (co (cfv (cv m) cvma) (cfv (co (cv n) (cv m) cdiv) cvma) cmul)) caddc))) $;

--| The sum of ~ selberg3r and ~ selberg4r . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 31-May-2016.)
theorem pntrlog2bndlem1 {x3 i n a: setvar} (R S: class i a):
  $ wceq S (cmpt a cr (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv a) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) cvma) (co (cfv (cv i) clog) (cfv (co (cv a) (cv i) cdiv) cchp) caddc) cmul))) $ >
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (co (co (cfv (cfv (cv x3) R) cabs) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) R) cabs) (co (cfv (cv n) S) (cfv (co (cv n) c1 cmin) S) cmin) cmul)) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) cmin) (cv x3) cdiv)) clo1 $;

--| Lemma for ~ pntrlog2bnd . Bound on the difference between the Selberg function and its approximation, inside a sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 31-May-2016.)
theorem pntrlog2bndlem2 {x3 y1 i n a: setvar} (ph: wff y1 i a) (A2: class) (R S: class i a):
  $ wceq S (cmpt a cr (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv a) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) cvma) (co (cfv (cv i) clog) (cfv (co (cv a) (cv i) cdiv) cchp) caddc) cmul))) $ >
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (cv y1) cchp) (co A2 (cv y1) cmul) cle) crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cv n) (cfv (co (cfv (co (cv x3) (co (cv n) c1 caddc) cdiv) R) (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) R) cmin) cabs) cmul)) (co (cv x3) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) cdiv)) co1) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pntrlog2bnd . Bound on the difference between the Selberg function and its approximation, inside a sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 31-May-2016.)
theorem pntrlog2bndlem3 {x3 y1 i n a: setvar} (ph: wff y1 i a) (A2: class) (R S: class i a):
  $ wceq S (cmpt a cr (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv a) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) cvma) (co (cfv (cv i) clog) (cfv (co (cv a) (cv i) cdiv) cchp) caddc) cmul))) $ >
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (co (cfv (cv y1) S) (cv y1) cdiv) (co c2 (cfv (cv y1) clog) cmul) cmin) cabs) A2 cle) (co c1 cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) R) cabs) (cfv (cfv (co (cv x3) (co (cv n) c1 caddc) cdiv) R) cabs) cmin) (co (cfv (cv n) S) (co c2 (co (cv n) (cfv (cv n) clog) cmul) cmul) cmin) cmul)) (co (cv x3) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) cdiv)) co1) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pntrlog2bnd . Bound on the difference between the Selberg function and its approximation, inside a sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 31-May-2016.)
theorem pntrlog2bndlem4 {x3 i n a: setvar} (R S: class i a) (T: class x3 i a):
  $ wceq S (cmpt a cr (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv a) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) cvma) (co (cfv (cv i) clog) (cfv (co (cv a) (cv i) cdiv) cchp) caddc) cmul))) $ >
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpt a cr (cif (wcel (cv a) crp) (co (cv a) (cfv (cv a) clog) cmul) cc0)) $ >
  $ wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (co (co (cfv (cfv (cv x3) R) cabs) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) (co (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) R) cabs) (co (cfv (cv n) T) (cfv (co (cv n) c1 cmin) T) cmin) cmul)) cmul) cmin) (cv x3) cdiv)) clo1 $;

--| Lemma for ~ pntrlog2bnd . Bound on the difference between the Selberg function and its approximation, inside a sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 31-May-2016.)
theorem pntrlog2bndlem5 {x3 y1 i n a: setvar} (ph: wff y1 i a) (B2 R S: class i a) (T: class x3 y1 i a):
  $ wceq S (cmpt a cr (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv a) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) cvma) (co (cfv (cv i) clog) (cfv (co (cv a) (cv i) cdiv) cchp) caddc) cmul))) $ >
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpt a cr (cif (wcel (cv a) crp) (co (cv a) (cfv (cv a) clog) cmul) cc0)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cv y1) R) (cv y1) cdiv) cabs) B2 cle) crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (co (co (cfv (cfv (cv x3) R) cabs) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) (co (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) (csu n (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) R) cabs) (cfv (cv n) clog) cmul)) cmul) cmin) (cv x3) cdiv)) clo1) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pntrlog2bndlem6 . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 7-Jun-2016.)
theorem pntrlog2bndlem6a {y1 i a: setvar} (ph: wff y1 i a) (x3: setvar) (A2: class) (B2 R S: class i a) (T: class y1 i a):
  $ wceq S (cmpt a cr (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv a) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) cvma) (co (cfv (cv i) clog) (cfv (co (cv a) (cv i) cdiv) cchp) caddc) cmul))) $ >
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpt a cr (cif (wcel (cv a) crp) (co (cv a) (cfv (cv a) clog) cmul) cc0)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cv y1) R) (cv y1) cdiv) cabs) B2 cle) crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr c1 A2 cle) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv x3) (co c1 cpnf cioo))) (wceq (co c1 (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz) (cun (co c1 (cfv (co (cv x3) A2 cdiv) cfl) cfz) (co (co (cfv (co (cv x3) A2 cdiv) cfl) c1 caddc) (cfv (cv x3) cfl) cfz))) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pntrlog2bnd . Bound on the difference between the Selberg function and its approximation, inside a sum. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 31-May-2016.)
theorem pntrlog2bndlem6 {x3 y1 i n a: setvar} (ph: wff y1 i a) (A2: class) (B2 R S: class i a) (T: class x3 y1 i a):
  $ wceq S (cmpt a cr (csu i (co c1 (cfv (cv a) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cv i) cvma) (co (cfv (cv i) clog) (cfv (co (cv a) (cv i) cdiv) cchp) caddc) cmul))) $ >
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wceq T (cmpt a cr (cif (wcel (cv a) crp) (co (cv a) (cfv (cv a) clog) cmul) cc0)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral y1 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cv y1) R) (cv y1) cdiv) cabs) B2 cle) crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr c1 A2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cmpt x3 (co c1 cpnf cioo) (co (co (co (cfv (cfv (cv x3) R) cabs) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) (co (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) (csu n (co c1 (cfv (co (cv x3) A2 cdiv) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) R) cabs) (cfv (cv n) clog) cmul)) cmul) cmin) (cv x3) cdiv)) clo1) $;

--| A bound on ` R ( x ) log ^ 2 ( x ) ` . Equation 10.6.15 of [Shapiro], p. 431. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 1-Jun-2016.)
theorem pntrlog2bnd {x3 n a c: setvar} (A2: class) (R: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr c1 A2 cle)) (wrex c (wral x3 (wbr (co (co (co (cfv (cfv (cv x3) R) cabs) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cmul) (co (co c2 (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) (csu n (co c1 (cfv (co (cv x3) A2 cdiv) cfl) cfz) (co (cfv (cfv (co (cv x3) (cv n) cdiv) R) cabs) (cfv (cv n) clog) cmul)) cmul) cmin) (cv x3) cdiv) (cv c) cle) (co c1 cpnf cioo)) crp) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pntpbnd . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Apr-2016.) Replace reference to OLD theorem. (Revised by Wolf Lammen, 8-Sep-2020.)
theorem pntpbnd1a {a: setvar} (ph: wff a) (R E K: class a) (N: class) (X Y: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E (co cc0 c1 cioo)) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv (co c2 E cdiv) ce) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y (co X cpnf cioo)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wbr Y N clt) (wbr N (co K Y cmul) cle)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cfv (cfv N R) cabs) (cfv (co (cfv (co N c1 caddc) R) (cfv N R) cmin) cabs) cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cfv (co (cfv N R) N cdiv) cabs) E cle) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pntpbnd . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Apr-2016.)
theorem pntpbnd1 {y1 i j n a: setvar} (ph: wff y1 i j a) (A2: class) (C: class y1 i j n a) (R: class a) (E: class i j a) (K: class a) (X: class y1 i j n a) (Y: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E (co cc0 c1 cioo)) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv (co c2 E cdiv) ce) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y (co X cpnf cioo)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral i (wral j (wbr (cfv (csu y1 (co (cv i) (cv j) cfz) (co (cfv (cv y1) R) (co (cv y1) (co (cv y1) c1 caddc) cmul) cdiv)) cabs) A2 cle) cz) cn) $ >
  $ wceq C (co A2 c2 caddc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K (co (cfv (co C E cdiv) ce) cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn (wrex y1 (wa (wa (wbr Y (cv y1) clt) (wbr (cv y1) (co K Y cmul) cle)) (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cv y1) R) (cv y1) cdiv) cabs) E cle)) cn)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (csu n (co (co (cfv Y cfl) c1 caddc) (cfv (co K Y cmul) cfl) cfz) (cfv (co (cfv (cv n) R) (co (cv n) (co (cv n) c1 caddc) cmul) cdiv) cabs)) A2 cle) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pntpbnd . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-Apr-2016.)
theorem pntpbnd2 {y1 i j a: setvar} (ph: wff y1 i j a) (A2: class) (C: class y1 i j a) (R: class a) (E: class i j a) (K: class a) (X: class y1 i j a) (Y: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E (co cc0 c1 cioo)) $ >
  $ wceq X (cfv (co c2 E cdiv) ce) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y (co X cpnf cioo)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral i (wral j (wbr (cfv (csu y1 (co (cv i) (cv j) cfz) (co (cfv (cv y1) R) (co (cv y1) (co (cv y1) c1 caddc) cmul) cdiv)) cabs) A2 cle) cz) cn) $ >
  $ wceq C (co A2 c2 caddc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K (co (cfv (co C E cdiv) ce) cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn (wrex y1 (wa (wa (wbr Y (cv y1) clt) (wbr (cv y1) (co K Y cmul) cle)) (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cv y1) R) (cv y1) cdiv) cabs) E cle)) cn)) $ >
  $ wn ph $;

--| Lemma for ~ pnt . Establish smallness of ` R ` at a point. Lemma 10.6.1 in [Shapiro], p. 436. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 10-Apr-2016.)
theorem pntpbnd {x3 y1 e k n a c: setvar} (R: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wrex c (wral e (wrex x3 (wral k (wral y1 (wrex n (wa (wa (wbr (cv y1) (cv n) clt) (wbr (cv n) (co (cv k) (cv y1) cmul) cle)) (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cv n) R) (cv n) cdiv) cabs) (cv e) cle)) cn) (co (cv x3) cpnf cioo)) (co (cfv (co (cv c) (cv e) cdiv) ce) cpnf cico)) crp) (co cc0 c1 cioo)) crp $;

--| Lemma for ~ pntibnd . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 10-Apr-2016.)
theorem pntibndlem1 {a: setvar} (ph: wff a) (A2 R L: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wceq L (co (co c1 c4 cdiv) (co A2 c3 caddc) cdiv) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel L (co cc0 c1 cioo)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pntibndlem2 . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 7-Jun-2016.)
theorem pntibndlem2a {x3 a: setvar} (ph: wff x3 a) (u: setvar) (A2: class a) (B2: class x3 a) (C R: class a) (E: class) (K: class x3 a) (L: class a) (N: class) (Z: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wceq L (co (co c1 c4 cdiv) (co A2 c3 caddc) cdiv) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral x3 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cv x3) R) (cv x3) cdiv) cabs) A2 cle) crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 crp) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv (co B2 (co E c2 cdiv) cdiv) ce) $ >
  $ wceq C (co (co c2 B2 cmul) (cfv c2 clog) caddc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E (co cc0 c1 cioo)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel (cv u) (co N (co (co c1 (co L E cmul) caddc) N cmul) cicc))) (w3a (wcel (cv u) cr) (wbr N (cv u) cle) (wbr (cv u) (co (co c1 (co L E cmul) caddc) N cmul) cle)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pntibnd . The main work, after eliminating all the quantifiers. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 10-Apr-2016.)
theorem pntibndlem2 {x3 y1 z u a: setvar} (ph: wff x3 y1 z a) (A2: class y1 z a) (B2: class x3 y1 z u a) (C: class z a) (R: class a) (T: class z u a) (E: class) (K: class x3 y1 z u a) (L: class y1 a) (M: class x3 y1 u a) (N: class) (X: class x3 y1 z u a) (Y: class x3 y1 u a) (Z: class z a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wceq L (co (co c1 c4 cdiv) (co A2 c3 caddc) cdiv) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral x3 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cv x3) R) (cv x3) cdiv) cabs) A2 cle) crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 crp) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv (co B2 (co E c2 cdiv) cdiv) ce) $ >
  $ wceq C (co (co c2 B2 cmul) (cfv c2 clog) caddc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E (co cc0 c1 cioo)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel N cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel T crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral x3 (wral y1 (wbr (co (cfv (cv y1) cchp) (cfv (cv x3) cchp) cmin) (co (co c2 (co (cv y1) (cv x3) cmin) cmul) (co T (co (cv x3) (cfv (cv x3) clog) cdiv) cmul) caddc) cle) (co (cv x3) (co c2 (cv x3) cmul) cicc)) (co c1 cpnf cioo)) $ >
  $ wceq X (co (cfv (co T (co E c4 cdiv) cdiv) ce) Z caddc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel M (co (cfv (co C E cdiv) ce) cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y (co X cpnf cioo)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wa (wbr Y N clt) (wbr N (co (co M c2 cdiv) Y cmul) cle)) (wbr (cfv (co (cfv N R) N cdiv) cabs) (co E c2 cdiv) cle)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wrex z (wa (wa (wbr Y (cv z) clt) (wbr (co (co c1 (co L E cmul) caddc) (cv z) cmul) (co M Y cmul) clt)) (wral u (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cv u) R) (cv u) cdiv) cabs) E cle) (co (cv z) (co (co c1 (co L E cmul) caddc) (cv z) cmul) cicc))) crp) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pntibnd . Package up ~ pntibndlem2 in quantifiers. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 10-Apr-2016.)
theorem pntibndlem3 {x3 y1 z v u i k m a: setvar} (ph: wff x3 z v i m a) (A2: class y1 z i k m a) (B2: class x3 y1 z v u i k m a) (C: class z i k m a) (R: class a) (E: class) (K: class x3 y1 z v u i k a) (L: class y1 i k m a) (Z: class z i a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wceq L (co (co c1 c4 cdiv) (co A2 c3 caddc) cdiv) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral x3 (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cv x3) R) (cv x3) cdiv) cabs) A2 cle) crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 crp) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv (co B2 (co E c2 cdiv) cdiv) ce) $ >
  $ wceq C (co (co c2 B2 cmul) (cfv c2 clog) caddc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E (co cc0 c1 cioo)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral m (wral v (wrex i (wa (wa (wbr (cv v) (cv i) clt) (wbr (cv i) (co (cv m) (cv v) cmul) cle)) (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cv i) R) (cv i) cdiv) cabs) (co E c2 cdiv) cle)) cn) (co Z cpnf cioo)) (co K cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wrex x3 (wral k (wral y1 (wrex z (wa (wa (wbr (cv y1) (cv z) clt) (wbr (co (co c1 (co L E cmul) caddc) (cv z) cmul) (co (cv k) (cv y1) cmul) clt)) (wral u (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cv u) R) (cv u) cdiv) cabs) E cle) (co (cv z) (co (co c1 (co L E cmul) caddc) (cv z) cmul) cicc))) crp) (co (cv x3) cpnf cioo)) (co (cfv (co C E cdiv) ce) cpnf cico)) crp) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pnt . Establish smallness of ` R ` on an interval. Lemma 10.6.2 in [Shapiro], p. 436. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 10-Apr-2016.)
theorem pntibnd {x3 y1 z u e k a c l: setvar} (R: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wrex c (wrex l (wral e (wrex x3 (wral k (wral y1 (wrex z (wa (wa (wbr (cv y1) (cv z) clt) (wbr (co (co c1 (co (cv l) (cv e) cmul) caddc) (cv z) cmul) (co (cv k) (cv y1) cmul) clt)) (wral u (wbr (cfv (co (cfv (cv u) R) (cv u) cdiv) cabs) (cv e) cle) (co (cv z) (co (co c1 (co (cv l) (cv e) cmul) caddc) (cv z) cmul) cicc))) crp) (co (cv x3) cpnf cioo)) (co (cfv (co (cv c) (cv e) cdiv) ce) cpnf cico)) crp) (co cc0 c1 cioo)) (co cc0 c1 cioo)) crp $;

--| Lemma for ~ pnt . Closure for the constants used in the proof. For comparison with Equation 10.6.27 of [Shapiro], p. 434, ` A ` is C^*, ` B ` is c_1, ` L ` is &lambda;, ` D ` is c_2, and ` F ` is c_3. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Apr-2016.)
theorem pntlemd {a: setvar} (ph: wff a) (A2 B2 D R F L: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel L (co cc0 c1 cioo)) $ >
  $ wceq D (co A2 c1 caddc) $ >
  $ wceq F (co (co c1 (co c1 D cdiv) cmin) (co (co L (co (cdc c3 c2) B2 cmul) cdiv) (co D c2 cexp) cdiv) cmul) $ >
  $ wi ph (w3a (wcel L crp) (wcel D crp) (wcel F crp)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pnt . Closure for the constants used in the proof. For comparison with Equation 10.6.27 of [Shapiro], p. 434, ` U ` is &alpha;, ` E ` is &epsilon;, and ` K ` is _K_. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Apr-2016.)
theorem pntlemc {a: setvar} (ph: wff a) (A2 B2 D R U: class a) (E: class) (F K L: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel L (co cc0 c1 cioo)) $ >
  $ wceq D (co A2 c1 caddc) $ >
  $ wceq F (co (co c1 (co c1 D cdiv) cmin) (co (co L (co (cdc c3 c2) B2 cmul) cdiv) (co D c2 cexp) cdiv) cmul) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr U A2 cle) $ >
  $ wceq E (co U D cdiv) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv (co B2 E cdiv) ce) $ >
  $ wi ph (w3a (wcel E crp) (wcel K crp) (w3a (wcel E (co cc0 c1 cioo)) (wbr c1 K clt) (wcel (co U E cmin) crp))) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pnt . Closure for the constants used in the proof. The mammoth expression ` W ` is a number large enough to satisfy all the lower bounds needed for ` Z ` . For comparison with Equation 10.6.27 of [Shapiro], p. 434, ` Y ` is x_2, ` X ` is x_1, ` C ` is the big-O constant in Equation 10.6.29 of [Shapiro], p. 435, and ` W ` is the unnamed lower bound of "for sufficiently large x" in Equation 10.6.34 of [Shapiro], p. 436. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Apr-2016.)
theorem pntlema {a: setvar} (ph: wff a) (A2 B2 C D R U: class a) (E: class) (F K L W X Y: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel L (co cc0 c1 cioo)) $ >
  $ wceq D (co A2 c1 caddc) $ >
  $ wceq F (co (co c1 (co c1 D cdiv) cmin) (co (co L (co (cdc c3 c2) B2 cmul) cdiv) (co D c2 cexp) cdiv) cmul) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr U A2 cle) $ >
  $ wceq E (co U D cdiv) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv (co B2 E cdiv) ce) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel Y crp) (wbr c1 Y cle)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel X crp) (wbr Y X clt)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C crp) $ >
  $ wceq W (co (co (co Y (co c4 (co L E cmul) cdiv) caddc) c2 cexp) (co (co (co X (co K c2 cexp) cmul) c4 cexp) (cfv (co (co (co (cdc c3 c2) B2 cmul) (co (co U E cmin) (co L (co E c2 cexp) cmul) cmul) cdiv) (co (co U c3 cmul) C caddc) cmul) ce) caddc) caddc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel W crp) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pnt . Unpack all the lower bounds contained in ` W ` , in the form they will be used. For comparison with Equation 10.6.27 of [Shapiro], p. 434, ` Z ` is x. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Apr-2016.)
theorem pntlemb {a: setvar} (ph: wff a) (A2 B2 C D R U: class a) (E: class) (F K L W X Y Z: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel L (co cc0 c1 cioo)) $ >
  $ wceq D (co A2 c1 caddc) $ >
  $ wceq F (co (co c1 (co c1 D cdiv) cmin) (co (co L (co (cdc c3 c2) B2 cmul) cdiv) (co D c2 cexp) cdiv) cmul) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U crp) $ >
