  $ wceq E (co U D cdiv) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv (co B2 E cdiv) ce) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel Y crp) (wbr c1 Y cle)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel X crp) (wbr Y X clt)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C crp) $ >
  $ wceq W (co (co (co Y (co c4 (co L E cmul) cdiv) caddc) c2 cexp) (co (co (co X (co K c2 cexp) cmul) c4 cexp) (cfv (co (co (co (cdc c3 c2) B2 cmul) (co (co U E cmin) (co L (co E c2 cexp) cmul) cmul) cdiv) (co (co U c3 cmul) C caddc) cmul) ce) caddc) caddc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z (co W cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wi ph (w3a (wcel Z crp) (w3a (wbr c1 Z clt) (wbr ceu (cfv Z csqrt) cle) (wbr (cfv Z csqrt) (co Z Y cdiv) cle)) (w3a (wbr (co c4 (co L E cmul) cdiv) (cfv Z csqrt) cle) (wbr (co (co (cfv X clog) (cfv K clog) cdiv) c2 caddc) (co (co (cfv Z clog) (cfv K clog) cdiv) c4 cdiv) cle) (wbr (co (co U c3 cmul) C caddc) (co (co (co U E cmin) (co (co L (co E c2 cexp) cmul) (co (cdc c3 c2) B2 cmul) cdiv) cmul) (cfv Z clog) cmul) cle))) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pnt . Closure for the constants used in the proof. For comparison with Equation 10.6.27 of [Shapiro], p. 434, ` M ` is j^* and ` N ` is &#309;. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Apr-2016.)
theorem pntlemg {a: setvar} (ph: wff a) (A2 B2 C D R U: class a) (E: class) (F K L M N W X Y Z: class a):
  $ wceq R (cmpt a crp (co (cfv (cv a) cchp) (cv a) cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel L (co cc0 c1 cioo)) $ >
  $ wceq D (co A2 c1 caddc) $ >
  $ wceq F (co (co c1 (co c1 D cdiv) cmin) (co (co L (co (cdc c3 c2) B2 cmul) cdiv) (co D c2 cexp) cdiv) cmul) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel U crp) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr U A2 cle) $ >
  $ wceq E (co U D cdiv) $ >
  $ wceq K (cfv (co B2 E cdiv) ce) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel Y crp) (wbr c1 Y cle)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel X crp) (wbr Y X clt)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C crp) $ >
  $ wceq W (co (co (co Y (co c4 (co L E cmul) cdiv) caddc) c2 cexp) (co (co (co X (co K c2 cexp) cmul) c4 cexp) (cfv (co (co (co (cdc c3 c2) B2 cmul) (co (co U E cmin) (co L (co E c2 cexp) cmul) cmul) cdiv) (co (co U c3 cmul) C caddc) cmul) ce) caddc) caddc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Z (co W cpnf cico)) $ >
  $ wceq M (co (cfv (co (cfv X clog) (cfv K clog) cdiv) cfl) c1 caddc) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv (co (co (cfv Z clog) (cfv K clog) cdiv) c2 cdiv) cfl) $ >
  $ wi ph (w3a (wcel M cn) (wcel N (cfv M cuz)) (wbr (co (co (cfv Z clog) (cfv K clog) cdiv) c4 cdiv) (co N M cmin) cle)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pnt . Bounds on the subintervals in the induction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Apr-2016.)
