  $ wi ph (wbr (co (co U E cmin) (co (co (co L E cmul) c8 cdiv) (cfv Z clog) cmul) cmul) (co (cfv I chash) (co (co U E cmin) (co (cfv (co Z V cdiv) clog) (co Z V cdiv) cdiv) cmul) cmul) cle) $;

--| Lemma for ~ pnt . The induction step. Using ~ pntibnd , we find an interval in ` K ^ J ... K ^ ( J + 1 ) ` which is sufficiently large and has a much smaller value, ` R ( z ) / z <_ E ` (instead of our original bound ` R ( z ) / z <_ U ` ). (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 13-Apr-2016.)
theorem pntlemj {y1 z u n a: setvar} (ph: wff y1 z u a) (A2 B2: class y1 z u n a) (C: class y1 u n a) (D: class y1 z u n a) (R: class a) (U: class y1 u a) (E: class) (F: class y1 z u n a) (I: class y1 z u a) (J K: class u a) (L: class a) (M N O: class y1 u a) (V: class y1 z a) (W: class y1 u a) (X: class u a) (Y: class y1 u a) (Z: class y1 a):
