theorem mulsproplem10 {w v u t e f2 g2 h i j s1 r q p a b c d: setvar} (ph: wff e f2 a b c d) (A2 B2: class) (C D E F: class w v u t g2 h i j s1 r q p):
  $ wi ph (wral a (wral b (wral c (wral d (wral e (wral f2 (wi (wcel (cun (co (cfv (cv a) cbday) (cfv (cv b) cbday) cnadd) (cun (cun (co (cfv (cv c) cbday) (cfv (cv e) cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv (cv d) cbday) (cfv (cv f2) cbday) cnadd)) (cun (co (cfv (cv c) cbday) (cfv (cv f2) cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv (cv d) cbday) (cfv (cv e) cbday) cnadd)))) (cun (co (cfv A2 cbday) (cfv B2 cbday) cnadd) (cun (cun (co (cfv C cbday) (cfv E cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv D cbday) (cfv F cbday) cnadd)) (cun (co (cfv C cbday) (cfv F cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv D cbday) (cfv E cbday) cnadd))))) (wa (wcel (co (cv a) (cv b) cmuls) csur) (wi (wa (wbr (cv c) (cv d) clts) (wbr (cv e) (cv f2) clts)) (wbr (co (co (cv c) (cv f2) cmuls) (co (cv c) (cv e) cmuls) csubs) (co (co (cv d) (cv f2) cmuls) (co (cv d) (cv e) cmuls) csubs) clts)))) csur) csur) csur) csur) csur) csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (w3a (wcel (co A2 B2 cmuls) csur) (wbr (cun (cab g2 (wrex p (wrex q (wceq (cv g2) (co (co (co (cv p) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv q) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv p) (cv q) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cleft)) (cfv A2 cleft))) (cab h (wrex r (wrex s1 (wceq (cv h) (co (co (co (cv r) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv s1) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv r) (cv s1) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cright)) (cfv A2 cright)))) (csn (co A2 B2 cmuls)) cslts) (wbr (csn (co A2 B2 cmuls)) (cun (cab i (wrex t (wrex u (wceq (cv i) (co (co (co (cv t) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv u) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv t) (cv u) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cright)) (cfv A2 cleft))) (cab j (wrex v (wrex w (wceq (cv j) (co (co (co (cv v) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv w) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv v) (cv w) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cleft)) (cfv A2 cright)))) cslts)) $;

--| Lemma for surreal multiplication. Under the inductive hypothesis, demonstrate closure of surreal multiplication. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 5-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulsproplem11 {e f2 a b c d: setvar} (ph: wff e f2 a b c d) (A2 B2 C D E F: class):
  $ wi ph (wral a (wral b (wral c (wral d (wral e (wral f2 (wi (wcel (cun (co (cfv (cv a) cbday) (cfv (cv b) cbday) cnadd) (cun (cun (co (cfv (cv c) cbday) (cfv (cv e) cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv (cv d) cbday) (cfv (cv f2) cbday) cnadd)) (cun (co (cfv (cv c) cbday) (cfv (cv f2) cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv (cv d) cbday) (cfv (cv e) cbday) cnadd)))) (cun (co (cfv A2 cbday) (cfv B2 cbday) cnadd) (cun (cun (co (cfv C cbday) (cfv E cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv D cbday) (cfv F cbday) cnadd)) (cun (co (cfv C cbday) (cfv F cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv D cbday) (cfv E cbday) cnadd))))) (wa (wcel (co (cv a) (cv b) cmuls) csur) (wi (wa (wbr (cv c) (cv d) clts) (wbr (cv e) (cv f2) clts)) (wbr (co (co (cv c) (cv f2) cmuls) (co (cv c) (cv e) cmuls) csubs) (co (co (cv d) (cv f2) cmuls) (co (cv d) (cv e) cmuls) csubs) clts)))) csur) csur) csur) csur) csur) csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co A2 B2 cmuls) csur) $;

--| Lemma for surreal multiplication. Demonstrate the second half of the inductive statement assuming ` C ` and ` D ` are not the same age and ` E ` and ` F ` are not the same age. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 5-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulsproplem12 {e f2 a b c d: setvar} (ph: wff e f2 a b c d) (A2 B2 C D E F: class):
  $ wi ph (wral a (wral b (wral c (wral d (wral e (wral f2 (wi (wcel (cun (co (cfv (cv a) cbday) (cfv (cv b) cbday) cnadd) (cun (cun (co (cfv (cv c) cbday) (cfv (cv e) cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv (cv d) cbday) (cfv (cv f2) cbday) cnadd)) (cun (co (cfv (cv c) cbday) (cfv (cv f2) cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv (cv d) cbday) (cfv (cv e) cbday) cnadd)))) (cun (co (cfv A2 cbday) (cfv B2 cbday) cnadd) (cun (cun (co (cfv C cbday) (cfv E cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv D cbday) (cfv F cbday) cnadd)) (cun (co (cfv C cbday) (cfv F cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv D cbday) (cfv E cbday) cnadd))))) (wa (wcel (co (cv a) (cv b) cmuls) csur) (wi (wa (wbr (cv c) (cv d) clts) (wbr (cv e) (cv f2) clts)) (wbr (co (co (cv c) (cv f2) cmuls) (co (cv c) (cv e) cmuls) csubs) (co (co (cv d) (cv f2) cmuls) (co (cv d) (cv e) cmuls) csubs) clts)))) csur) csur) csur) csur) csur) csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C D clts) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr E F clts) $ >
  $ wi ph (wo (wcel (cfv C cbday) (cfv D cbday)) (wcel (cfv D cbday) (cfv C cbday))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wo (wcel (cfv E cbday) (cfv F cbday)) (wcel (cfv F cbday) (cfv E cbday))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co (co C F cmuls) (co C E cmuls) csubs) (co (co D F cmuls) (co D E cmuls) csubs) clts) $;

--| Lemma for surreal multiplication. Remove the restriction on ` C ` and ` D ` from ~ mulsproplem12 . (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 5-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulsproplem13 {e f2 a b c d: setvar} (ph: wff e f2 a b c d) (A2 B2 C D E F: class):
  $ wi ph (wral a (wral b (wral c (wral d (wral e (wral f2 (wi (wcel (cun (co (cfv (cv a) cbday) (cfv (cv b) cbday) cnadd) (cun (cun (co (cfv (cv c) cbday) (cfv (cv e) cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv (cv d) cbday) (cfv (cv f2) cbday) cnadd)) (cun (co (cfv (cv c) cbday) (cfv (cv f2) cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv (cv d) cbday) (cfv (cv e) cbday) cnadd)))) (cun (co (cfv A2 cbday) (cfv B2 cbday) cnadd) (cun (cun (co (cfv C cbday) (cfv E cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv D cbday) (cfv F cbday) cnadd)) (cun (co (cfv C cbday) (cfv F cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv D cbday) (cfv E cbday) cnadd))))) (wa (wcel (co (cv a) (cv b) cmuls) csur) (wi (wa (wbr (cv c) (cv d) clts) (wbr (cv e) (cv f2) clts)) (wbr (co (co (cv c) (cv f2) cmuls) (co (cv c) (cv e) cmuls) csubs) (co (co (cv d) (cv f2) cmuls) (co (cv d) (cv e) cmuls) csubs) clts)))) csur) csur) csur) csur) csur) csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C D clts) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr E F clts) $ >
  $ wi ph (wo (wcel (cfv E cbday) (cfv F cbday)) (wcel (cfv F cbday) (cfv E cbday))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co (co C F cmuls) (co C E cmuls) csubs) (co (co D F cmuls) (co D E cmuls) csubs) clts) $;

--| Lemma for surreal multiplication. Finally, we remove the restriction on ` E ` and ` F ` from ~ mulsproplem12 and ~ mulsproplem13 . This completes the induction on surreal multiplication. ~ mulsprop brings all this together technically. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 5-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulsproplem14 {e f2 a b c d: setvar} (ph: wff e f2 a b c d) (A2 B2 C D E F: class):
  $ wi ph (wral a (wral b (wral c (wral d (wral e (wral f2 (wi (wcel (cun (co (cfv (cv a) cbday) (cfv (cv b) cbday) cnadd) (cun (cun (co (cfv (cv c) cbday) (cfv (cv e) cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv (cv d) cbday) (cfv (cv f2) cbday) cnadd)) (cun (co (cfv (cv c) cbday) (cfv (cv f2) cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv (cv d) cbday) (cfv (cv e) cbday) cnadd)))) (cun (co (cfv A2 cbday) (cfv B2 cbday) cnadd) (cun (cun (co (cfv C cbday) (cfv E cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv D cbday) (cfv F cbday) cnadd)) (cun (co (cfv C cbday) (cfv F cbday) cnadd) (co (cfv D cbday) (cfv E cbday) cnadd))))) (wa (wcel (co (cv a) (cv b) cmuls) csur) (wi (wa (wbr (cv c) (cv d) clts) (wbr (cv e) (cv f2) clts)) (wbr (co (co (cv c) (cv f2) cmuls) (co (cv c) (cv e) cmuls) csubs) (co (co (cv d) (cv f2) cmuls) (co (cv d) (cv e) cmuls) csubs) clts)))) csur) csur) csur) csur) csur) csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel E csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel F csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C D clts) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr E F clts) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co (co C F cmuls) (co C E cmuls) csubs) (co (co D F cmuls) (co D E cmuls) csubs) clts) $;

--| Surreals are closed under multiplication and obey a particular ordering law. Theorem 3.4 of [Gonshor] p. 17. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 5-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulsprop (A2 B2 C D E F: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wa (wcel A2 csur) (wcel B2 csur)) (wa (wcel C csur) (wcel D csur)) (wa (wcel E csur) (wcel F csur))) (wa (wcel (co A2 B2 cmuls) csur) (wi (wa (wbr C D clts) (wbr E F clts)) (wbr (co (co C F cmuls) (co C E cmuls) csubs) (co (co D F cmuls) (co D E cmuls) csubs) clts))) $;

--| Lemma for ~ mulcut . State the theorem with extra DV conditions. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 7-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulcutlem {w v u t s1 r q p a b c d: setvar} (ph: wff w v u t s1 r q p a b c d) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (w3a (wcel (co A2 B2 cmuls) csur) (wbr (cun (cab a (wrex p (wrex q (wceq (cv a) (co (co (co (cv p) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv q) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv p) (cv q) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cleft)) (cfv A2 cleft))) (cab b (wrex r (wrex s1 (wceq (cv b) (co (co (co (cv r) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv s1) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv r) (cv s1) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cright)) (cfv A2 cright)))) (csn (co A2 B2 cmuls)) cslts) (wbr (csn (co A2 B2 cmuls)) (cun (cab c (wrex t (wrex u (wceq (cv c) (co (co (co (cv t) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv u) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv t) (cv u) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cright)) (cfv A2 cleft))) (cab d (wrex v (wrex w (wceq (cv d) (co (co (co (cv v) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv w) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv v) (cv w) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cleft)) (cfv A2 cright)))) cslts)) $;

--| Show the cut properties of surreal multiplication. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 8-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulcut {w v u t s1 r q p a b c d: setvar} (ph: wff w v u t s1 r q p a b c d) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (w3a (wcel (co A2 B2 cmuls) csur) (wbr (cun (cab a (wrex p (wrex q (wceq (cv a) (co (co (co (cv p) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv q) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv p) (cv q) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cleft)) (cfv A2 cleft))) (cab b (wrex r (wrex s1 (wceq (cv b) (co (co (co (cv r) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv s1) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv r) (cv s1) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cright)) (cfv A2 cright)))) (csn (co A2 B2 cmuls)) cslts) (wbr (csn (co A2 B2 cmuls)) (cun (cab c (wrex t (wrex u (wceq (cv c) (co (co (co (cv t) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv u) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv t) (cv u) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cright)) (cfv A2 cleft))) (cab d (wrex v (wrex w (wceq (cv d) (co (co (co (cv v) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv w) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv v) (cv w) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cleft)) (cfv A2 cright)))) cslts)) $;

--| Show the cut properties of surreal multiplication. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 8-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulcut_b {w v u t a: setvar} (ph: wff w v u t a) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (w3a (wcel (co A2 B2 cmuls) csur) (wbr (cun (cab a (wrex t (wrex w (wceq (cv a) (co (co (co (cv t) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv w) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv t) (cv w) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cleft)) (cfv A2 cleft))) (cab a (wrex v (wrex u (wceq (cv a) (co (co (co (cv v) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv u) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv v) (cv u) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cright)) (cfv A2 cright)))) (csn (co A2 B2 cmuls)) cslts) (wbr (csn (co A2 B2 cmuls)) (cun (cab a (wrex t (wrex u (wceq (cv a) (co (co (co (cv t) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv u) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv t) (cv u) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cright)) (cfv A2 cleft))) (cab a (wrex v (wrex w (wceq (cv a) (co (co (co (cv v) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv w) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv v) (cv w) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cleft)) (cfv A2 cright)))) cslts)) $;

--| Show that the cut involved in surreal multiplication is actually a cut. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 7-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulcut2 {w v u t s1 r q p a b c d: setvar} (ph: wff w v u t s1 r q p a b c d) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cun (cab a (wrex p (wrex q (wceq (cv a) (co (co (co (cv p) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv q) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv p) (cv q) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cleft)) (cfv A2 cleft))) (cab b (wrex r (wrex s1 (wceq (cv b) (co (co (co (cv r) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv s1) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv r) (cv s1) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cright)) (cfv A2 cright)))) (cun (cab c (wrex t (wrex u (wceq (cv c) (co (co (co (cv t) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv u) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv t) (cv u) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cright)) (cfv A2 cleft))) (cab d (wrex v (wrex w (wceq (cv d) (co (co (co (cv v) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv w) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv v) (cv w) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cleft)) (cfv A2 cright)))) cslts) $;

--| Show that the cut involved in surreal multiplication is actually a cut. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 7-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulcut2_b {w v u t a: setvar} (ph: wff w v u t a) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cun (cab a (wrex t (wrex w (wceq (cv a) (co (co (co (cv t) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv w) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv t) (cv w) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cleft)) (cfv A2 cleft))) (cab a (wrex v (wrex u (wceq (cv a) (co (co (co (cv v) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv u) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv v) (cv u) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cright)) (cfv A2 cright)))) (cun (cab a (wrex t (wrex u (wceq (cv a) (co (co (co (cv t) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv u) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv t) (cv u) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cright)) (cfv A2 cleft))) (cab a (wrex v (wrex w (wceq (cv a) (co (co (co (cv v) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv w) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv v) (cv w) cmuls) csubs)) (cfv B2 cleft)) (cfv A2 cright)))) cslts) $;

--| The surreals are closed under multiplication. Theorem 8(i) of [Conway] p. 19. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 5-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulscl (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 csur) (wcel B2 csur)) (wcel (co A2 B2 cmuls) csur) $;

--| The surreals are closed under multiplication. Theorem 8(i) of [Conway] p. 19. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 6-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulscld (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co A2 B2 cmuls) csur) $;

--| An ordering relationship for surreal multiplication. Compare theorem 8(iii) of [Conway] p. 19. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 5-Mar-2025.)
theorem ltmuls (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 csur) (wcel B2 csur)) (wa (wcel C csur) (wcel D csur))) (wi (wa (wbr A2 B2 clts) (wbr C D clts)) (wbr (co (co A2 D cmuls) (co A2 C cmuls) csubs) (co (co B2 D cmuls) (co B2 C cmuls) csubs) clts)) $;

--| An ordering relationship for surreal multiplication. Compare theorem 8(iii) of [Conway] p. 19. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 6-Mar-2025.)
theorem ltmulsd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 clts) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C D clts) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co (co A2 D cmuls) (co A2 C cmuls) csubs) (co (co B2 D cmuls) (co B2 C cmuls) csubs) clts) $;

--| An ordering relationship for surreal multiplication. Compare theorem 8(iii) of [Conway] p. 19. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 7-Mar-2025.)
theorem lemulsd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 cles) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C D cles) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co (co A2 D cmuls) (co A2 C cmuls) csubs) (co (co B2 D cmuls) (co B2 C cmuls) csubs) cles) $;

--| Surreal multiplication is commutative. Part of theorem 7 of [Conway] p. 19. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 6-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulscom (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 csur) (wcel B2 csur)) (wceq (co A2 B2 cmuls) (co B2 A2 cmuls)) $;

--| Surreal multiplication is commutative. Part of theorem 7 of [Conway] p. 19. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 6-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulscomd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 B2 cmuls) (co B2 A2 cmuls)) $;

--| Surreal multiplication by zero. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 4-Feb-2025.)
theorem muls02 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 csur) (wceq (co c0s A2 cmuls) c0s) $;

--| Surreal one is a left identity element for multiplication. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 4-Feb-2025.)
theorem mulslid (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 csur) (wceq (co c1s A2 cmuls) A2) $;

--| Surreal one is a left identity element for multiplication. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 14-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulslidd (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co c1s A2 cmuls) A2) $;

--| The product of two positive surreals is positive. Theorem 9 of [Conway] p. 20. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 6-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulsgt0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 csur) (wbr c0s A2 clts)) (wa (wcel B2 csur) (wbr c0s B2 clts))) (wbr c0s (co A2 B2 cmuls) clts) $;

--| The product of two positive surreals is positive. Theorem 9 of [Conway] p. 20. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 6-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulsgt0d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr c0s A2 clts) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr c0s B2 clts) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr c0s (co A2 B2 cmuls) clts) $;

--| The product of two non-negative surreals is non-negative. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 6-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulsge0d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 csur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr c0s A2 cles) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr c0s B2 cles) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr c0s (co A2 B2 cmuls) cles) $;

--| One surreal set less-than relationship for cuts of ` A ` and ` B ` . (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 7-Mar-2025.)
theorem sltmuls1 {s1 r q p a b: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (R S: class q p a) (L M: class s1 r b):
  $ wi ph (wbr L R cslts) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr M S cslts) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 (co L R ccuts)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq B2 (co M S ccuts)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cun (cab a (wrex p (wrex q (wceq (cv a) (co (co (co (cv p) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv q) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv p) (cv q) cmuls) csubs)) M) L)) (cab b (wrex r (wrex s1 (wceq (cv b) (co (co (co (cv r) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv s1) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv r) (cv s1) cmuls) csubs)) S) R))) (csn (co A2 B2 cmuls)) cslts) $;

--| One surreal set less-than relationship for cuts of ` A ` and ` B ` . (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 7-Mar-2025.)
theorem sltmuls2 {w v u t c d: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class) (R: class u t c) (S L: class w v d) (M: class u t c):
  $ wi ph (wbr L R cslts) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr M S cslts) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 (co L R ccuts)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq B2 (co M S ccuts)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (csn (co A2 B2 cmuls)) (cun (cab c (wrex t (wrex u (wceq (cv c) (co (co (co (cv t) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv u) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv t) (cv u) cmuls) csubs)) S) L)) (cab d (wrex v (wrex w (wceq (cv d) (co (co (co (cv v) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv w) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv v) (cv w) cmuls) csubs)) M) R))) cslts) $;

