--| Surreal multiplication has the uniformity property. That is, any cuts that define ` A ` and ` B ` can be used in the definition of ` ( A x.s B ) ` . Theorem 3.5 of [Gonshor] p. 18. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 7-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulsunif {w v u t s1 r q p a b c d: setvar} (ph: wff w v u t s1 r q p a b c d) (A2 B2: class) (R: class w u t s1 q p a c) (S: class w v q p a d) (L: class w v u s1 r q b d) (M: class u t s1 r b c):
  $ wi ph (wbr L R cslts) $ >
