  $ wi ph (wceq A2 (co L R ccuts)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq B2 (co M S ccuts)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 B2 cmuls) (co (cun (cab a (wrex p (wrex q (wceq (cv a) (co (co (co (cv p) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv q) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv p) (cv q) cmuls) csubs)) M) L)) (cab b (wrex r (wrex s1 (wceq (cv b) (co (co (co (cv r) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv s1) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv r) (cv s1) cmuls) csubs)) S) R))) (cun (cab c (wrex t (wrex u (wceq (cv c) (co (co (co (cv t) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv u) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv t) (cv u) cmuls) csubs)) S) L)) (cab d (wrex v (wrex w (wceq (cv d) (co (co (co (cv v) B2 cmuls) (co A2 (cv w) cmuls) cadds) (co (cv v) (cv w) cmuls) csubs)) M) R))) ccuts)) $;

--| Surreal multiplication has the uniformity property. That is, any cuts that define ` A ` and ` B ` can be used in the definition of ` ( A x.s B ) ` . Theorem 3.5 of [Gonshor] p. 18. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 7-Mar-2025.)
