--| Surreal multiplication has the uniformity property. That is, any cuts that define ` A ` and ` B ` can be used in the definition of ` ( A x.s B ) ` . Theorem 3.5 of [Gonshor] p. 18. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 7-Mar-2025.)
theorem mulsunif_b1 {w v t a: setvar} (ph: wff w v t a) (A2 B2: class) (R: class w t) (S: class) (L: class w v) (M: class):
