--| The set of zeroes of ` F ` satisfies the conditions to have a supremum. (Contributed by Thierry Arnoux, 1-Dec-2016.) (Revised by AV, 6-Oct-2020.)
theorem ballotlemsup {x3 y1 z w i k c: setvar} (C: class x3 c) (P: class x3 y1 z w i k c) (E: class x3 y1 z w) (F: class x3) (I: class x3 y1 z w c) (M N: class x3) (O: class x3 y1 z w):
  $ wcel M cn $ >
  $ wcel N cn $ >
  $ wceq O (crab c (wceq (cfv (cv c) chash) M) (cpw (co c1 (co M N caddc) cfz))) $ >
  $ wceq P (cmpt x3 (cpw O) (co (cfv (cv x3) chash) (cfv O chash) cdiv)) $ >
  $ wceq F (cmpt c O (cmpt i cz (co (cfv (cin (co c1 (cv i) cfz) (cv c)) chash) (cfv (cdif (co c1 (cv i) cfz) (cv c)) chash) cmin))) $ >
