--| Definition (using hypotheses for readability) of the function giving the transitive closure of ` X ` in ` A ` by ` R ` . (Contributed by Jonathan Ben-Naim, 3-Jun-2011.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem bnj882 {y1 f2 i n: setvar} (ph ps: wff y1 f2 i n) (A2: class) (B2 D: class y1 f2 i n) (R X: class):
  $ wb ph (wceq (cfv c0 (cv f2)) (c_bnj14 A2 R X)) $ >
  $ wb ps (wral i (wi (wcel (csuc (cv i)) (cv n)) (wceq (cfv (csuc (cv i)) (cv f2)) (ciun y1 (cfv (cv i) (cv f2)) (c_bnj14 A2 R (cv y1))))) com) $ >
  $ wceq D (cdif com (csn c0)) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cab f2 (wrex n (w3a (wfn (cv f2) (cv n)) ph ps) D)) $ >
  $ wceq (c_bnj18 A2 R X) (ciun f2 B2 (ciun i (cdm (cv f2)) (cfv (cv i) (cv f2)))) $;

--| Equality theorem for transitive closure. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 22-Dec-2016.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem bnj18eq1 (A2 R X Y: class):
  $ wi (wceq X Y) (wceq (c_bnj18 A2 R X) (c_bnj18 A2 R Y)) $;

--| Property of ` _trCl ` . Under certain conditions, the transitive closure of ` X ` in ` A ` by ` R ` is a set. (Contributed by Jonathan Ben-Naim, 3-Jun-2011.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem bnj893 (A2 R X: class):
  $ wi (wa (w_bnj15 A2 R) (wcel X A2)) (wcel (c_bnj18 A2 R X) cvv) $;

