  $ wb ph (w3a (w_bnj15 A2 R) (wss B2 A2) (wne B2 c0)) $ >
  $ wb ps (w3a (wcel (cv x3) B2) (wcel (cv y1) B2) (wbr (cv y1) (cv x3) R)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wrex w (wral z (wn (wbr (cv z) (cv w) R)) B2) B2) $;

--| Technical lemma for ~ bnj69 . This lemma may no longer be used or have become an indirect lemma of the theorem in question (i.e. a lemma of a lemma... of the theorem). (Contributed by Jonathan Ben-Naim, 3-Jun-2011.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem bnj1189 {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff) (ps ch: wff x3 y1) (A2: class x3 y1) (B2 R: class):
  $ wb ph (w3a (w_bnj15 A2 R) (wss B2 A2) (wne B2 c0)) $ >
  $ wb ps (w3a (wcel (cv x3) B2) (wcel (cv y1) B2) (wbr (cv y1) (cv x3) R)) $ >
  $ wb ch (wral y1 (wn (wbr (cv y1) (cv x3) R)) B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wrex x3 (wral y1 (wn (wbr (cv y1) (cv x3) R)) B2) B2) $;

--| Existence of a minimal element in certain classes: if ` R ` is well-founded and set-like on ` A ` , then every nonempty subclass of ` A ` has a minimal element. The proof has been taken from Chapter 4 of Don Monk's notes on Set Theory. See ~ http://euclid.colorado.edu/~~monkd/setth.pdf . (Contributed by Jonathan Ben-Naim, 3-Jun-2011.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem bnj69 {x3 y1: setvar} (A2 B2 R: class):
  $ wi (w3a (w_bnj15 A2 R) (wss B2 A2) (wne B2 c0)) (wrex x3 (wral y1 (wn (wbr (cv y1) (cv x3) R)) B2) B2) $;

--| Existence of a minimal element in certain classes: if ` R ` is well-founded and set-like on ` A ` , then every nonempty subclass of ` A ` has a minimal element. The proof has been taken from Chapter 4 of Don Monk's notes on Set Theory. See ~ http://euclid.colorado.edu/~~monkd/setth.pdf . (Contributed by Jonathan Ben-Naim, 3-Jun-2011.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem bnj1228 {x3 y1 w: setvar} (A2: class x3 w) (B2: class x3) (R: class w):
  $ wi (wcel (cv w) B2) (wal x3 (wcel (cv w) B2)) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (w_bnj15 A2 R) (wss B2 A2) (wne B2 c0)) (wrex x3 (wral y1 (wn (wbr (cv y1) (cv x3) R)) B2) B2) $;

--| Well-founded induction. The proof has been taken from Chapter 4 of Don Monk's notes on Set Theory. See ~ http://euclid.colorado.edu/~~monkd/setth.pdf . (Contributed by Jonathan Ben-Naim, 3-Jun-2011.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem bnj1204 {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff x3) (ps: wff x3 y1) (A2 R: class):
  $ wb ps (wral y1 (wi (wbr (cv y1) (cv x3) R) (wsbc x3 ph (cv y1))) A2) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w_bnj15 A2 R) (wral x3 (wi ps ph) A2)) (wral x3 ph A2) $;

