--| Lemma for ~ 3dim1 . (Contributed by NM, 26-Jul-2012.)
theorem _3dim1lem5 {s1 r q: setvar} (w v u: setvar) (A2 P c_or: class) (K: class s1 r q) (c_le: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel (cv u) A2) (wcel (cv v) A2) (wcel (cv w) A2)) (w3a (wne P (cv u)) (wn (wbr (cv v) (co P (cv u) c_or) c_le)) (wn (wbr (cv w) (co (co P (cv u) c_or) (cv v) c_or) c_le)))) (wrex q (wrex r (wrex s1 (w3a (wne P (cv q)) (wn (wbr (cv r) (co P (cv q) c_or) c_le)) (wn (wbr (cv s1) (co (co P (cv q) c_or) (cv r) c_or) c_le))) A2) A2) A2) $;

--| Construct a 3-dimensional volume (height-4 element) on top of a given atom ` P ` . (Contributed by NM, 25-Jul-2012.)
theorem _3dim1 {s1 r q: setvar} (A2 P c_or: class) (K: class s1 r q) (c_le: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel P A2)) (wrex q (wrex r (wrex s1 (w3a (wne P (cv q)) (wn (wbr (cv r) (co P (cv q) c_or) c_le)) (wn (wbr (cv s1) (co (co P (cv q) c_or) (cv r) c_or) c_le))) A2) A2) A2) $;

--| Construct 2 new layers on top of 2 given atoms. (Contributed by NM, 27-Jul-2012.)
theorem _3dim2 {s1 r: setvar} (A2 P Q c_or: class) (K: class s1 r) (c_le: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2)) (wrex r (wrex s1 (wa (wn (wbr (cv r) (co P Q c_or) c_le)) (wn (wbr (cv s1) (co (co P Q c_or) (cv r) c_or) c_le))) A2) A2) $;

--| Construct a new layer on top of 3 given atoms. (Contributed by NM, 27-Jul-2012.)
theorem _3dim3 {s1: setvar} (A2 P Q R c_or: class) (K: class s1) (c_le: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2))) (wrex s1 (wn (wbr (cv s1) (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) c_le)) A2) $;

--| Generate a height-3 element (2-dimensional plane) from an atom. (Contributed by NM, 3-May-2012.)
theorem _2dim {r q: setvar} (A2: class) (C: class r q) (P c_or K: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel P A2)) (wrex q (wrex r (wa (wbr P (co P (cv q) c_or) C) (wbr (co P (cv q) c_or) (co (co P (cv q) c_or) (cv r) c_or) C)) A2) A2) $;

--| An atom is covered by a height-2 element (1-dimensional line). (Contributed by NM, 3-May-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem _1dimN {q: setvar} (A2: class) (C: class q) (P c_or K: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel P A2)) (wrex q (wbr P (co P (cv q) c_or) C) A2) $;

--| The orthocomplement of an element covered by 1 is an atom. (Contributed by NM, 7-May-2012.)
theorem _1cvrco (A2 B2 C c_1 K c_pe X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv K cp1) $ >
  $ wceq c_pe (cfv K coc) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel X B2)) (wb (wbr X c_1 C) (wcel (cfv X c_pe) A2)) $;

--| There exists an atom less than an element covered by 1. (Contributed by NM, 7-May-2012.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 13-Jun-2014.)
theorem _1cvratex {p: setvar} (A2 B2 C c_lt c_1 K X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_lt (cfv K cplt) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv K cp1) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X B2) (wbr X c_1 C)) (wrex p (wbr (cv p) X c_lt) A2) $;

--| An atom less than or equal to an element covered by 1 is less than the element. (Contributed by NM, 7-May-2012.)
theorem _1cvratlt (A2 B2 C P c_lt c_1 K c_le X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_lt (cfv K cplt) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv K cp1) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel P A2) (wcel X B2)) (wa (wbr X c_1 C) (wbr P X c_le))) (wbr P X c_lt) $;

--| An element covered by the lattice unity, when joined with an atom not under it, equals the lattice unity. (Contributed by NM, 30-Apr-2012.)
theorem _1cvrjat (A2 B2 C P c_1 c_or K c_le X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv K cp1) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X B2) (wcel P A2)) (wa (wbr X c_1 C) (wn (wbr P X c_le)))) (wceq (co X P c_or) c_1) $;

--| Create an atom under an element covered by the lattice unity. Part of proof of Lemma B in [Crawley] p. 112. (Contributed by NM, 30-Apr-2012.)
theorem _1cvrat (A2 B2 C P Q c_1 c_or K c_le c_an X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq c_an (cfv K cmee) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv K cp1) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2) (wcel X B2)) (w3a (wne P Q) (wbr X c_1 C) (wn (wbr P X c_le)))) (wcel (co (co P Q c_or) X c_an) A2) $;

--| The join of two atoms ` R .\/ S ` (specifying a projective geometry line) is determined uniquely by any two atoms (specifying two points) less than or equal to that join. Part of Lemma 16.4 of [MaedaMaeda] p. 69, showing projective space postulate PS1 in [MaedaMaeda] p. 67. (Contributed by NM, 15-Nov-2011.)
theorem ps_1 (A2 P Q R S c_or K c_le: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2) (wne P Q)) (wa (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2))) (wb (wbr (co P Q c_or) (co R S c_or) c_le) (wceq (co P Q c_or) (co R S c_or))) $;

--| Lattice analogue for the projective geometry axiom, "if a line intersects two sides of a triangle at different points then it also intersects the third side." Projective space condition PS2 in [MaedaMaeda] p. 68 and part of Theorem 16.4 in [MaedaMaeda] p. 69. (Contributed by NM, 1-Dec-2011.)
theorem ps_2 {u: setvar} (A2 P Q R S T c_or K c_le: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2)) (wa (wcel S A2) (wcel T A2))) (wa (wa (wn (wbr P (co Q R c_or) c_le)) (wne S T)) (wa (wbr S (co P Q c_or) c_le) (wbr T (co Q R c_or) c_le)))) (wrex u (wa (wbr (cv u) (co P R c_or) c_le) (wbr (cv u) (co S T c_or) c_le)) A2) $;

--| Two atoms are different if their join majorizes the join of two different atoms. (Contributed by NM, 4-Jun-2013.)
theorem _2atjlej (A2 P Q R S c_or K c_le: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2) (wne P Q)) (w3a (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2) (wbr (co P Q c_or) (co R S c_or) c_le))) (wne R S) $;

--| Rearrange join of atoms in an equality. (Contributed by NM, 29-Jul-2013.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem hlatexch3N (A2 P Q R c_or K: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2)) (wa (wne Q R) (wceq (co P Q c_or) (co P R c_or)))) (wceq (co P Q c_or) (co Q R c_or)) $;

--| Exchange 2 atoms. (Contributed by NM, 13-May-2013.)
theorem hlatexch4 (A2 P Q R S c_or K: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2)) (wa (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2)) (w3a (wne P R) (wne Q S) (wceq (co P Q c_or) (co R S c_or)))) (wceq (co P R c_or) (co Q S c_or)) $;

--| Variation of projective geometry axiom ~ ps-2 . (Contributed by NM, 3-Jul-2012.)
theorem ps_2b (A2 P Q R S T c_or K c_le c_an c_0: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq c_an (cfv K cmee) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv K cp0) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2)) (w3a (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2) (wcel T A2)) (w3a (wn (wbr P (co Q R c_or) c_le)) (wne S T) (wa (wbr S (co P Q c_or) c_le) (wbr T (co Q R c_or) c_le)))) (wne (co (co P R c_or) (co S T c_or) c_an) c_0) $;

--| Lemma for ~ 3at . (Contributed by NM, 22-Jun-2012.)
theorem _3atlem1 (A2 P Q R S T U c_or K c_le: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2)) (w3a (wcel S A2) (wcel T A2) (wcel U A2))) (w3a (wn (wbr R (co P Q c_or) c_le)) (wn (wbr P (co T U c_or) c_le)) (wn (wbr Q (co P U c_or) c_le))) (wbr (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) (co (co S T c_or) U c_or) c_le)) (wceq (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) (co (co S T c_or) U c_or)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ 3at . (Contributed by NM, 22-Jun-2012.)
theorem _3atlem2 (A2 P Q R S T U c_or K c_le: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2)) (w3a (wcel S A2) (wcel T A2) (wcel U A2))) (w3a (wn (wbr R (co P Q c_or) c_le)) (wa (wne P U) (wbr P (co T U c_or) c_le)) (wn (wbr Q (co P U c_or) c_le))) (wbr (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) (co (co S T c_or) U c_or) c_le)) (wceq (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) (co (co S T c_or) U c_or)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ 3at . (Contributed by NM, 23-Jun-2012.)
theorem _3atlem3 (A2 P Q R S T U c_or K c_le: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2)) (w3a (wcel S A2) (wcel T A2) (wcel U A2))) (w3a (wn (wbr R (co P Q c_or) c_le)) (wne P U) (wn (wbr Q (co P U c_or) c_le))) (wbr (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) (co (co S T c_or) U c_or) c_le)) (wceq (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) (co (co S T c_or) U c_or)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ 3at . (Contributed by NM, 23-Jun-2012.)
theorem _3atlem4 (A2 P Q R S T c_or K c_le: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
