  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2)) (wa (wcel S A2) (wcel T A2))) (wa (wn (wbr R (co P Q c_or) c_le)) (wne P Q)) (wbr (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) (co (co S T c_or) R c_or) c_le)) (wceq (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) (co (co S T c_or) R c_or)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ 3at . (Contributed by NM, 23-Jun-2012.)
theorem _3atlem5 (A2 P Q R S T U c_or K c_le: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2)) (w3a (wcel S A2) (wcel T A2) (wcel U A2))) (w3a (wn (wbr R (co P Q c_or) c_le)) (wne P Q) (wn (wbr Q (co P U c_or) c_le))) (wbr (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) (co (co S T c_or) U c_or) c_le)) (wceq (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) (co (co S T c_or) U c_or)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ 3at . (Contributed by NM, 23-Jun-2012.)
theorem _3atlem6 (A2 P Q R S T U c_or K c_le: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2)) (w3a (wcel S A2) (wcel T A2) (wcel U A2))) (w3a (wn (wbr R (co P Q c_or) c_le)) (wne P Q) (wbr Q (co P U c_or) c_le)) (wbr (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) (co (co S T c_or) U c_or) c_le)) (wceq (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) (co (co S T c_or) U c_or)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ 3at . (Contributed by NM, 23-Jun-2012.)
theorem _3atlem7 (A2 P Q R S T U c_or K c_le: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2)) (w3a (wcel S A2) (wcel T A2) (wcel U A2))) (wa (wn (wbr R (co P Q c_or) c_le)) (wne P Q)) (wbr (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) (co (co S T c_or) U c_or) c_le)) (wceq (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) (co (co S T c_or) U c_or)) $;

--| Any three non-colinear atoms in a (lattice) plane determine the plane uniquely. This is the 2-dimensional analogue of ~ ps-1 for lines and ~ 4at for volumes. I could not find this proof in the literature on projective geometry (where it is either given as an axiom or stated as an unproved fact), but it is similar to Theorem 15 of Veblen, "The Foundations of Geometry" (1911), p. 18, which uses different axioms. This proof was written before I became aware of Veblen's, and it is possible that a shorter proof could be obtained by using Veblen's proof for hints. (Contributed by NM, 23-Jun-2012.)
theorem _3at (A2 P Q R S T U c_or K c_le: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2)) (w3a (wcel S A2) (wcel T A2) (wcel U A2))) (wa (wn (wbr R (co P Q c_or) c_le)) (wne P Q))) (wb (wbr (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) (co (co S T c_or) U c_or) c_le) (wceq (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) (co (co S T c_or) U c_or))) $;

--| Extend class notation with set of all "lattice lines" (lattice elements which cover an atom) in a Hilbert lattice.
term clln: class;

--| Extend class notation with set of all "lattice planes" (lattice elements which cover a line) in a Hilbert lattice.
term clpl: class;

--| Extend class notation with set of all 3-dimensional "lattice volumes" (lattice elements which cover a plane) in a Hilbert lattice.
term clvol: class;

--| Extend class notation with set of all projective lines for a Hilbert lattice.
term clines: class;

--| Extend class notation with set of all projective points.
term cpointsN: class;

--| Extend class notation with set of all projective subspaces.
term cpsubsp: class;

--| Extend class notation with projective map.
term cpmap: class;

--| Define the set of all "lattice lines" (lattice elements which cover an atom) in a Hilbert lattice ` k ` , in other words all elements of height 2 (or lattice dimension 2 or projective dimension 1). (Contributed by NM, 16-Jun-2012.)
axiom df_llines {x3 k p: setvar}:
  $ wceq clln (cmpt k cvv (crab x3 (wrex p (wbr (cv p) (cv x3) (cfv (cv k) ccvr)) (cfv (cv k) catm)) (cfv (cv k) cbs))) $;

--| Define the set of all "lattice planes" (lattice elements which cover a line) in a Hilbert lattice ` k ` , in other words all elements of height 3 (or lattice dimension 3 or projective dimension 2). (Contributed by NM, 16-Jun-2012.)
axiom df_lplanes {x3 k p: setvar}:
  $ wceq clpl (cmpt k cvv (crab x3 (wrex p (wbr (cv p) (cv x3) (cfv (cv k) ccvr)) (cfv (cv k) clln)) (cfv (cv k) cbs))) $;

--| Define the set of all 3-dimensional "lattice volumes" (lattice elements which cover a plane) in a Hilbert lattice ` k ` , in other words all elements of height 4 (or lattice dimension 4 or projective dimension 3). (Contributed by NM, 1-Jul-2012.)
axiom df_lvols {x3 k p: setvar}:
  $ wceq clvol (cmpt k cvv (crab x3 (wrex p (wbr (cv p) (cv x3) (cfv (cv k) ccvr)) (cfv (cv k) clpl)) (cfv (cv k) cbs))) $;

--| Define set of all projective lines for a Hilbert lattice (actually in any set at all, for simplicity). The join of two distinct atoms equals a line. Definition of lines in item 1 of [Holland95] p. 222. (Contributed by NM, 19-Sep-2011.)
axiom df_lines {k s1 r q p: setvar}:
  $ wceq clines (cmpt k cvv (cab s1 (wrex q (wrex r (wa (wne (cv q) (cv r)) (wceq (cv s1) (crab p (wbr (cv p) (co (cv q) (cv r) (cfv (cv k) cjn)) (cfv (cv k) cple)) (cfv (cv k) catm)))) (cfv (cv k) catm)) (cfv (cv k) catm)))) $;

--| Define set of all projective points in a Hilbert lattice (actually in any set at all, for simplicity). A projective point is the singleton of a lattice atom. Definition 15.1 of [MaedaMaeda] p. 61. Note that item 1 in [Holland95] p. 222 defines a point as the atom itself, but this leads to a complicated subspace ordering that may be either membership or inclusion based on its arguments. (Contributed by NM, 2-Oct-2011.)
axiom df_pointsN {k q p: setvar}:
  $ wceq cpointsN (cmpt k cvv (cab q (wrex p (wceq (cv q) (csn (cv p))) (cfv (cv k) catm)))) $;

--| Define set of all projective subspaces. Based on definition of subspace in [Holland95] p. 212. (Contributed by NM, 2-Oct-2011.)
axiom df_psubsp {k s1 r q p: setvar}:
  $ wceq cpsubsp (cmpt k cvv (cab s1 (wa (wss (cv s1) (cfv (cv k) catm)) (wral p (wral q (wral r (wi (wbr (cv r) (co (cv p) (cv q) (cfv (cv k) cjn)) (cfv (cv k) cple)) (wcel (cv r) (cv s1))) (cfv (cv k) catm)) (cv s1)) (cv s1))))) $;

--| Define projective map for ` k ` at ` a ` . Definition in Theorem 15.5 of [MaedaMaeda] p. 62. (Contributed by NM, 2-Oct-2011.)
axiom df_pmap {k p a: setvar}:
  $ wceq cpmap (cmpt k cvv (cmpt a (cfv (cv k) cbs) (crab p (wbr (cv p) (cv a) (cfv (cv k) cple)) (cfv (cv k) catm)))) $;

--| The set of lattice lines in a Hilbert lattice. (Contributed by NM, 16-Jun-2012.)
theorem llnset {x3 p: setvar} (A2: class x3) (B2: class p) (C D: class x3 p) (K: class) (N: class x3 p):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (wcel K D) (wceq N (crab x3 (wrex p (wbr (cv p) (cv x3) C) A2) B2)) $;

--| The predicate "is a lattice line". (Contributed by NM, 16-Jun-2012.)
theorem islln {p: setvar} (A2: class) (B2 C D: class p) (K: class) (N: class p) (X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (wcel K D) (wb (wcel X N) (wa (wcel X B2) (wrex p (wbr (cv p) X C) A2))) $;

--| The predicate "is a lattice line". (Contributed by NM, 16-Jun-2012.)
theorem islln4 {p: setvar} (A2: class) (B2 C D: class p) (K: class) (N: class p) (X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K D) (wcel X B2)) (wb (wcel X N) (wrex p (wbr (cv p) X C) A2)) $;

--| Condition implying a lattice line. (Contributed by NM, 17-Jun-2012.)
theorem llni (A2 B2 C D P K N X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K D) (wcel X B2) (wcel P A2)) (wbr P X C)) (wcel X N) $;

--| A lattice line is a lattice element. (Contributed by NM, 16-Jun-2012.)
theorem llnbase (B2 K N X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (wcel X N) (wcel X B2) $;

--| The predicate "is a lattice line". (Contributed by NM, 17-Jun-2012.)
theorem islln3 {q p: setvar} (A2 B2: class) (c_or: class q p) (K: class) (N: class q p) (X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel X B2)) (wb (wcel X N) (wrex p (wrex q (wa (wne (cv p) (cv q)) (wceq X (co (cv p) (cv q) c_or))) A2) A2)) $;

--| The predicate "is a lattice line". (Contributed by NM, 23-Jun-2012.)
theorem islln2 {q p: setvar} (A2 B2: class) (c_or: class q p) (K: class) (N: class q p) (X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (wcel K chlt) (wb (wcel X N) (wa (wcel X B2) (wrex p (wrex q (wa (wne (cv p) (cv q)) (wceq X (co (cv p) (cv q) c_or))) A2) A2))) $;

--| The join of two different atoms is a lattice line. (Contributed by NM, 26-Jun-2012.)
theorem llni2 (A2 P Q c_or K N: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2)) (wne P Q)) (wcel (co P Q c_or) N) $;

--| An atom cannot majorize a lattice line. (Contributed by NM, 8-Jul-2012.)
theorem llnnleat (A2 P K c_le N X: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X N) (wcel P A2)) (wn (wbr X P c_le)) $;

--| A lattice line is not an atom. (Contributed by NM, 19-Jun-2012.)
theorem llnneat (A2 K N X: class):
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel X N)) (wn (wcel X A2)) $;

--| The join of two distinct atoms is not an atom. (Contributed by NM, 12-Oct-2012.)
theorem _2atneat (A2 P Q c_or K: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2) (wne P Q))) (wn (wcel (co P Q c_or) A2)) $;

--| A lattice line is nonzero. (Contributed by NM, 15-Jul-2012.)
theorem llnn0 (K N X c_0: class):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv K cp0) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel X N)) (wne X c_0) $;

--| The predicate "is a lattice line" in terms of atoms. (Contributed by NM, 15-Jul-2012.)
theorem islln2a (A2 P Q c_or K N: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2)) (wb (wcel (co P Q c_or) N) (wne P Q)) $;

--| Any element greater than 0 and not an atom majorizes a lattice line. (Contributed by NM, 28-Jun-2012.)
theorem llnle {y1: setvar} (A2 B2: class y1) (K c_le N X: class) (c_0: class y1):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv K cp0) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel X B2)) (wa (wne X c_0) (wn (wcel X A2)))) (wrex y1 (wbr (cv y1) X c_le) N) $;

--| An atom under a line is covered by it. (Contributed by NM, 2-Jul-2012.)
theorem atcvrlln2 (A2 C P K c_le N X: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel P A2) (wcel X N)) (wbr P X c_le)) (wbr P X C) $;

--| An element covering an atom is a lattice line and vice-versa. (Contributed by NM, 18-Jun-2012.)
theorem atcvrlln (A2 B2 C K N X Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2)) (wbr X Y C)) (wb (wcel X A2) (wcel Y N)) $;

--| Given an atom on a line, there is another atom whose join equals the line. (Contributed by NM, 26-Jun-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem llnexatN {q: setvar} (A2 P: class) (c_or: class q) (K c_le N X: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X N) (wcel P A2)) (wbr P X c_le)) (wrex q (wa (wne P (cv q)) (wceq X (co P (cv q) c_or))) A2) $;

--| If two lattice lines are comparable, they are equal. (Contributed by NM, 19-Jun-2012.)
theorem llncmp (K c_le N X Y: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X N) (wcel Y N)) (wb (wbr X Y c_le) (wceq X Y)) $;

--| Two lattice lines cannot satisfy the less than relation. (Contributed by NM, 26-Jun-2012.)
theorem llnnlt (c_lt K N X Y: class):
  $ wceq c_lt (cfv K cplt) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X N) (wcel Y N)) (wn (wbr X Y c_lt)) $;

--| Two intersecting lines intersect at an atom. (Contributed by NM, 30-Apr-2012.)
theorem _2llnmat (A2 K c_an N X Y c_0: class):
  $ wceq c_an (cfv K cmee) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv K cp0) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X N) (wcel Y N)) (wa (wne X Y) (wne (co X Y c_an) c_0))) (wcel (co X Y c_an) A2) $;

--| Special case of ~ 2atmat0 where one atom could be zero. (Contributed by NM, 30-May-2013.)
theorem _2at0mat0 (A2 P Q R S c_or K c_an c_0: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq c_an (cfv K cmee) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv K cp0) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2)) (w3a (wcel R A2) (wo (wcel S A2) (wceq S c_0)) (wne (co P Q c_or) (co R S c_or)))) (wo (wcel (co (co P Q c_or) (co R S c_or) c_an) A2) (wceq (co (co P Q c_or) (co R S c_or) c_an) c_0)) $;

--| The meet of two unequal lines (expressed as joins of atoms) is an atom or zero. (Contributed by NM, 2-Dec-2012.)
theorem _2atmat0 (A2 P Q R S c_or K c_an c_0: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq c_an (cfv K cmee) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv K cp0) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2)) (w3a (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2) (wne (co P Q c_or) (co R S c_or)))) (wo (wcel (co (co P Q c_or) (co R S c_or) c_an) A2) (wceq (co (co P Q c_or) (co R S c_or) c_an) c_0)) $;

--| An atom majorized by two different atom joins (which could be atoms or lines) is equal to their intersection. (Contributed by NM, 30-Jun-2013.)
theorem _2atm (A2 P Q R S T c_or K c_le c_an: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq c_an (cfv K cmee) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2)) (w3a (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2) (wcel T A2)) (w3a (wbr T (co P Q c_or) c_le) (wbr T (co R S c_or) c_le) (wne (co P Q c_or) (co R S c_or)))) (wceq T (co (co P Q c_or) (co R S c_or) c_an)) $;

--| Variation of projective geometry axiom ~ ps-2 . (Contributed by NM, 3-Jul-2012.)
theorem ps_2c (A2 P Q R S T c_or K c_le c_an: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq c_an (cfv K cmee) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2)) (w3a (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2) (wcel T A2)) (w3a (wa (wn (wbr P (co Q R c_or) c_le)) (wne S T)) (wne (co P R c_or) (co S T c_or)) (wa (wbr S (co P Q c_or) c_le) (wbr T (co Q R c_or) c_le)))) (wcel (co (co P R c_or) (co S T c_or) c_an) A2) $;

--| The set of lattice planes in a Hilbert lattice. (Contributed by NM, 16-Jun-2012.)
theorem lplnset {x3 y1: setvar} (A2: class x3 y1) (B2: class y1) (C P: class x3 y1) (K: class) (N: class x3):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wcel K A2) (wceq P (crab x3 (wrex y1 (wbr (cv y1) (cv x3) C) N) B2)) $;

--| The predicate "is a lattice plane". (Contributed by NM, 16-Jun-2012.)
theorem islpln {y1: setvar} (A2 B2 C P: class y1) (K N X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wcel K A2) (wb (wcel X P) (wa (wcel X B2) (wrex y1 (wbr (cv y1) X C) N))) $;

--| The predicate "is a lattice plane". (Contributed by NM, 17-Jun-2012.)
theorem islpln4 {y1: setvar} (A2 B2 C P: class y1) (K N X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K A2) (wcel X B2)) (wb (wcel X P) (wrex y1 (wbr (cv y1) X C) N)) $;

--| Condition implying a lattice plane. (Contributed by NM, 20-Jun-2012.)
theorem lplni (B2 C D P K N X Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K D) (wcel Y B2) (wcel X N)) (wbr X Y C)) (wcel Y P) $;

--| The predicate "is a lattice plane". (Contributed by NM, 17-Jun-2012.)
theorem islpln3 {y1 p: setvar} (A2: class y1) (B2: class) (P c_or: class y1 p) (K: class) (c_le: class y1) (N X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel X B2)) (wb (wcel X P) (wrex y1 (wrex p (wa (wn (wbr (cv p) (cv y1) c_le)) (wceq X (co (cv y1) (cv p) c_or))) A2) N)) $;

--| A lattice plane is a lattice element. (Contributed by NM, 17-Jun-2012.)
theorem lplnbase (B2 P K X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wcel X P) (wcel X B2) $;

--| The predicate "is a lattice plane" in terms of atoms. (Contributed by NM, 24-Jun-2012.)
theorem islpln5 {r q p: setvar} (A2 B2: class) (P: class r q p) (c_or K c_le X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel X B2)) (wb (wcel X P) (wrex p (wrex q (wrex r (w3a (wne (cv p) (cv q)) (wn (wbr (cv r) (co (cv p) (cv q) c_or) c_le)) (wceq X (co (co (cv p) (cv q) c_or) (cv r) c_or))) A2) A2) A2)) $;

--| The predicate "is a lattice plane" in terms of atoms. (Contributed by NM, 25-Jun-2012.)
theorem islpln2 {r q p: setvar} (A2 B2: class) (P: class r q p) (c_or K c_le X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wcel K chlt) (wb (wcel X P) (wa (wcel X B2) (wrex p (wrex q (wrex r (w3a (wne (cv p) (cv q)) (wn (wbr (cv r) (co (cv p) (cv q) c_or) c_le)) (wceq X (co (co (cv p) (cv q) c_or) (cv r) c_or))) A2) A2) A2))) $;

--| The join of 3 different atoms is a lattice plane. (Contributed by NM, 4-Jul-2012.)
theorem lplni2 (A2 P Q R S c_or K c_le: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2)) (wa (wne Q R) (wn (wbr S (co Q R c_or) c_le)))) (wcel (co (co Q R c_or) S c_or) P) $;

--| There is an atom outside of a lattice plane i.e. a 3-dimensional lattice volume exists. (Contributed by NM, 28-Jul-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem lvolex3N {q: setvar} (A2: class) (P: class q) (K c_le X: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel X P)) (wrex q (wn (wbr (cv q) X c_le)) A2) $;

--| The intersection of a line with a plane not containing it is an atom. (Contributed by NM, 29-Jun-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem llnmlplnN (A2 P K c_le c_an N X Y c_0: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_an (cfv K cmee) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv K cp0) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X N) (wcel Y P)) (wa (wn (wbr X Y c_le)) (wne (co X Y c_an) c_0))) (wcel (co X Y c_an) A2) $;

--| Any element greater than 0 and not an atom and not a lattice line majorizes a lattice plane. (Contributed by NM, 28-Jun-2012.)
theorem lplnle {y1: setvar} (A2 B2: class y1) (P K c_le: class) (N: class y1) (X: class) (c_0: class y1):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv K cp0) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel X B2)) (w3a (wne X c_0) (wn (wcel X A2)) (wn (wcel X N)))) (wrex y1 (wbr (cv y1) X c_le) P) $;

--| A lattice line (or atom) cannot majorize a lattice plane. (Contributed by NM, 8-Jul-2012.)
theorem lplnnle2at (A2 P Q R c_or K c_le X: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel X P) (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2))) (wn (wbr X (co Q R c_or) c_le)) $;

--| A lattice plane cannot majorize an atom. (Contributed by NM, 14-Jul-2012.)
theorem lplnnleat (A2 P Q K c_le X: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X P) (wcel Q A2)) (wn (wbr X Q c_le)) $;

--| A lattice plane is not less than or equal to a lattice line. (Contributed by NM, 14-Jul-2012.)
theorem lplnnlelln (P K c_le N X Y: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X P) (wcel Y N)) (wn (wbr X Y c_le)) $;

--| The join of two atoms is not a lattice plane. (Contributed by NM, 16-Jul-2012.)
theorem _2atnelpln (A2 P Q R c_or K: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2)) (wn (wcel (co Q R c_or) P)) $;

--| No lattice plane is an atom. (Contributed by NM, 15-Jul-2012.)
theorem lplnneat (A2 P K X: class):
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel X P)) (wn (wcel X A2)) $;

--| No lattice plane is a lattice line. (Contributed by NM, 19-Jun-2012.)
theorem lplnnelln (P K N X: class):
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel X P)) (wn (wcel X N)) $;

--| A lattice plane is nonzero. (Contributed by NM, 15-Jul-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem lplnn0N (P K X c_0: class):
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv K cp0) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel X P)) (wne X c_0) $;

--| The predicate "is a lattice plane" for join of atoms. (Contributed by NM, 16-Jul-2012.)
theorem islpln2a (A2 P Q R S c_or K c_le: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2))) (wb (wcel (co (co Q R c_or) S c_or) P) (wa (wne Q R) (wn (wbr S (co Q R c_or) c_le)))) $;

--| The predicate "is a lattice plane" for join of atoms. Version of ~ islpln2a expressed with an abbreviation hypothesis. (Contributed by NM, 30-Jul-2012.)
theorem islpln2ah (A2 P Q R S c_or K c_le Y: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wceq Y (co (co Q R c_or) S c_or) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2))) (wb (wcel Y P) (wa (wne Q R) (wn (wbr S (co Q R c_or) c_le)))) $;

--| Property of a lattice plane expressed as the join of 3 atoms. (Contributed by NM, 30-Jul-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem lplnriaN (A2 P Q R S c_or K c_le Y: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wceq Y (co (co Q R c_or) S c_or) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2)) (wcel Y P)) (wn (wbr Q (co R S c_or) c_le)) $;

--| Property of a lattice plane expressed as the join of 3 atoms. (Contributed by NM, 30-Jul-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem lplnribN (A2 P Q R S c_or K c_le Y: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wceq Y (co (co Q R c_or) S c_or) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2)) (wcel Y P)) (wn (wbr R (co Q S c_or) c_le)) $;

--| Property of a lattice plane expressed as the join of 3 atoms. (Contributed by NM, 30-Jul-2012.)
theorem lplnric (A2 P Q R S c_or K c_le Y: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wceq Y (co (co Q R c_or) S c_or) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2)) (wcel Y P)) (wn (wbr S (co Q R c_or) c_le)) $;

--| Property of a lattice plane expressed as the join of 3 atoms. (Contributed by NM, 30-Jul-2012.)
theorem lplnri1 (A2 P Q R S c_or K Y: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wceq Y (co (co Q R c_or) S c_or) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2)) (wcel Y P)) (wne Q R) $;

--| Property of a lattice plane expressed as the join of 3 atoms. (Contributed by NM, 30-Jul-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem lplnri2N (A2 P Q R S c_or K Y: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wceq Y (co (co Q R c_or) S c_or) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2)) (wcel Y P)) (wne Q S) $;

--| Property of a lattice plane expressed as the join of 3 atoms. (Contributed by NM, 30-Jul-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem lplnri3N (A2 P Q R S c_or K Y: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wceq Y (co (co Q R c_or) S c_or) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2)) (wcel Y P)) (wne R S) $;

--| Two lattice lines defined by atoms defining a lattice plane are not equal. (Contributed by NM, 9-Oct-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem lplnllnneN (A2 P Q R S c_or K Y: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wceq Y (co (co Q R c_or) S c_or) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2)) (wcel Y P)) (wne (co Q S c_or) (co R S c_or)) $;

--| A lattice line under a lattice plane is covered by it. (Contributed by NM, 24-Jun-2012.)
theorem llncvrlpln2 (C P K c_le N X Y: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X N) (wcel Y P)) (wbr X Y c_le)) (wbr X Y C) $;

--| An element covering a lattice line is a lattice plane and vice-versa. (Contributed by NM, 26-Jun-2012.)
theorem llncvrlpln (B2 C P K N X Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X B2) (wcel Y B2)) (wbr X Y C)) (wb (wcel X N) (wcel Y P)) $;

--| If the join of two lattice planes covers one of them, their meet is a lattice line. (Contributed by NM, 30-Jun-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem _2lplnmN (C P c_or K c_an N X Y: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq c_an (cfv K cmee) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X P) (wcel Y P)) (wbr X (co X Y c_or) C)) (wcel (co X Y c_an) N) $;

--| The meet of two lattice lines is an atom iff their join is a lattice plane. (Contributed by NM, 27-Jun-2012.)
theorem _2llnmj (A2 P c_or K c_an N X Y: class):
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq c_an (cfv K cmee) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X N) (wcel Y N)) (wb (wcel (co X Y c_an) A2) (wcel (co X Y c_or) P)) $;

--| The meet of two intersecting lines (expressed as joins of atoms) is an atom. (Contributed by NM, 21-Nov-2012.)
theorem _2atmat (A2 P Q R S c_or K c_le c_an: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq c_an (cfv K cmee) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2)) (w3a (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2) (wne P Q)) (w3a (wne R S) (wn (wbr R (co P Q c_or) c_le)) (wbr S (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) c_le))) (wcel (co (co P Q c_or) (co R S c_or) c_an) A2) $;

--| If two lattice planes are comparable, they are equal. (Contributed by NM, 24-Jun-2012.)
theorem lplncmp (P K c_le X Y: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X P) (wcel Y P)) (wb (wbr X Y c_le) (wceq X Y)) $;

--| Given a lattice line on a lattice plane, there is an atom whose join with the line equals the plane. (Contributed by NM, 29-Jun-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem lplnexatN {q: setvar} (A2: class) (P c_or: class q) (K c_le: class) (N: class q) (X Y: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X P) (wcel Y N)) (wbr Y X c_le)) (wrex q (wa (wn (wbr (cv q) Y c_le)) (wceq X (co Y (cv q) c_or))) A2) $;

--| Given an atom on a lattice plane, there is a lattice line whose join with the atom equals the plane. (Contributed by NM, 26-Jun-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem lplnexllnN {y1: setvar} (A2 P: class y1) (Q c_or: class) (K: class y1) (c_le N X: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X P) (wcel Q A2)) (wbr Q X c_le)) (wrex y1 (wa (wn (wbr Q (cv y1) c_le)) (wceq X (co (cv y1) Q c_or))) N) $;

--| Two lattice planes cannot satisfy the less than relation. (Contributed by NM, 7-Jul-2012.)
theorem lplnnlt (P c_lt K X Y: class):
  $ wceq c_lt (cfv K cplt) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X P) (wcel Y P)) (wn (wbr X Y c_lt)) $;

--| The join of two different lattice lines in a lattice plane equals the plane (version of ~ 2llnjN in terms of atoms). (Contributed by NM, 5-Jul-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem _2llnjaN (A2 P Q R S T c_or K c_le N W: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W P)) (w3a (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2) (wne Q R)) (w3a (wcel S A2) (wcel T A2) (wne S T))) (w3a (wbr (co Q R c_or) W c_le) (wbr (co S T c_or) W c_le) (wne (co Q R c_or) (co S T c_or)))) (wceq (co (co Q R c_or) (co S T c_or) c_or) W) $;

--| The join of two different lattice lines in a lattice plane equals the plane. (Contributed by NM, 4-Jul-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem _2llnjN (P c_or K c_le N W X Y: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel X N) (wcel Y N) (wcel W P)) (w3a (wbr X W c_le) (wbr Y W c_le) (wne X Y))) (wceq (co X Y c_or) W) $;

--| The meet of two different lattice lines in a lattice plane is an atom. (Contributed by NM, 5-Jul-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem _2llnm2N (A2 P K c_le c_an N W X Y: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_an (cfv K cmee) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel X N) (wcel Y N) (wcel W P)) (w3a (wbr X W c_le) (wbr Y W c_le) (wne X Y))) (wcel (co X Y c_an) A2) $;

--| Two lattice lines in a lattice plane always meet. (Contributed by NM, 5-Jul-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem _2llnm3N (P K c_le c_an N W X Y c_0: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_an (cfv K cmee) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv K cp0) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel X N) (wcel Y N) (wcel W P)) (wa (wbr X W c_le) (wbr Y W c_le))) (wne (co X Y c_an) c_0) $;

--| Two lattice lines that majorize the same atom always meet. (Contributed by NM, 20-Jul-2012.)
theorem _2llnm4 (A2 P K c_le c_an N X Y c_0: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_an (cfv K cmee) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv K cp0) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel P A2) (wcel X N) (wcel Y N)) (wa (wbr P X c_le) (wbr P Y c_le))) (wne (co X Y c_an) c_0) $;

--| An atom equals the intersection of two majorizing lines. (Contributed by NM, 3-Apr-2013.)
theorem _2llnmeqat (A2 P K c_le c_an N X Y: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_an (cfv K cmee) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (w3a (wcel X N) (wcel Y N) (wcel P A2)) (wa (wne X Y) (wbr P (co X Y c_an) c_le))) (wceq P (co X Y c_an)) $;

--| The set of 3-dim lattice volumes in a Hilbert lattice. (Contributed by NM, 1-Jul-2012.)
theorem lvolset {x3 y1: setvar} (A2: class x3 y1) (B2: class y1) (C: class x3 y1) (P: class x3) (K: class) (V: class x3 y1):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv K clvol) $ >
  $ wi (wcel K A2) (wceq V (crab x3 (wrex y1 (wbr (cv y1) (cv x3) C) P) B2)) $;

--| The predicate "is a 3-dim lattice volume". (Contributed by NM, 1-Jul-2012.)
theorem islvol {y1: setvar} (A2 B2 C: class y1) (P K: class) (V: class y1) (X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv K clvol) $ >
  $ wi (wcel K A2) (wb (wcel X V) (wa (wcel X B2) (wrex y1 (wbr (cv y1) X C) P))) $;

--| The predicate "is a 3-dim lattice volume". (Contributed by NM, 1-Jul-2012.)
theorem islvol4 {y1: setvar} (A2 B2 C: class y1) (P K: class) (V: class y1) (X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv K clvol) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K A2) (wcel X B2)) (wb (wcel X V) (wrex y1 (wbr (cv y1) X C) P)) $;

--| Condition implying a 3-dim lattice volume. (Contributed by NM, 1-Jul-2012.)
theorem lvoli (B2 C D P K V X Y: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv K ccvr) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv K clvol) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K D) (wcel Y B2) (wcel X P)) (wbr X Y C)) (wcel Y V) $;

--| The predicate "is a 3-dim lattice volume". (Contributed by NM, 1-Jul-2012.)
theorem islvol3 {y1 p: setvar} (A2: class y1) (B2 P: class) (c_or: class y1 p) (K: class) (c_le: class y1) (V: class y1 p) (X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv K clvol) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel X B2)) (wb (wcel X V) (wrex y1 (wrex p (wa (wn (wbr (cv p) (cv y1) c_le)) (wceq X (co (cv y1) (cv p) c_or))) A2) P)) $;

--| Condition implying a 3-dim lattice volume. (Contributed by NM, 2-Aug-2012.)
theorem lvoli3 (A2 P Q c_or K c_le V X: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv K clvol) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X P) (wcel Q A2)) (wn (wbr Q X c_le))) (wcel (co X Q c_or) V) $;

--| A 3-dim lattice volume is a lattice element. (Contributed by NM, 1-Jul-2012.)
theorem lvolbase (B2 K V X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv K clvol) $ >
  $ wi (wcel X V) (wcel X B2) $;

--| The predicate "is a 3-dim lattice volume" in terms of atoms. (Contributed by NM, 1-Jul-2012.)
theorem islvol5 {s1 r q p: setvar} (A2 B2 c_or K c_le: class) (V: class s1 r q p) (X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv K clvol) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel X B2)) (wb (wcel X V) (wrex p (wrex q (wrex r (wrex s1 (wa (w3a (wne (cv p) (cv q)) (wn (wbr (cv r) (co (cv p) (cv q) c_or) c_le)) (wn (wbr (cv s1) (co (co (cv p) (cv q) c_or) (cv r) c_or) c_le))) (wceq X (co (co (co (cv p) (cv q) c_or) (cv r) c_or) (cv s1) c_or))) A2) A2) A2) A2)) $;

--| The predicate "is a 3-dim lattice volume" in terms of atoms. (Contributed by NM, 1-Jul-2012.)
theorem islvol2 {s1 r q p: setvar} (A2 B2 c_or K c_le: class) (V: class s1 r q p) (X: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv K clvol) $ >
  $ wi (wcel K chlt) (wb (wcel X V) (wa (wcel X B2) (wrex p (wrex q (wrex r (wrex s1 (wa (w3a (wne (cv p) (cv q)) (wn (wbr (cv r) (co (cv p) (cv q) c_or) c_le)) (wn (wbr (cv s1) (co (co (cv p) (cv q) c_or) (cv r) c_or) c_le))) (wceq X (co (co (co (cv p) (cv q) c_or) (cv r) c_or) (cv s1) c_or))) A2) A2) A2) A2))) $;

--| The join of 4 different atoms is a lattice volume. (Contributed by NM, 8-Jul-2012.)
theorem lvoli2 (A2 P Q R S c_or K c_le V: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv K clvol) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2)) (wa (wcel R A2) (wcel S A2)) (w3a (wne P Q) (wn (wbr R (co P Q c_or) c_le)) (wn (wbr S (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) c_le)))) (wcel (co (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) S c_or) V) $;

--| A lattice plane (or lattice line or atom) cannot majorize a lattice volume. (Contributed by NM, 8-Jul-2012.)
theorem lvolnle3at (A2 P Q R c_or K c_le V X: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv K clvol) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel X V)) (w3a (wcel P A2) (wcel Q A2) (wcel R A2))) (wn (wbr X (co (co P Q c_or) R c_or) c_le)) $;

--| An atom cannot majorize a lattice volume. (Contributed by NM, 14-Jul-2012.)
theorem lvolnleat (A2 P K c_le V X: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv K clvol) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X V) (wcel P A2)) (wn (wbr X P c_le)) $;

--| A lattice line cannot majorize a lattice volume. (Contributed by NM, 14-Jul-2012.)
theorem lvolnlelln (K c_le N V X Y: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv K clln) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv K clvol) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X V) (wcel Y N)) (wn (wbr X Y c_le)) $;

--| A lattice plane cannot majorize a lattice volume. (Contributed by NM, 14-Jul-2012.)
theorem lvolnlelpln (P K c_le V X Y: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq P (cfv K clpl) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv K clvol) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel X V) (wcel Y P)) (wn (wbr X Y c_le)) $;

--| The join of 3 atoms is not a lattice volume. (Contributed by NM, 17-Jul-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem _3atnelvolN (A2 P Q R c_or K V: class):
