--| Lemma for ~ 4atexlem7 . Show that when ` C =/= S ` , ` C ` satisfies the existence condition of the consequent. (Contributed by NM, 25-Nov-2012.)
theorem _4atexlemex2 {z: setvar} (ph: wff z) (A2 C P: class) (Q R: class z) (S: class) (T U H: class z) (c_or: class) (K: class z) (c_le: class) (c_an V: class z) (W: class):
  $ wb ph (w3a (w3a (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) (wa (wcel P A2) (wn (wbr P W c_le))) (wa (wcel Q A2) (wn (wbr Q W c_le)))) (w3a (wcel S A2) (w3a (wcel R A2) (wn (wbr R W c_le)) (wceq (co P R c_or) (co Q R c_or))) (wa (wcel T A2) (wceq (co U T c_or) (co V T c_or)))) (wa (wne P Q) (wn (wbr S (co P Q c_or) c_le)))) $ >
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq c_an (cfv K cmee) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv K catm) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq U (co (co P Q c_or) W c_an) $ >
  $ wceq V (co (co P S c_or) W c_an) $ >
  $ wceq C (co (co Q T c_or) (co P S c_or) c_an) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wne C S)) (wrex z (wa (wn (wbr (cv z) W c_le)) (wceq (co P (cv z) c_or) (co S (cv z) c_or))) A2) $;

--| Lemma for ~ 4atexlem7 . (Contributed by NM, 24-Nov-2012.)
