  $ wceq F (co (co S U c_or) (co Q (co (co P S c_or) W c_an) c_or) c_an) $ >
  $ wceq G (co (co P Q c_or) (co F (co (co Q S c_or) W c_an) c_or) c_an) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) (w3a (wa (wcel P A2) (wn (wbr P W c_le))) (wa (wcel Q A2) (wn (wbr Q W c_le))) (wa (wcel S A2) (wn (wbr S W c_le)))) (wa (wne P Q) (wn (wbr S (co P Q c_or) c_le)))) (wn (wbr G W c_le)) $;

--| Part of proof of Lemma E in [Crawley] p. 114, 2nd sentence of 4th paragraph. ` F ` , ` G ` represent f(s), f_s(q) respectively. We show ` -. ` f_s(q) ` =/= ` q. (Contributed by NM, 12-Oct-2012.)
