--| Part of proof of Lemma E in [Crawley] p. 114, 2nd sentence of 4th paragraph. ` F ` , ` G ` represent f(s), f_s(q) respectively. We show ` -. ` f_s(q) = p whenever p ` \/ ` q has three atoms under it (implied by the negated existential condition). (Contributed by NM, 10-Nov-2012.)
theorem cdleme18c {r: setvar} (A2 P Q: class) (S U F: class r) (G: class) (H: class r) (c_or: class) (K: class r) (c_le: class) (c_an: class r) (W: class):
