--| Part of proof of Lemma E in [Crawley] p. 113, 5th paragraph on p. 114, 1st line. ` D ` represents s_2. In their notation, we prove that if r ` <_ ` s ` \/ ` t, then s_2=(s ` \/ ` t) ` /\ ` w. (Contributed by NM, 13-Nov-2012.)
theorem cdleme19a (A2 D P Q R S T U F G H c_or K c_le c_an W Y: class):
