  $ wi (w3a (w3a (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H) (wcel T A2)) (w3a (wa (wcel P A2) (wn (wbr P W c_le))) (wa (wcel Q A2) (wn (wbr Q W c_le))) (wne P Q)) (w3a (wcel S A2) (w3a (wcel V A2) (wbr V W c_le) (wceq (co T V c_or) (co P Q c_or))) (wa (wa (wcel (cv y1) A2) (wn (wbr (cv y1) W c_le))) (wa (wcel (cv z) A2) (wn (wbr (cv z) W c_le)))))) (wbr N (co O V c_or) c_le) $;

--| Part of proof of Lemma E in [Crawley] p. 113, 3rd paragraph, 6th and 7th lines on p. 115. ` F ` , ` N ` represent f(t), f_t(s) respectively. If s ` <_ ` t ` \/ ` v, then f_t(s) ` <_ ` f(t) ` \/ ` v. (Contributed by NM, 6-Dec-2012.)
theorem cdleme22f (A2 P Q S T U F H c_or K c_le c_an N V W: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
