--| Part of proof of Lemma G in [Crawley] p. 117, 4th line. Whenever (in their terminology) p ` \/ ` q/0 (i.e. the sublattice from 0 to p ` \/ ` q) contains precisely three atoms and g is not the identity, g(p) = q. See also comments under ~ cdleme0nex . (Contributed by NM, 8-May-2013.)
theorem cdlemg17b {r: setvar} (A2 P Q: class) (R T: class r) (G: class) (H: class r) (c_or: class) (K: class r) (c_le: class) (c_an: class r) (W: class):
