--| Lemma K of [Crawley] p. 118. Final result, lines 11 and 12 on p. 120: given two translations f and k with the same trace, there exists a trace-preserving endomorphism tau whose value at f is k. We use ` F ` , ` N ` , and ` u ` to represent f, k, and tau. (Contributed by NM, 1-Aug-2013.)
theorem cdlemk {u: setvar} (R T E F: class) (H: class u) (K N W: class):
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq T (cfv W (cfv K cltrn)) $ >
  $ wceq R (cfv W (cfv K ctrl)) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv W (cfv K ctendo)) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) (wa (wcel F T) (wcel N T)) (wceq (cfv F R) (cfv N R))) (wrex u (wceq (cfv F (cv u)) N) E) $;

--| Generalization of Lemma K of [Crawley] p. 118, ~ cdlemk . TODO: can this be used to shorten uses of ~ cdlemk ? (Contributed by NM, 15-Oct-2013.)
theorem tendoex {u: setvar} (R T E F: class) (H: class u) (K: class) (c_le: class u) (N W: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq T (cfv W (cfv K cltrn)) $ >
  $ wceq R (cfv W (cfv K ctrl)) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv W (cfv K ctendo)) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) (wa (wcel F T) (wcel N T)) (wbr (cfv N R) (cfv F R) c_le)) (wrex u (wceq (cfv F (cv u)) N) E) $;

--| Part of proof of Lemma L of [Crawley] p. 120. TODO: fix comment. (Contributed by NM, 1-Aug-2013.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem cdleml1N (B2 R T U: class) (f2: setvar) (E H K V W: class):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq T (cfv W (cfv K cltrn)) $ >
  $ wceq R (cfv W (cfv K ctrl)) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv W (cfv K ctendo)) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) (w3a (wcel U E) (wcel V E) (wcel (cv f2) T)) (w3a (wne (cv f2) (cres cid B2)) (wne (cfv (cv f2) U) (cres cid B2)) (wne (cfv (cv f2) V) (cres cid B2)))) (wceq (cfv (cfv (cv f2) U) R) (cfv (cfv (cv f2) V) R)) $;

