theorem cdleml9 {z f2 g2 h s1 b: setvar} (B2: class h s1) (Q R: class f2 h s1) (T: class h s1) (U E: class z f2 g2 h s1 b) (H c_or K c_an W: class f2 h s1) (X: class z f2 g2 h s1 b) (Y: class f2 g2 h s1 b) (c_0: class z f2 g2 h s1 b) (Z: class z f2 h s1 b):
  $ wceq B2 (cfv K cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_or (cfv K cjn) $ >
  $ wceq c_an (cfv K cmee) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq T (cfv W (cfv K cltrn)) $ >
  $ wceq R (cfv W (cfv K ctrl)) $ >
  $ wceq Q (cfv W (cfv K coc)) $ >
  $ wceq Z (co (co Q (cfv (cv b) R) c_or) (co (cfv Q (cv h)) (cfv (ccom (cv b) (ccnv (cfv (cv h) (cv s1)))) R) c_or) c_an) $ >
  $ wceq Y (co (co Q (cfv (cv g2) R) c_or) (co Z (cfv (ccom (cv g2) (ccnv (cv b))) R) c_or) c_an) $ >
  $ wceq X (crio z (wral b (wi (w3a (wne (cv b) (cres cid B2)) (wne (cfv (cv b) R) (cfv (cfv (cv h) (cv s1)) R)) (wne (cfv (cv b) R) (cfv (cv g2) R))) (wceq (cfv Q (cv z)) Y)) T) T) $ >
  $ wceq U (cmpt g2 T (cif (wceq (cfv (cv h) (cv s1)) (cv h)) (cv g2) X)) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv W (cfv K ctendo)) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cmpt f2 T (cres cid B2)) $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) (wa (wcel (cv h) T) (wne (cv h) (cres cid B2))) (wa (wcel (cv s1) E) (wne (cv s1) c_0))) (wne U c_0) $;

--| Two expressions for the 1-dimensional subspaces of partial vector space A. Remark in [Crawley] p. 120 line 21, but using a non-identity translation (nonzero vector) ` F ` whose trace is ` P ` rather than ` P ` itself; ` F ` exists by ~ cdlemf . ` E ` is the division ring base by ~ erngdv , and ` s `` F ` is the scalar product by ~ dvavsca . ` F ` must be a non-identity translation for the expression to be a 1-dimensional subspace, although the theorem doesn't require it. (Contributed by NM, 14-Oct-2013.)
theorem dva1dim {g2 s1: setvar} (R: class g2) (T: class) (E: class g2) (F H K: class) (c_le: class g2) (W: class):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq T (cfv W (cfv K cltrn)) $ >
  $ wceq R (cfv W (cfv K ctrl)) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv W (cfv K ctendo)) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) (wcel F T)) (wceq (cab g2 (wrex s1 (wceq (cv g2) (cfv F (cv s1))) E)) (crab g2 (wbr (cfv (cv g2) R) (cfv F R) c_le) T)) $;

--| Two expressions for the 1-dimensional subspaces of vector space ` H ` , in the isomorphism B case where the second vector component is zero. (Contributed by NM, 23-Feb-2014.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem dvhb1dimN {g2 h s1: setvar} (B2: class g2 h s1) (R: class g2 h) (T: class) (E: class g2 h) (F H K: class h) (c_le: class g2 h) (W: class h) (c_0: class g2 h):
  $ wceq c_le (cfv K cple) $ >
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq T (cfv W (cfv K cltrn)) $ >
  $ wceq R (cfv W (cfv K ctrl)) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv W (cfv K ctendo)) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cmpt h T (cres cid B2)) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) (wcel F T)) (wceq (crab g2 (wrex s1 (wceq (cv g2) (cop (cfv F (cv s1)) c_0)) E) (cxp T E)) (crab g2 (wa (wbr (cfv (cfv (cv g2) c1st) R) (cfv F R) c_le) (wceq (cfv (cv g2) c2nd) c_0)) (cxp T E))) $;

--| Value of the endomorphism division ring unity. (Contributed by NM, 12-Oct-2013.)
theorem erng1lem (D T E H K W: class):
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq T (cfv W (cfv K cltrn)) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv W (cfv K ctendo)) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv W (cfv K cedring)) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) (wcel D crg) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) (wceq (cfv D cur) (cres cid T)) $;

