--| Value of the map defined by ~ df-mapd at an atom. (Contributed by NM, 10-Feb-2015.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem mapd1dim2lem1N {v f2: setvar} (ph: wff) (A2: class v f2) (Q: class) (U: class f2) (F: class) (H: class v f2) (K: class v) (L: class f2) (M: class v f2) (O: class f2) (W: class v):
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv W (cfv K cdvh)) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv U clsa) $ >
  $ wceq F (cfv U clfn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv U clk) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv W (cfv K coch)) $ >
  $ wceq M (cfv W (cfv K cmpd)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Q A2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv Q M) (crab f2 (wrex v (wceq (cfv (csn (cv v)) O) (cfv (cv f2) L)) Q) F)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ mapdrval . TODO: very long antecedents are dragged through proof in some places - see if it shortens proof to remove unused conjuncts. (Contributed by NM, 2-Feb-2015.)
theorem mapdrvallem2 {f2 g2 h: setvar} (ph: wff g2) (A2: class f2 g2 h) (C: class g2) (D: class f2 g2 h) (Q R: class g2) (S T: class f2 g2 h) (U: class f2) (F: class h) (H: class f2 g2 h) (K: class g2 h) (L: class f2) (M: class f2 g2 h) (N: class f2 g2) (O: class f2) (V: class f2 g2) (W: class g2 h) (Y c_0: class f2 g2):
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv W (cfv K coch)) $ >
  $ wceq M (cfv W (cfv K cmpd)) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv W (cfv K cdvh)) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv U clss) $ >
  $ wceq F (cfv U clfn) $ >
  $ wceq L (cfv U clk) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv U cld) $ >
  $ wceq T (cfv D clss) $ >
  $ wceq C (crab g2 (wceq (cfv (cfv (cfv (cv g2) L) O) O) (cfv (cv g2) L)) F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel R T) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss R C) $ >
  $ wceq Q (ciun h R (cfv (cfv (cv h) L) O)) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv U cbs) $ >
  $ wceq A2 (cfv U clsa) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv U clspn) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv U c0g) $ >
  $ wceq Y (cfv D c0g) $ >
  $ wi ph (wss (crab f2 (wss (cfv (cfv (cv f2) L) O) Q) C) R) $;

