--| The inner product of the reference vector ` E ` with itself is nonzero. This shows the inner product condition in the proof of Theorem 3.6 of [Holland95] p. 14 line 32, ` [ ` e , e ` ] =/= 0 ` is satisfied. TODO: remove redundant hypothesis hdmapevec.j. (Contributed by NM, 1-Jun-2015.)
theorem hdmapevec2 (ph: wff) (R S U c_1 E H J K W: class):
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq E (cop (cres cid (cfv K cbs)) (cres cid (cfv W (cfv K cltrn)))) $ >
  $ wceq J (cfv W (cfv K chvm)) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv W (cfv K chdma)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv W (cfv K cdvh)) $ >
  $ wceq R (cfv U csca) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv R cur) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv E (cfv E S)) c_1) $;

