--| Nonzero vector closure of map from vectors to functionals with closed kernels. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-2015.)
theorem hdmapnzcl (ph: wff) (C D Q S T U H K V W c_0: class):
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv W (cfv K cdvh)) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv U cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv U c0g) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv W (cfv K clcd)) $ >
  $ wceq Q (cfv C c0g) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv C cbs) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv W (cfv K chdma)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel T (cdif V (csn c_0))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cfv T S) (cdif D (csn Q))) $;

--| Part of proof of part 12 in [Baer] p. 49 line 4. The sigma map of a negative is the negative of the sigma map. (Contributed by NM, 24-May-2015.)
theorem hdmapneg (ph: wff) (C S T U H I K M V W: class):
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv W (cfv K cdvh)) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv U cbs) $ >
  $ wceq M (cfv U cminusg) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv W (cfv K clcd)) $ >
  $ wceq I (cfv C cminusg) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv W (cfv K chdma)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel T V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv (cfv T M) S) (cfv (cfv T S) I)) $;

--| Part of proof of part 12 in [Baer] p. 49 line 5, (a-b)S = aS-bS in their notation (S = sigma). (Contributed by NM, 26-May-2015.)
theorem hdmapsub (ph: wff) (C S U H K c_mi N V W X Y: class):
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv W (cfv K cdvh)) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv U cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_mi (cfv U csg) $ >
  $ wceq C (cfv W (cfv K clcd)) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv C csg) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv W (cfv K chdma)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv (co X Y c_mi) S) (co (cfv X S) (cfv Y S) N)) $;

--| Part of proof of part 12 in [Baer] p. 49 line 4, aS=bS iff a=b in their notation (S = sigma). The sigma map is one-to-one. (Contributed by NM, 26-May-2015.)
theorem hdmap11 (ph: wff) (S U H K V W X Y: class):
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv W (cfv K cdvh)) $ >
