  $ wceq S (cfv W (cfv K chdma)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (cfv X S) (cfv Y S)) (wceq X Y)) $;

--| Part of proof of part 12 in [Baer] p. 49 line 10, Gu' ` =/= ` Gs. Our ` ( N `` { v } ) ` is Baer's T. (Contributed by NM, 26-May-2015.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem hdmaprnlem1N {v u s1: setvar} (ph: wff v u s1) (C D Q S U H K L M N V W: class v u s1):
