--| Kernel of the vector to dual map. Line 16 in [Holland95] p. 14. TODO: eliminate ` F ` hypothesis. (Contributed by NM, 9-Jun-2015.)
theorem hdmaplkr (ph: wff) (S U F H K O V W X Y: class):
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv W (cfv K coch)) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv W (cfv K cdvh)) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv U cbs) $ >
  $ wceq F (cfv U clfn) $ >
  $ wceq Y (cfv U clk) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv W (cfv K chdma)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv (cfv X S) Y) (cfv (csn X) O)) $;

--| Membership in the kernel (as shown by ~ hdmaplkr ) of the vector to dual map. Line 17 in [Holland95] p. 14. (Contributed by NM, 16-Jun-2015.)
theorem hdmapellkr (ph: wff) (R S U H K O V W X Y c_0: class):
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
