--| Construct a proportional vector ` Y ` whose inner product with the original ` X ` equals one. (Contributed by NM, 13-Jun-2015.)
theorem hdmapip1 (ph: wff) (R S c_x U c_1 H K N V W X Y c_0: class):
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv W (cfv K cdvh)) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv U cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv U cvsca) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv U c0g) $ >
  $ wceq R (cfv U csca) $ >
  $ wceq c_1 (cfv R cur) $ >
  $ wceq N (cfv R cinvr) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv W (cfv K chdma)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X (cdif V (csn c_0))) $ >
  $ wceq Y (co (cfv (cfv X (cfv X S)) N) X c_x) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv Y (cfv X S)) c_1) $;

--| Commutation property of Baer's sigma map (Holland's A map). Line 20 of [Holland95] p. 14. Also part of Lemma 1 of [Baer] p. 110 line 7. (Contributed by NM, 9-Jun-2015.)
theorem hdmapip0com (ph: wff) (R S U H K V W X Y c_0: class):
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv W (cfv K cdvh)) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv U cbs) $ >
  $ wceq R (cfv U csca) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv R c0g) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv W (cfv K chdma)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel X V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Y V) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (cfv Y (cfv X S)) c_0) (wceq (cfv X (cfv Y S)) c_0)) $;

--| Line 27 in [Baer] p. 110. We use ` C ` for Baer's u. Our unit vector ` E ` has the required properties for his w by ~ hdmapevec2 . Our ` ( ( S `` E ) `` C ) ` means the inner product ` <. C , E >. ` i.e. his f(u,w) (note argument reversal). (Contributed by NM, 11-Jun-2015.)
theorem hdmapinvlem1 (ph: wff) (B2 C R S c_x U E H K O V W c_0: class):
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq E (cop (cres cid (cfv K cbs)) (cres cid (cfv W (cfv K cltrn)))) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv W (cfv K coch)) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv W (cfv K cdvh)) $ >
  $ wceq V (cfv U cbs) $ >
  $ wceq R (cfv U csca) $ >
  $ wceq B2 (cfv R cbs) $ >
  $ wceq c_x (cfv R cmulr) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cfv R c0g) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv W (cfv K chdma)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wcel K chlt) (wcel W H)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C (cfv (csn E) O)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cfv C (cfv E S)) c_0) $;

--| Line 28 in [Baer] p. 110, 0 = f(w,u). (Contributed by NM, 11-Jun-2015.)
theorem hdmapinvlem2 (ph: wff) (B2 C R S c_x U E H K O V W c_0: class):
  $ wceq H (cfv K clh) $ >
  $ wceq E (cop (cres cid (cfv K cbs)) (cres cid (cfv W (cfv K cltrn)))) $ >
  $ wceq O (cfv W (cfv K coch)) $ >
  $ wceq U (cfv W (cfv K cdvh)) $ >
