  $ wi ph (wcel S (cpw B2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wcel S (cfv X N)) (wn (wcel (cdif B2 S) (cfv X M)))) $;

--| The complement of a subset being an element of a neighborhood at a point is equivalent to that subset not being a element of the convergent at that point. (Contributed by RP, 12-Jun-2021.)
theorem neicvgel2 {i j k m n o p l: setvar} (ph: wff m) (B2 D: class) (P: class i j k m n o p l) (S: class i j k n p l) (F: class m) (G: class) (H: class i j k m n o p l) (M: class m) (N: class) (O: class i j k m n o p l) (X: class i j k n o p):
  $ wceq O (cmpo i j cvv cvv (cmpt k (co (cpw (cv j)) (cv i) cmap) (cmpt l (cv j) (crab m (wcel (cv l) (cfv (cv m) (cv k))) (cv i))))) $ >
  $ wceq P (cmpt n cvv (cmpt p (co (cpw (cv n)) (cpw (cv n)) cmap) (cmpt o (cpw (cv n)) (cdif (cv n) (cfv (cdif (cv n) (cv o)) (cv p)))))) $ >
  $ wceq D (cfv B2 P) $ >
  $ wceq F (co (cpw B2) B2 O) $ >
