  $ wvd1 ch th $ >
  $ wvd1 ta et $ >
  $ wi (w3a ps th et) ze $ >
  $ wvd1 (wvhc3 ph ch ta) ze $;

--| A virtual deduction elimination rule. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 29-Feb-2012.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem e233 (ph ps ch th ta et ze: wff):
  $ wvd2 ph ps ch $ >
  $ wvd3 ph ps th ta $ >
  $ wvd3 ph ps th et $ >
  $ wi ch (wi ta (wi et ze)) $ >
  $ wvd3 ph ps th ze $;

--| A virtual deduction elimination rule. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 17-Apr-2012.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem e323 (ph ps ch th ta et ze: wff):
  $ wvd3 ph ps ch th $ >
  $ wvd2 ph ps ta $ >
  $ wvd3 ph ps ch et $ >
  $ wi th (wi ta (wi et ze)) $ >
  $ wvd3 ph ps ch ze $;

--| A virtual deduction elimination rule. The non-virtual deduction form of ~ e000 is the virtual deduction form. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 14-Jun-2011.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem e000 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ ps $ >
  $ ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ th $;

--| Elimination rule identical to ~ mp2 . The non-virtual deduction form is the virtual deduction form, which is ~ mp2 . (Contributed by Alan Sare, 14-Jun-2011.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem e00 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ ch $;

--| Elimination rule identical to ~ mp2an . The non-virtual deduction form is the virtual deduction form, which is ~ mp2an . (Contributed by Alan Sare, 15-Jun-2011.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem e00an (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ ch $;

--| An elimination deduction. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 4-Feb-2017.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem eel00cT (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi wtru ch $;

--| An elimination deduction. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 4-Feb-2017.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem eelTT (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi wtru ph $ >
  $ wi wtru ps $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ ch $;

--| Elimination rule identical to ~ ax-mp . The non-virtual deduction form is the virtual deduction form, which is ~ ax-mp . (Contributed by Alan Sare, 14-Jun-2011.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem e0a (ph ps: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ ps $;

--| An elimination deduction. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 5-Feb-2017.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem eelT (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi wtru ph $ >
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ ps $;

--| An elimination deduction. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 4-Feb-2017.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem eel0cT (ph ps: wff):
