--| The intersection points of a line ` L ` and a circle around the origin. (Contributed by AV, 25-Feb-2023.)
theorem itsclc0 {p: setvar} (A2 B2 C: class) (D: class p) (P: class) (Q: class p) (R: class) (S: class p) (E I: class) (L: class p) (X c_0: class):
  $ wceq I (co cc0 c2 cfzo) $ >
  $ wceq E (cfv I crrx) $ >
  $ wceq P (co cr I cmap) $ >
  $ wceq S (cfv E csph) $ >
  $ wceq c_0 (cxp I (csn cc0)) $ >
